    "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"optomind.fullbody.payload.v1\",\n  \"language\": \"zh\",\n  \"research_question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\n  \"review_argument\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\n  \"user_request\": \"\",\n  \"target_reader\": \"\",\n  \"review_scope\": {\n    \"statement\": \"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"\n  },\n  \"approved_plan\": {\n    \"canonical_book_reference\": \"approved_plan\",\n    \"sha256\": \"b08bdc1f745404a9b893a88495e44c04fa96945bb03a0460bb47281e85dbe7fb\",\n    \"normalized_outline_reference\": \"shared_fullbody_context\"\n  },\n  \"missing_original_context_fields\": [\n    \"user_request\",\n    \"target_reader\"\n  ],\n  \"editable_task_ids\": [\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n    \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n  ],\n  \"chapters\": [\n    {\n      \"schema_version\": \"optomind.writer_candidates.payload.v1\",\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch6\",\n      \"language\": \"zh\",\n      \"chapter_frame\": {\n        \"chapter_title\": \"微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\",\n        \"chapter_purpose\": \"明确微生物组作为 ICI 毒性预测标志物的临床潜力与局限，理解疗效与毒性耦合/解耦的生物学基础，并掌握基于供体特征与 ICI 方案的情境化安全性管理策略。特别需注意非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的微生物组证据仍受限于样本量，当前结论主要基于结肠炎数据。\",\n        \"chapter_scope\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因癌种特异性、毒性表型（结肠炎 vs 心肌炎）及干预情境（供体特征、ICI 骨架方案）而异。观察性关联在结肠炎中证据最强，心肌炎等罕见 irAEs 仍受限于样本量；微生物干预（如 FMT）的获益与风险高度依赖于供体菌群组成与联合用药方案的交互作用。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用。\",\n        \"chapter_thesis\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因癌种特异性、毒性表型（结肠炎 vs 心肌炎）及干预情境（供体特征、ICI 骨架方案）而异。观察性关联在结肠炎中证据最强，心肌炎等罕见 irAEs 仍受限于样本量；微生物干预（如 FMT）的获益与风险高度依赖于供体菌群组成与联合用药方案的交互作用。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用。\",\n        \"chapter_argument\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因癌种特异性、毒性表型（结肠炎 vs 心肌炎）及干预情境（供体特征、ICI 骨架方案）而异。观察性关联在结肠炎中证据最强，心肌炎等罕见 irAEs 仍受限于样本量；微生物干预（如 FMT）的获益与风险高度依赖于供体菌群组成与联合用药方案的交互作用。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用。\",\n        \"reader_objective\": \"明确微生物组作为 ICI 毒性预测标志物的临床潜力与局限，理解疗效与毒性耦合/解耦的生物学基础，并掌握基于供体特征与 ICI 方案的情境化安全性管理策略。特别需注意非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的微生物组证据仍受限于样本量，当前结论主要基于结肠炎数据。\",\n        \"research_question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\",\n        \"review_argument\": \"肠道微生物组通过分类学特征、代谢产物及免疫通路调节实体瘤患者对 ICI 的临床疗效，但证据强度因肿瘤类型、研究设计及干预策略而异。观察性关联证据在黑色素瘤中最强，NSCLC 和 RCC 次之，但关联不等于因果。机制证据主要来自动物模型，人类验证有限，特别是肿瘤微环境内代谢物浓度数据缺失（如肌苷仅有血浆数据）。干预策略在初治人群中显示希望（FMT-LUMINate ORR 75-80%），但在难治人群中效果有限（MITRIC ORR 0%），且安全性受 ICI 方案调节（Prevotella 相关心肌炎仅在双 ICI 背景下出现）。目前缺乏 Phase III RCT 证据支持微生物干预的常规临床应用，未来研究需解决标准化、因果推断及人群分层问题。\",\n        \"shared_scope\": {\n          \"statement\": \"本综述聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、结直肠癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4 抑制剂）治疗期间，肠道微生物组对治疗疗效（ORR、PFS、OS）及毒性（irAEs）的调节作用。涵盖观察性关联证据（区分回顾性与前瞻性队列）、因果机制解析（免疫细胞、分子通路、代谢物）、外部干扰因素（抗生素、PPI、饮食）及微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）的临床试验数据。明确排除血液系统恶性肿瘤及非免疫治疗背景下的微生物组研究（除非用于机制对比）。严格区分肠道微生物组与肿瘤内微生物组的作用边界。证据等级标注明确：观察性关联不推断因果，干预试验区分 I/II 期与 III 期，代谢物数据区分血浆与肿瘤组织浓度。\"\n        },\n        \"review_argument_status\": \"calibrated\",\n        \"review_argument_source\": \"whole_plan_improvement\"\n      },\n      \"editable_task_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n      ],\n      \"units\": [\n        {\n          \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U1\",\n          \"focus\": \"特定菌属与 irAEs 的癌种特异性关联及预测模型困境\",\n          \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P01\",\n              \"point\": \"结肠炎型 irAEs 的微生物指纹与整体多样性下降\",\n              \"development\": \"比较结肠炎型与非结肠炎型 irAE 患者的粪便宏基因组/16S 特征，指出主要产丁酸菌丰度降低、拟杆菌门/双歧杆菌减少及肠球菌富集是结肠炎的核心表型。P0017 通过抗生素预处理小鼠 FMT 实验验证其因果致病潜力：接受结肠炎型患者菌群移植的小鼠出现致命性严重结肠炎（3/9 死亡），而非结肠炎型菌群移植小鼠全部存活。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供结肠炎型患者菌群移植小鼠出现致命性严重结肠炎的因果证据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供肺癌及多癌种队列中结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物指纹差异，并通过人源化小鼠 FMT 实验确立菌群致结肠炎的因果性\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U1_P01\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P01\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U1\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 1,\n                  \"point\": \"结肠炎型 irAEs 的微生物指纹与整体多样性下降\",\n                  \"development\": \"比较结肠炎型与非结肠炎型 irAE 患者的粪便宏基因组/16S 特征，指出主要产丁酸菌丰度降低、拟杆菌门/双歧杆菌减少及肠球菌富集是结肠炎的核心表型。P0017 通过抗生素预处理小鼠 FMT 实验验证其因果致病潜力：接受结肠炎型患者菌群移植的小鼠出现致命性严重结肠炎（3/9 死亡），而非结肠炎型菌群移植小鼠全部存活。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0017\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P02\",\n              \"point\": \"胃肠道癌症的保护性菌群与器官特异性毒性差异\",\n              \"development\": \"聚焦食管癌、胃癌、结直肠癌队列（P0011，n=95），指出 Ruminococcus callidus 和 Bacteroides xylanisolvens 在无重症 irAEs 患者中显著富集，且尿素循环/精氨酸生物合成通路与低毒性相关。同时强调皮肤、血液、内分泌及肝脏毒性各自呈现独立的微生物通路特征，反驳单一通用标志物假设。但需注意该研究样本量有限且缺乏外部验证。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供胃肠道癌症队列中 Ruminococcus callidus 和 Bacteroides xylanisolvens 富集与低毒性相关的实证数据\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U1_P02\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P02\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U1\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 2,\n                  \"point\": \"胃肠道癌症的保护性菌群与器官特异性毒性差异\",\n                  \"development\": \"聚焦食管癌、胃癌、结直肠癌队列（P0011，n=95），指出 Ruminococcus callidus 和 Bacteroides xylanisolvens 在无重症 irAEs 患者中显著富集，且尿素循环/精氨酸生物合成通路与低毒性相关。同时强调皮肤、血液、内分泌及肝脏毒性各自呈现独立的微生物通路特征，反驳单一通用标志物假设。但需注意该研究样本量有限且缺乏外部验证。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0011\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P03\",\n              \"point\": \"预测模型的构建困境与非结肠炎 irAEs 证据不足\",\n              \"development\": \"评估基于机器学习（如 RF14 分类器，P0308）的 irAEs 预测模型性能，指出尽管 AUC 可达 0.88，但在多重检验校正后部分特征显著性不足。P0312 综述指出，即使在大样本队列中，非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的样本量仍不足以支持独立的微生物组分析，当前证据主要集中于结肠炎。不同研究间测序平台、CTCAE 分级版本及队列异质性导致模型泛化能力受限。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0308\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 RF14 分类器性能数据及多重检验校正后特征显著性不足的证据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0312\",\n                  \"role\": \"背景\",\n                  \"use\": \"综述指出非结肠炎 irAEs 样本量不足以支持独立微生物组分析的限制\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n                  \"role\": \"局限\",\n                  \"use\": \"揭示 F. prausnitzii 等标志物在多重检验下的不一致性及大样本队列中非结肠炎亚组样本量极小（n=2）的现状\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0605\",\n                  \"role\": \"局限\",\n                  \"use\": \"量化心肌炎/脑膜炎等亚组样本量极小，直接支撑预测模型构建困境及非结肠炎毒性证据不足的论述\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U1_P03\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U1_P03\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U1\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 3,\n                  \"point\": \"预测模型的构建困境与非结肠炎 irAEs 证据不足\",\n                  \"development\": \"评估基于机器学习（如 RF14 分类器，P0308）的 irAEs 预测模型性能，指出尽管 AUC 可达 0.88，但在多重检验校正后部分特征显著性不足。P0312 综述指出，即使在大样本队列中，非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的样本量仍不足以支持独立的微生物组分析，当前证据主要集中于结肠炎。不同研究间测序平台、CTCAE 分级版本及队列异质性导致模型泛化能力受限。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0308\",\n                    \"P0312\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"table_tasks\": [],\n          \"owner_unit_context\": {\n            \"evidence_conditions\": \"\",\n            \"synthesis\": \"微生物组对 irAEs 的预测价值呈现显著的癌种与器官特异性，结肠炎表型的微生物驱动证据最为坚实（包括动物因果验证），而其他毒性类型（心肌炎、神经毒性等）的独立预测标志物仍需大样本前瞻性队列验证。当前非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组证据受限于样本量，不能外推为领域层面的确定性结论。\",\n            \"transition\": \"在确认特定菌群与毒性关联的基础上，需进一步解析为何某些微生物特征既能促进抗肿瘤响应，又会引发过度免疫激活，从而引出疗效与毒性的耦合与解耦机制。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供肺癌及多癌种队列中结肠炎与非结肠炎irAEs的微生物指纹差异，并通过人源化小鼠FMT实验确立菌群致结肠炎的因果性，直接支撑癌种特异性关联与样本量局限性的论述。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0600\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"基于大样本前瞻性队列揭示Ruminococcaceae科动态下降与严重irAEs的关联，并剖析F. prausnitzii等标志物在多重检验下的不一致性，用于论证预测模型构建的方法学困境。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0049\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供大样本前瞻性纵向队列数据，证实Ruminococcaceae动态耗竭与严重irAEs关联，并量化心肌炎/脑膜炎等亚组样本量极小（n=2），直接支撑预测模型构建困境及非结肠炎毒性证据不足的论述。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0605\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"unit_notes\": \"将 P0600 从 case_level_uses 整合进 P01，强化因果证据；将 P0049/P0605 整合进 P03，明确样本量局限。\",\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0017\",\n            \"P0600\",\n            \"P0011\",\n            \"P0308\",\n            \"P0312\",\n            \"P0049\",\n            \"P0605\"\n          ],\n          \"editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n              \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n              \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          },\n          \"local_editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n            \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n            \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"fullbody_task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U2\",\n          \"focus\": \"疗效与毒性的耦合及解耦关系与免疫稳态中介\",\n          \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P01\",\n              \"point\": \"共享免疫激活通路的\\\"双刃剑\\\"效应\",\n              \"development\": \"指出高丰度 Akkermansia muciniphila 在 NSCLC 队列中与延长 OS 正相关，但同时增加 irAEs 风险（P0260），提示微生物介导的 CD8+ T 细胞活化与 IFN-γ分泌是疗效提升与自身免疫毒性共有的上游驱动力。这种关联是观察性的，不能推断因果。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 Akkermansia muciniphila 与 OS 正相关但增加 irAEs 风险的观察性关联证据\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U2_P01\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P01\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U2\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 1,\n                  \"point\": \"共享免疫激活通路的\\\"双刃剑\\\"效应\",\n                  \"development\": \"指出高丰度 Akkermansia muciniphila 在 NSCLC 队列中与延长 OS 正相关，但同时增加 irAEs 风险（P0260），提示微生物介导的 CD8+ T 细胞活化与 IFN-γ分泌是疗效提升与自身免疫毒性共有的上游驱动力。这种关联是观察性的，不能推断因果。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0260\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P02\",\n              \"point\": \"解耦路径：特定菌属与无毒性响应的共存\",\n              \"development\": \"对比黑色素瘤纵向队列数据（P0239），发现 Eubacterium siraeum 高丰度与无 irAEs 的客观缓解状态显著相关，且短链脂肪酸产生菌（如 Coprococcus comes, Blautia glucerasea）在未发生 irAEs 的患者中同样富集（P0428），挑战\\\"毒性必然预示疗效\\\"的直觉假设。但需注意这些发现主要来自回顾性分析。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0239\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 Eubacterium siraeum 高丰度与无 irAEs 的客观缓解状态显著相关的纵向队列数据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0428\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"证实 SCFA 产生菌在无 irAEs 响应者中显著富集，为解耦疗效与毒性提供直接的表型证据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"识别 Blautia luti 等 Lachnospiraceae 成员与“有效且无 irAE\\\"状态的独立关联，补充代谢功能菌群线索\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U2_P02\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P02\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U2\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 2,\n                  \"point\": \"解耦路径：特定菌属与无毒性响应的共存\",\n                  \"development\": \"对比黑色素瘤纵向队列数据（P0239），发现 Eubacterium siraeum 高丰度与无 irAEs 的客观缓解状态显著相关，且短链脂肪酸产生菌（如 Coprococcus comes, Blautia glucerasea）在未发生 irAEs 的患者中同样富集（P0428），挑战\\\"毒性必然预示疗效\\\"的直觉假设。但需注意这些发现主要来自回顾性分析。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0239\",\n                    \"P0428\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P03\",\n              \"point\": \"基线免疫稳态与纵向动态变化的中介作用\",\n              \"development\": \"整合黑色素瘤配对粪便与外周血 PBMC 纵向数据（P0098，n=126），显示基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）高丰度与治疗后 Tregs 频率显著下降相关，且 Tregs 耗竭程度直接预测严重 irAEs 的发生；相反，瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）主导的基线状态则与更好的治疗响应及较低的毒性风险同步出现。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供基线拟杆菌属高丰度与 Tregs 频率下降及严重 irAEs 相关的纵向免疫细胞动态数据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"揭示基线病原共生菌富集与治疗早期产丁酸菌耗竭的时序特征，为免疫稳态失衡提供临床动态证据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0605\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"通过纵向宏基因组数据证实 Ruminococcaceae 动态耗竭与严重 irAEs 关联，补充免疫稳态失衡的微生物组证据\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U2_P03\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U2_P03\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U2\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 3,\n                  \"point\": \"基线免疫稳态与纵向动态变化的中介作用\",\n                  \"development\": \"整合黑色素瘤配对粪便与外周血 PBMC 纵向数据（P0098，n=126），显示基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）高丰度与治疗后 Tregs 频率显著下降相关，且 Tregs 耗竭程度直接预测严重 irAEs 的发生；相反，瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）主导的基线状态则与更好的治疗响应及较低的毒性风险同步出现。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0098\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"table_tasks\": [],\n          \"owner_unit_context\": {\n            \"evidence_conditions\": \"\",\n            \"synthesis\": \"疗效与毒性的耦合源于微生物驱动的广谱免疫激活，而解耦则依赖于特定共生菌维持的 Treg 稳态与屏障完整性；基线免疫细胞亚群比例可作为区分\\\"有益激活\\\"与\\\"病理性炎症\\\"的关键中介指标。但解耦证据主要来自回顾性分析，尚未通过干预试验证实。\",\n            \"transition\": \"当微生物干预被用于逆转耐药或增强疗效时，其安全性表现并非均一，而是强烈依赖于供体来源特征与联合使用的 ICI 药物骨架，这构成了本章第三部分的实证核心。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"通过对比晚期黑色素瘤响应亚组基线特征，证实SCFA产生菌（如Coprococcus comes, Blautia glucerasea）在无irAEs响应者中显著富集，为解耦疗效与毒性提供直接的表型证据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"bb6b1be372fbcd8282307d93b91745ca4c844e92\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0428\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"前瞻性纵向数据识别Blautia luti等Lachnospiraceae成员与“有效且无irAE”状态的独立关联，补充了特定代谢功能菌群实现疗效-毒性解耦的分子线索。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0314\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"通过纵向宏基因组数据揭示基线病原共生菌富集与治疗早期产丁酸菌耗竭的时序特征，为微生物组介导的免疫稳态失衡及疗效-毒性耦合关系提供具体的临床动态证据。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0605\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"unit_notes\": \"\",\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0260\",\n            \"P0239\",\n            \"P0428\",\n            \"P0314\",\n            \"P0098\",\n            \"P0049\",\n            \"P0605\"\n          ],\n          \"editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n              \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n              \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          },\n          \"local_editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n            \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n            \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"fullbody_task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U3\",\n          \"focus\": \"微生物干预的安全性与供体特征的情境依赖性\",\n          \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P01\",\n              \"point\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的疗效分化与毒性起病时间提前\",\n              \"development\": \"报告 NSCLC 队列（抗 PD-1 单药，n=20）ORR 达 80% 且无≥3 级 AEs；而黑色素瘤队列（抗 PD-1+ 抗 CTLA-4 双免，n=20）ORR 为 75%，但 65% 患者经历≥3 级 AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占 20%，心肌炎发生率高达 15%（文献报道通常<1%），且严重毒性中位起病时间提前至 40 天（P0583）。需明确这是 Phase II 单臂试验，非 Phase III RCT。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"报告 FMT-LUMINate 试验中双免背景下 ORR 75% 但 65% 患者经历≥3 级 AEs 及心肌炎发生率高达 15% 的数据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 MITRIC 试验在难治人群中 ORR 0% 的结果，对比显示干预效果在初治与难治人群中的异质性\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0212\",\n                  \"role\": \"背景\",\n                  \"use\": \"荟萃分析量化 FMT 联合 ICI 的总体 ORR 及 3-4 级 AE 发生率，为安全性边界提供定量基准\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U3_P01\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P01\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U3\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 1,\n                  \"point\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的疗效分化与毒性起病时间提前\",\n                  \"development\": \"报告 NSCLC 队列（抗 PD-1 单药，n=20）ORR 达 80% 且无≥3 级 AEs；而黑色素瘤队列（抗 PD-1+ 抗 CTLA-4 双免，n=20）ORR 为 75%，但 65% 患者经历≥3 级 AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占 20%，心肌炎发生率高达 15%（文献报道通常<1%），且严重毒性中位起病时间提前至 40 天（P0583）。需明确这是 Phase II 单臂试验，非 Phase III RCT。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0583\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P02\",\n              \"point\": \"供体微生物组聚类与特定毒性事件的因果关联\",\n              \"development\": \"基于 Bray-Curtis 指数无监督聚类将健康供体分为 Cluster A 与 Cluster B（含供体 5、11）。Cluster B 以 Segatella copri、Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119 等高丰度为特征。接受 Cluster B 供体 FMT 的黑色素瘤患者中，这些菌属显著富集并与≥3 级 AEs 强相关；进一步流式分析显示 S. copri 定植与外周血 CD4+ T 细胞亚群比例增加相关，且该毒性仅在双 ICI 背景下显现，单药抗 PD-1 治疗中未观察到类似风险（P0583）。但 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（抗原或代谢物）尚未解析。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供供体无监督聚类结果及 Cluster B（Prevotella 富集）与≥3 级 AEs 强相关的因果关联证据\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U3_P02\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P02\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U3\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 2,\n                  \"point\": \"供体微生物组聚类与特定毒性事件的因果关联\",\n                  \"development\": \"基于 Bray-Curtis 指数无监督聚类将健康供体分为 Cluster A 与 Cluster B（含供体 5、11）。Cluster B 以 Segatella copri、Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119 等高丰度为特征。接受 Cluster B 供体 FMT 的黑色素瘤患者中，这些菌属显著富集并与≥3 级 AEs 强相关；进一步流式分析显示 S. copri 定植与外周血 CD4+ T 细胞亚群比例增加相关，且该毒性仅在双 ICI 背景下显现，单药抗 PD-1 治疗中未观察到类似风险（P0583）。但 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（抗原或代谢物）尚未解析。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0583\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P03\",\n              \"point\": \"益生菌的双向调节与伴随用药的干扰效应\",\n              \"development\": \"指出特定共生菌（如 LGG）可通过释放脂磷壁酸激活巨噬细胞保护肠上皮，但在免疫抑制状态下存在机会性感染风险（P0040）；同时汇总药物警戒数据，显示 PPI 联用可能增加肝胆及皮肤毒性报告率（P0088），而近期广谱抗生素暴露不仅削弱疗效，还独立增加严重结肠炎风险（P0310）。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0040\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"指出 LGG 激活巨噬细胞保护肠上皮但在免疫抑制状态下存在机会性感染风险\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0088\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"汇总药物警戒数据，显示 PPI 联用可能增加肝胆及皮肤毒性报告率\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0310\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"显示近期广谱抗生素暴露独立增加严重结肠炎风险\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0357\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"系统梳理益生菌菌株特异性效应及商业制剂异质性，阐明其在调节 irAEs 中的双向作用及定植挑战\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U3_P03\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U3_P03\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U3\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 3,\n                  \"point\": \"益生菌的双向调节与伴随用药的干扰效应\",\n                  \"development\": \"指出特定共生菌（如 LGG）可通过释放脂磷壁酸激活巨噬细胞保护肠上皮，但在免疫抑制状态下存在机会性感染风险（P0040）；同时汇总药物警戒数据，显示 PPI 联用可能增加肝胆及皮肤毒性报告率（P0088），而近期广谱抗生素暴露不仅削弱疗效，还独立增加严重结肠炎风险（P0310）。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0040\",\n                    \"P0088\",\n                    \"P0310\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"table_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"table_id\": \"Ch6_U3_T01\",\n              \"purpose\": \"比较 FMT 供体聚类特征与 ICI 方案交互下的毒性风险\",\n              \"columns\": [\n                \"供体聚类\",\n                \"特征菌属\",\n                \"ICI 方案背景\",\n                \"主要毒性事件\",\n                \"发生率/关联强度\"\n              ],\n              \"row_tasks\": [\n                {\n                  \"content\": \"Cluster A (非 Prevotella 富集)\",\n                  \"source_uses\": [\n                    {\n                      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                      \"role\": \"比较\",\n                      \"use\": \"提供 Cluster A 供体在双免背景下的安全性基线数据\"\n                    }\n                  ]\n                },\n                {\n                  \"content\": \"Cluster B (Prevotella/Segatella 富集)\",\n                  \"source_uses\": [\n                    {\n                      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                      \"role\": \"比较\",\n                      \"use\": \"提供 Cluster B 供体与加速发作心肌炎及≥3 级 AEs 的强关联数据\"\n                    }\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"owner_unit_context\": {\n            \"evidence_conditions\": \"\",\n            \"synthesis\": \"微生物干预的安全性具有严格的情境依赖性：供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella 富集）与 ICI 骨架（双免 vs 单免）的交互作用是触发加速发作心肌炎等严重 irAEs 的决定性因素，提示未来 FMT 试验必须建立基于供体聚类的风险分层筛选标准。但目前证据主要来自 Phase II 试验，缺乏 Phase III RCT 验证，且 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体分子通路未完全解析。\",\n            \"transition\": \"上述临床表型与干预结果的背后，隐藏着从肠道屏障破坏到远端器官免疫风暴的多层次分子通路，下一章将系统拆解介导这些毒性效应的具体生物学机制。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"荟萃分析量化FMT联合ICI的总体ORR(43%)及3-4级AE发生率(37%)，明确双药方案下毒性风险显著升高，为评估供体选择与免疫骨架交互的安全性边界提供定量基准。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0212\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"系统梳理益生菌菌株特异性效应及商业制剂异质性，阐明其在调节irAEs中的双向作用及定植挑战，用于支撑干预策略安全性讨论中的菌株依赖性与监管障碍。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"9bda8266e0dc2c5949effec25ef1dea48f7de6ee\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0357\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"unit_notes\": \"\",\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0212\",\n            \"P0040\",\n            \"P0088\",\n            \"P0310\",\n            \"P0357\"\n          ],\n          \"editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\"\n          ],\n          \"task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n              \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n              \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"local_editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n            \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n            \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n            \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\"\n          ],\n          \"fullbody_task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U4\",\n          \"focus\": \"介导毒性的分子与免疫通路机制\",\n          \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P01\",\n              \"point\": \"肠道屏障受损与内毒素易位的促炎级联\",\n              \"development\": \"描述 Akkermansia 等黏液降解菌减少或致病菌扩张导致的紧密连接蛋白（ZO-1, Occludin）表达下调，促使 LPS 入血并持续激活 TLR4/NF-κB 通路，为全身性 irAEs 提供持续的先天免疫刺激背景（P0217）。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0217\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"描述 Akkermansia 等黏液降解菌减少致 LPS 入血并激活 TLR4/NF-κB 通路的机制\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"揭示 Paraclostridium bifermentans 通过活菌破坏上皮屏障致结肠炎的具体机制\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U4_P01\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P01\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U4\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 1,\n                  \"point\": \"肠道屏障受损与内毒素易位的促炎级联\",\n                  \"development\": \"描述 Akkermansia 等黏液降解菌减少或致病菌扩张导致的紧密连接蛋白（ZO-1, Occludin）表达下调，促使 LPS 入血并持续激活 TLR4/NF-κB 通路，为全身性 irAEs 提供持续的先天免疫刺激背景（P0217）。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0217\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P02\",\n              \"point\": \"代谢物介导的表观遗传重编程与炎症抑制/促进\",\n              \"development\": \"指出非 irAEs 患者肠道中甲萘醌（维生素 K2）生物合成途径（menH/menC 基因）显著富集，血清甲萘醌水平更高，其可能通过抑制 NF-κB 通路发挥抗炎保护作用（P0308）；反之，SCFAs 在特定浓度下可通过 HDAC 抑制影响 Treg/Th17 分化平衡，剂量依赖性决定了其是维持稳态还是加剧炎症（P0472）。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0308\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"指出甲萘醌生物合成途径富集与血清甲萘醌水平更高及抗炎保护作用的关联\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0472\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"阐述 SCFAs 通过 HDAC 抑制影响 Treg/Th17 分化平衡的剂量依赖性效应\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"补充肠道微生物组代谢物与分子模拟驱动长期疗效和不良事件结局的机制线索\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U4_P02\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P02\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U4\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 2,\n                  \"point\": \"代谢物介导的表观遗传重编程与炎症抑制/促进\",\n                  \"development\": \"指出非 irAEs 患者肠道中甲萘醌（维生素 K2）生物合成途径（menH/menC 基因）显著富集，血清甲萘醌水平更高，其可能通过抑制 NF-κB 通路发挥抗炎保护作用（P0308）；反之，SCFAs 在特定浓度下可通过 HDAC 抑制影响 Treg/Th17 分化平衡，剂量依赖性决定了其是维持稳态还是加剧炎症（P0472）。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0308\",\n                    \"P0472\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P03\",\n              \"point\": \"MyD88 依赖的髓系激活与心肌炎中的 CD8+ T 细胞 TNF 轴\",\n              \"development\": \"综合临床前与转录组证据，阐明微生物抗原通过 MyD88 通路激活巨噬细胞分泌 TNFα/IL-6 导致肝损伤（P0126），或在 ICI 心肌炎中驱动 CD8+ T 细胞释放 TNF 并通过 TNFR2 信号招募髓系细胞、诱发心律失常（P0149）。结合 HLA 限制性抗原呈递框架，指出细菌肽段（如β-半乳糖苷酶）与心脏肌球蛋白的分子模拟可交叉激活自体反应性 CD4+/CD8+ T 细胞（P0597），但 Prevotella 特异性机制尚未解析。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0126\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"阐述肠道微生物通过 MyD88 通路激活巨噬细胞/CD8+ T 细胞引发肝损伤的炎症级联\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0149\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 ICI 心肌炎中 CD8+ T 细胞释放 TNF 并通过 TNFR2 信号诱发心律失常的机制证据\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n                  \"role\": \"主论据\",\n                  \"use\": \"结合 HLA 限制性抗原呈递框架，指出细菌肽段与心脏肌球蛋白的分子模拟机制\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n                  \"role\": \"例证\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 PD-1 抑制剂诱导心肌炎的动物实验证据，阐明肠道菌群失调通过抑制心脏局部 Treg 功能导致炎症的机制\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0604\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"综述 TN-C 介导的树突状细胞激活与 Th17 极化通路，以及特定肠道菌群通过分子模拟触发心脏自身免疫反应的实例\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n                  \"role\": \"发展\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供肠道微生物组作为 ICI 相关心肌炎新兴治疗靶点的理论框架与机制综述\"\n                }\n              ],\n              \"carried_over\": true,\n              \"point_changed_from_brief\": false,\n              \"source_briefs\": [\n                \"Ch6_U4_P03\"\n              ],\n              \"source_brief_details\": [\n                {\n                  \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch6_U4_P03\",\n                  \"unit_id\": \"Ch6_U4\",\n                  \"ordinal\": 3,\n                  \"point\": \"MyD88 依赖的髓系激活与心肌炎中的 CD8+ T 细胞 TNF 轴\",\n                  \"development\": \"综合临床前与转录组证据，阐明微生物抗原通过 MyD88 通路激活巨噬细胞分泌 TNFα/IL-6 导致肝损伤（P0126），或在 ICI 心肌炎中驱动 CD8+ T 细胞释放 TNF 并通过 TNFR2 信号招募髓系细胞、诱发心律失常（P0149）。结合 HLA 限制性抗原呈递框架，指出细菌肽段（如β-半乳糖苷酶）与心脏肌球蛋白的分子模拟可交叉激活自体反应性 CD4+/CD8+ T 细胞（P0597），但 Prevotella 特异性机制尚未解析。\",\n                  \"source_handles\": [\n                    \"P0126\",\n                    \"P0149\",\n                    \"P0597\"\n                  ]\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"table_tasks\": [],\n          \"owner_unit_context\": {\n            \"evidence_conditions\": \"\",\n            \"synthesis\": \"微生物介导的 irAEs 并非单一通路所致，而是屏障完整性丧失、代谢物信号失衡、分子模拟触发的交叉反应以及 MyD88/TNF 炎症级联共同作用的结果；理解这些通路有助于开发靶向特定节点（如 TNFR2 阻断、甲萘醌补充）的精准毒性管理策略。但机制证据多来自动物模型或体外实验，人体内直接验证有限，特别是 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制尚未解析。\",\n            \"transition\": \"综上所述，微生物组对 ICI 毒性的调节是一个多层次、情境依赖的系统工程。后续章节将基于本章确立的证据等级与机制框架，转向方法学挑战与未来标准化研究方向。\",\n            \"supporting_studies\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"结合宏基因组与培养组学揭示Paraclostridium bifermentans通过活菌破坏上皮屏障致结肠炎、同时分泌低分子量代谢物增强疗效的双重机制，为介导毒性的物理屏障与代谢通路提供实证对照。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0284\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"阐述肠道微生物通过MyD88通路激活巨噬细胞/CD8+ T细胞引发肝损伤的炎症级联，区分不同免疫激动剂背景下的髓系激活路径，补充系统性毒性介导的先天免疫机制细节。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"378cf66d179d103b23a392cdb8e99a650e346e11\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0126\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"提供PD-1抑制剂诱导心肌炎的动物实验证据，阐明肠道菌群失调通过抑制心脏局部Treg功能、打破Th17/Treg平衡导致炎症的具体机制，补充“肠道-心脏轴”介导毒性的分子细节。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0602\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"综述TN-C介导的树突状细胞激活与Th17极化通路，以及特定肠道菌群（如Bacteroides）通过分子模拟触发心脏自身免疫反应的实例，为解释非结肠炎irAEs的免疫病理机制提供理论框架。\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:231980805\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0604\"\n              }\n            ]\n          },\n          \"unit_notes\": \"\",\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0217\",\n            \"P0284\",\n            \"P0308\",\n            \"P0472\",\n            \"P0462\",\n            \"P0126\",\n            \"P0149\",\n            \"P0597\",\n            \"P0602\",\n            \"P0604\",\n            \"P0598\"\n          ],\n          \"editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n            \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n              \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n              \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          },\n          \"local_editable_task_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n            \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n            \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n          ],\n          \"fullbody_task_keys\": {\n            \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n              \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n            ],\n            \"table_tasks\": []\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"chapter_tool_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N64e929a3f9de2888bd6a-5a6b848383c152a3\",\n          \"question\": \"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群）在 FMT-LUMINate 研究中仅表现为相关性，是否有后续研究解析其下游信号通路？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"现有材料未提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或 FMT-LUMINate 研究的后续信号通路解析。提供的文献主要聚焦于肠道菌群对实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的调节机制，而非自身免疫性心肌炎。在肿瘤免疫背景下，Prevotella 属菌种与 ICI 治疗反应存在关联：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，特定 Prevotella OTU（如 OTU264, OTU263, OTU261）富集于影像学生物学应答者；同时，P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这被描述为减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫的作用，与心肌炎的致病机制不同。关于代谢物介导的 T 细胞激活机制，材料详细阐述了其他菌属的路径：L. plantarum 产生的 ILA 通过增强 DCs 中 IL-12 分泌激活 CD8+ T 细胞；B. pseudolongum 产物结合 CD4+ T 细胞 A2AR 促进 Th1 分化；以及色氨酸代谢物（如 IAA, IPA, ILA）通过 AhR 通路调节免疫。然而，这些机制均针对肿瘤微环境中的抗肿瘤免疫，未涉及 Prevotella 在心肌炎中的特异性抗原或代谢物-受体相互作用及下游信号级联。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或后续信号通路解析。在 P0583 研究中，Prevotella spp. 的定植与抗 CTLA-4 治疗相关的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）发生显著相关，但明确报告其与肿瘤反应（response）无关联，且未深入探讨其致病机制。其他综述性材料（如 P0261, P0319, P0447, P0460, P0486, P0036, P0013, P0146, P0297）主要聚焦于 Prevotella 或其他菌种通过代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节抗肿瘤免疫（如 CD8+ T 细胞激活、Treg 分化、DC 成熟）以增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的机制。虽然 P0486 提到某些微生物代谢物可能抑制 Tregs 并增强细胞毒性 T 细胞功能从而阻碍结直肠癌进展，P0447 讨论了色氨酸代谢物对免疫的微环境调节，但这些均属于抗肿瘤免疫调节范畴，并未涉及心肌炎这一特定自身免疫不良反应的分子通路。因此，关于 Prevotella 导致心肌炎的特异性抗原识别或下游信号级联反应，当前材料中缺乏直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This study identified pivotal immune-related genes (NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1) and signaling pathways (CD8+ T cell receptor, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, RAGE signaling) enriched in ICI-associated myocarditis samples compared to controls. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and highlighted cell lysis and proinflammatory pathways as characteristic biological enrichments. These findings provide a detailed map of the host immune response landscape in ICI-associated myocarditis, specifically emphasizing cytotoxic lymphocyte activation and inflammatory signaling cascades that could theoretically serve as downstream effectors if triggered by microbial antigens.\\\", \\\"This study utilized bioinformatics analysis on datasets GSE180045 and GSE4172 to characterize the molecular landscape of ICI-associated myocarditis (ICI-MC). The authors identified 32 immune-related differentially expressed genes (IR-DEGs) and highlighted hub genes including KLRB1, NKG7, and GZMH. Functional enrichment analyses indicated that the pathophysiology involves CD8+ T cell receptor signaling, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, cell lysis, and RAGE signaling. These findings delineate the downstream immune effector mechanisms (specifically cytotoxic T cell and NK cell activation) that characterize ICI-MC, providing a potential target profile for any upstream trigger, including microbial factors.\\\", \\\"本综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制框架，特别是“分子模拟”（molecular mimicry）概念。作者引用了 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该材料详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递（HLA 类分子向 CD4+ T 细胞呈递外源性肽段）在打破免疫耐受中的核心作用，以及微生物抗原如何通过交叉反应激活针对心脏自身抗原的免疫应答。这为理解肠道菌群（包括潜在的 Prevotella spp.）如何通过抗原模拟激活特定 T 细胞亚群提供了理论模型和机制参考。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The analysis relied on bioinformatics methods using the GSE180045 and GSE4172 datasets without explicit wet-lab validation of causal function reported in the abstract. The study design is retrospective and computational, focusing on transcriptomic differences between ICI patients with and without myocarditis. The authors noted drug predictions (e.g., acetohydroxamic-acid) via cMAP database but did not incorporate microbiome data or stratify patients by microbial composition such as Prevotella spp. abundance.\\\", \\\"The study design is a bioinformatics-based screening and validation approach rather than experimental validation of microbial causality. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and predicted potential target drugs, noting acetohydroxamic acid as a compound requiring caution during ICI treatment. The analysis distinguishes ICI-MC from other immune adverse events based on gene expression profiles. The results are derived from public transcriptomic datasets, and the authors note the findings are predictive or hypothesis-generating rather than causal proof.\\\", \\\"文中总结了 HLA 类 I 和类 II 分子在心肌炎中的不同功能（类 I 呈递病毒肽给 CD8+ T 细胞，类 II 呈递外源肽给 CD4+ T 细胞），并列出了与心肌炎或扩张型心肌病（DCM）相关的具体 HLA 等位基因（如 HLA-DR4, HLA-B27, HLA-DR15 等）。此外，文章提出了心肌炎的三相模型（触发、免疫反应、慢性炎症），并指出 HLA 多态性影响胸腺阴性选择和 T 细胞克隆扩增，这些背景信息有助于构建宿主遗传与环境互作的整体病理生理图景。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于下游信号通路的直接证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析明确了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主效应机制，发现 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 是关键枢纽基因，富集通路包括 CD8+ T 细胞受体信号、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路；但这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法建立微生物与这些通路的因果联系。P0597 提供了“分子模拟”理论框架，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可通过产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位相似的肽段，经 HLA 限制性抗原呈递激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，但该综述未涉及 Prevotella 的具体抗原或代谢物证据。P0261 仅报道了在接受抗 PD-(L)1 或联合治疗的患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263 等分类群与最佳放射学疗效存在关联，属于疗效预测标志物，而非心肌炎发病机制的研究。综上，目前缺乏将 Prevotella 特异性成分与 ICI-MC 中观察到的 CD8+/NK 细胞毒性或 RAGE 通路激活直接连接的实验性或临床验证数据。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析确定了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的关键宿主免疫效应基因（如 NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1）及通路（CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性、RAGE 信号），但明确指出这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法验证微生物触发假说。P0261 在人类临床数据中观察到特定菌群（包括 Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的相关性，但未涉及心肌炎机制或特异性抗原/代谢物。P0319 综述表格指出 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这主要关联于炎症缓解而非心肌炎的特异性 T 细胞激活机制。P0597 提供的理论框架（分子模拟）以拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）为例，未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性机制。因此，Prevotella 是否通过特定抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群并导致心肌炎的因果链条，在当前材料中仍为未解之谜。\\n\\n[\\\"该综述阐述了微生物组通过分子模拟（molecular mimicry）诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制。文中指出，共生细菌（引用 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，具体为拟杆菌属 Bacteroides species）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内启动自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该研究还提到抗生素治疗可阻断这一过程，证实了微生物组衍生抗原模拟在疾病启动中的因果作用。此外，文中详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递如何决定特定 T 细胞亚群（CD4+ 或 CD8+）的激活，以及下游的细胞因子放大和免疫细胞浸润机制，为理解微生物 - 宿主互作提供了理论框架。\\\", \\\"This study identifies a specific molecular mimicry mechanism where Bacillus infantis (strain NRRL B-14911) induces autoimmune myocarditis. The authors found that an epitope (BAC 25-40) from the bacterial allantoate amidohydrolase (AAH) protein shares sequence homology with cardiac myosin heavy chain alpha (Myhc-α 334-352). Active immunization with this epitope induced myocarditis in A/J mice by generating cardiac-reactive T cells. The study provides genomic evidence of virulence factors and confirms the conservation of this mimicry epitope. This serves as a concrete example of a bacterium inducing myocarditis via antigen-specific T cell cross-reactivity, which parallels the type of mechanism (antigen/metabolite -> T cell subset) sought in the gap question, albeit for a different bacterial species.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"文中提供了 HLA I 类和 II 类分子在心肌炎中的功能对比，包括抗原呈递对象（CD8+ vs CD4+ T 细胞）、表达细胞类型及在自身免疫中的具体角色。还涉及病毒持续感染与自身免疫的复杂关系，以及抗肌球蛋白自身抗体与β1-肾上腺素能受体的交叉反应机制。这些内容虽不直接针对 Prevotella，但构成了心肌炎免疫病理的基础背景。\\\", \\\"The authors performed complete genome sequencing using PacBio SMRT technology, phylogenetic analysis of 16S rRNA and ITS regions, and phenotypic microarray analysis to classify the bacterium as Bacillus infantis. They identified 623 potential virulence factors, including adhesins, invasins, and transporters. The study also notes the presence of unique methyltransferases and insertion sequence elements. These details support the characterization of the bacterium but are less directly relevant to the specific signaling pathway question regarding Prevotella.\\\"]\\n\\n当前提供的材料未能回答关于 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制及其在 FMT-LUMINate 研究后的后续解析进展。现有文献主要聚焦于以下两个与目标问题不直接匹配的方向：一是针对其他菌属（如 Bacillus infantis 或 Bacteroides）的分子模拟机制，证实了细菌抗原（如 AAH 蛋白表位）通过与心脏肌球蛋白同源性激活 CD4+ T 细胞导致心肌炎的通用原理，但这并非 Prevotella 的特异性证据；二是基于生物信息学分析的免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）宿主下游效应机制，识别出 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体和 RAGE 信号通路作为组织损伤的共同终末路径，但明确声明这些分析未纳入微生物组数据，无法建立特定微生物（如 Prevotella）与这些通路的因果联系。因此，Prevotella 特异性抗原/代谢物身份、其激活的特定 T 细胞亚群细节，以及 FMT-LUMINate 研究后是否有独立实验验证其下游信号通路，在当前材料中均处于未解状态。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。材料中关于 Prevotella 的信息主要局限于其与癌症免疫治疗疗效的相关性：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU263 等物种与最佳放射学反应（RECIST v1.1）相关；P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，从而减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫，这一代谢机制并未被证实与心肌炎发病有关。针对心肌炎机制，P0601 详细描述了 Bacillus infantis 通过分子模拟（BAC 25-40 表位与心脏肌球蛋白重链 α 同源性）激活心脏反应性 T 细胞的特异性路径，但这属于不同菌属的机制，不能外推至 Prevotella。P0595 和 P0596 阐明了免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主下游效应机制，包括 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因上调，以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路的富集，但这些研究均为生物信息学分析，未涉及微生物组数据，因此无法建立 Prevotella 与这些特定信号通路之间的因果联系。P0597 综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用框架（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides 的分子模拟），但未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性抗原或代谢物证据。综上，Prevotella 是否通过类似分子模拟或特定代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群进而触发上述 ICI-MC 信号通路，目前仍缺乏直接验证。\\n\\n[\\\"This study provides a mechanistic framework for how gut microbiota can trigger autoimmune myocarditis, specifically citing *Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron* where bacterial beta-galactosidase shares sequence homology with cardiac MyHC-α, inducing Th17 polarization. It also details a downstream signaling pathway in myocarditis involving Tenascin-C (TN-C) activating dendritic cells via TLR4 to produce IL-6, IL-1β, and GM-CSF, driving Th17 differentiation.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"General triggers of myocarditis including viruses (CVB3, SARS-CoV-2) and immune checkpoint inhibitors; description of central and peripheral immune tolerance mechanisms; TN-C as a biomarker for disease activity and prognosis.\\\"]\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"专门针对 Prevotella spp. 在心肌炎中的功能验证研究；FMT-LUMINate 研究团队发表的后续出版物，特别是那些旨在解析 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体抗原表位、代谢产物或其与 CD8+/CD4+ T 细胞交叉反应性的实验数据。\"\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"The supplied text does not mention *Prevotella spp.*, the FMT-LUMINate study, or any specific antigens, metabolites, or downstream signaling pathways associated with *Prevotella*-induced myocarditis. The specific molecular mechanism requested in the gap question remains unidentified in this material.\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0601\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"title\": \"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\n              \"year\": \"2016\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"title\": \"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\n              \"title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0486\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"daf9a1dede2bf1241ba0b187914be958d46b79fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Targeting Microbiome Metabolites: Reshaping Immunotherapy and Clinical Management Strategies for Colorectal Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/imm3.70030\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\n              \"title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"title\": \"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0601\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"title\": \"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\n              \"year\": \"2016\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:267380691\",\n              \"title\": \"Potential clinical implications of molecular mimicry‐induced autoimmunity\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"unresolved_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0604\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:231980805\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:231980805\",\n              \"title\": \"Immunomodulatory Role of Tenascin-C in Myocarditis and Inflammatory Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2021\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2021.624703\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"downloads\": 0,\n            \"model_calls\": 2,\n            \"source\": \"judge+focused_local_read\",\n            \"whole_paper_rereads\": 0\n          },\n          \"chapter_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6\"\n          ],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\",\n          \"question\": \"是否有针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究，以验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"提供的材料中未包含针对非结肠炎类 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有证据主要聚焦于免疫相关结肠炎（ir-colitis）或整体 irAE 分级与临床预后的关联。具体而言，P0284 对黑色素瘤和 NSCLC 患者进行了分析，其中 P0284 的摘要部分明确提到收集了 32 名发生 irAE 的患者粪便样本，并特别指出在培养组学分析中，21 名（66%）患者发生了 ir-colitis，11 名（34%）未发生；其机制验证部分也仅涉及 ir-colitis 的小鼠模型（FMT 实验）。P0017 同样仅关注“immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis”，比较了 8 例结肠炎性 irAE 和 24 例非结肠炎性 irAE 患者的微生物组差异，样本量较小且未扩展至其他器官特异性 irAEs。P0462 虽然探讨了长期生存和 irAEs 的整体关联及分子模拟机制，但未提供针对非结肠炎特定类型 irAEs 的大规模独立验证数据。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模微生物组证据在当前材料中缺失，无法直接解决样本量小或证据不足的问题。\\n\\n现有材料未提供针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究证据，无法证实 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题已得到解决。相反，材料显示目前的研究主要集中在结肠炎型 irAEs 或整体 irAEs 的发生上。例如，P0284 仅分析了 ir-colitis 患者的微生物特征；P0017 的摘要也明确限定于探讨肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂相关结肠炎的关系。虽然 P0197 提到了黑色素瘤患者中出现的心肌炎案例，但将其归因于特定供体菌群（Prevotella copri），这属于个案观察而非大规模验证研究。此外，P0067 指出不同器官的 irAEs 可能涉及不同的机制，且目前缺乏针对非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模数据支持。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组机制仍缺乏大规模研究的直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis. The authors report that while specific microbial signatures (e.g., Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides) and mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) have been identified, current research 'remains in its infancy.' The study explicitly states that therapeutic applications and mechanistic links are currently supported only by preclinical animal studies or small-scale clinical correlations, with 'clinical validation still pending' and a 'considerable distance between research and clinical practice.' It confirms that large-scale rigorously designed studies are lacking.\\\", \\\"The authors state that emerging evidence highlights the gut microbiota as a critical regulator potentially influencing the development and progression of ICI-associated cardiovascular toxicities, including severe conditions such as myocarditis. This study systematically analyzes the incidence, pathophysiological mechanisms, diagnostic criteria, and prognosis of major cardiovascular toxicities linked to ICIs in the context of microbiome interplay.\\\", \\\"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The review details specific mechanistic hypotheses such as the release of mimic peptides triggering autoimmune responses against the heart and the suppression of anti-inflammatory Tregs by dysbiosis. It also notes confounding factors like concomitant use of proton pump inhibitors or statins which may alter microbiota composition and irAE risk. Additionally, it highlights the controversy around antibiotic use, noting that while antibiotics reduced myocardial injury in mouse models, retrospective human studies associate broad-spectrum antibiotics with shortened survival and increased tumor progression risk during ICI therapy.\\\", \\\"The review explores immunomodulatory functions of the gut microbiome that may underlie these adverse events, emphasizing microbiota-mediated systemic immune dysregulation and cardiovascular-specific toxicity pathways. It also discusses future research directions and the clinical implications of integrating gut microbiota modulation into the management of ICI-associated cardiovascular complications.\\\", \\\"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究目前尚不存在。P0600 的研究虽然纳入了发生 irAEs 的患者，但明确将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并为一组进行分析，未对特定器官毒性进行验证；其数据中仅包含 3 例心肌炎病例，作者指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，针对不同类型 irAE 的亚组分析缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0284 的研究同样聚焦于结肠炎（ir-colitis），在黑色素瘤队列中仅有 14 例 ir-colitis 患者，且未涉及心肌炎或神经毒性的独立分析。尽管 P0284 通过宏基因组和培养组学证实了 ir-colitis 患者存在α多样性降低和特定菌群富集，但这些发现仅限于结肠炎表型。因此，当前证据不足以解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的关于非结肠炎 irAEs 样本量小或证据不足的问题，缺乏针对这些罕见非结肠炎表型的特异性微生物组机制验证。\\nP0600 (32名irAE患者队列) / 心肌炎病例数 / 基线微生物组分析时点：myocarditis: 3例\\nP0284 (黑色素瘤队列, n=45) / ir-colitis病例数 / ICI治疗前基线样本：ir-colitis: 14例\\nP0284 (培养组学亚组, n=32) / ir-colitis检出菌种中位数 / 基线或急性期粪便样本：ir-colitis group: 12 species；no-ir-colitis group: 22 species\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏。多项研究指出，由于特定类型 irAEs 发生率较低或样本量有限，亚组分析往往缺乏统计效力或无法进行。例如，P0600 的研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎患者，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组可能缺乏统计效力或不可行。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的整体微生物组差异，但未对心肌炎等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的关联分析。此外，P0197 的摘要提到在黑色素瘤 FMT 试验中，13 名出现 >3 级 irAE 的患者中有 3 例（15%）发生心肌炎，并观察到供体 D5 的粪菌移植与心肌炎相关，但这属于小样本观察性数据，而非大规模验证性研究。其他研究如 P0011 虽然分析了皮肤、血液、内分泌和肝脏毒性，但并未提供针对心肌炎或神经毒性的大规模独立队列数据。因此，目前仍缺乏能够充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题的大规模特异性研究。\\n\\n[\\\"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\\\", \\\"This study provides preclinical mechanistic evidence linking gut microbiota to PD-1 inhibitor-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. The authors established a melanoma mouse model (n=6 per group) showing that PD-1 inhibition induced myocarditis, reduced cardiac regulatory T cells (Tregs), and altered gut microbiota composition. Specific taxa (e.g., Ruminococcaceae, Flexispira) were correlated with cardiac injury markers (CK-MB, cTn-I) and Treg-related gene expression (FOXP3, IL-10). Fecal microbiota removal (antibiotic treatment) attenuated myocarditis and restored Treg levels without compromising antitumor efficacy in this model. These findings support the biological plausibility of a microbiome-immune axis in non-colitis irAEs.\\\", \\\"该综述确认了肠道微生物群被视为 ICI 相关心血管不良事件（包括心肌炎）的关键调节者，并提出了微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调和心血管特异性毒性通路作为潜在机制。作者指出该领域证据正在涌现（Emerging evidence），并强调需要整合微生物群调节管理，这间接支持了当前可能缺乏成熟大规模验证研究的现状。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\\\", \\\"The introduction and discussion cite general background on the association between gut dysbiosis and cardiovascular or autoimmune diseases, and the role of Tregs in maintaining immune homeostasis. The methods detail the 16S rRNA sequencing protocol and the antibiotic cocktail used for microbiota depletion, which may inform future experimental designs. The study also notes limitations such as the small number of experimental animals and the resolution limits of 16S sequencing.\\\", \\\"综述提供了 ICI 相关心血管毒性的发病率、病理生理机制、诊断标准和预后的系统分析框架，旨在为基础和临床研究提供理论基础。材料明确区分了安全性事件（如心肌炎）与治疗效果，但指出免疫调节功能可能 underlying 这些不良事件。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎免疫相关不良反应（irAEs，如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究目前仍然缺乏。具体而言：1. P0600 研究纳入了32名发生irAEs的患者，其中包含3例心肌炎，但作者明确指出由于样本量小且irAE发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型irAE患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行，因此未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。2. P0462 研究是一个前瞻性队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），其严重irAE组仅包含13例患者，其中包括2例心血管毒性和1例肌肉毒性，同样未针对特定非结肠炎亚型进行大规模独立分析，且作者承认样本量有限。3. P0602 提供的是临床前小鼠模型证据（每组n=6），虽然证实了肠道菌群与PD-1抑制剂诱导的心肌炎之间的因果机制（通过调节心脏调节性T细胞），但这属于小规模动物实验，并非人类临床队列的大规模关联研究。综上，现有文献多将非结肠炎irAEs合并分析或因病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，未能充分验证P0051和P0530中提到的证据不足问题。\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏，未能充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题。具体而言：\\n\\n1. **人类队列研究的局限性**：多项已发表的人类研究（如 P0600, P0462, P0049）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论。例如，P0600 纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0462 的严重 irAE 组（n=13）中包含多种类型的 irAEs（包括 2 例心血管毒性），但未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析，且作者承认样本量相对较小。\\n\\n2. **动物模型的补充与局限**：虽然有小规模动物实验（如 P0602，每组 n=6）提供了机制性证据，显示 PD-1 抑制诱导的小鼠心肌炎与肠道微生物群改变及调节性 T 细胞（Tregs）减少有关，并通过粪菌移植（FMT）验证了因果作用，但这些研究规模小，属于临床前模型，不能替代大规模人类队列研究来验证临床流行病学证据。\\n\\n3. **综述与背景研究的共识**：相关综述（如 P0603）指出，尽管有理论框架支持微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调可能导致心肌炎等非结肠炎 irAEs，但该领域的实证证据正在涌现但仍显不足，呼吁未来需要整合更大规模的微生物组数据。\\n\\n综上，目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模、独立分析的微生物组关联研究。现有研究多受限于样本量，无法提供足够的统计效力来明确区分不同器官特异性 irAEs 的微生物组特征。\\n\\n[\\\"This prospective cohort study (Verheijden et al., 2025) analyzed 497 stool samples from 195 cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) to assess gut microbiome associations with severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The study included various irAE types listed in Table 1, such as myocarditis (n=2 total), meningitis (n=2 total), pneumonitis (n=4 total), and colitis (n=6 total), but aggregated them into a single 'severe irAE' endpoint for analysis due to low incidence of individual types. Key findings indicated that a higher baseline relative abundance of a prespecified pathobiont group and a stronger decrease in Ruminococcaceae during treatment were associated with developing severe irAEs. At irAE onset, Ruminococcaceae and specific species (R. bromii, R. callidus) were significantly lower, while Haemophilus parainfluenzae was higher compared to other time points. The authors explicitly note in Section 3.6 that only 17 patients provided samples at severe irAE onset, with diverse irAE types (8 colitis, 3 pancreatitis/diabetes, 2 meningitis, 4 others), limiting subtype-specific analysis.\\\", \\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. It identifies specific microbial signatures linked to severe irAEs, such as higher abundance of pathobionts, decreased Ruminococcaceae, and dynamic changes in Bacteroides (citing Verheijden et al., 2025; Zeng et al., 2023). The authors propose mechanistic hypotheses including molecular mimicry between microbial epitopes and cardiac tissues, and microbiota-mediated suppression of regulatory T cells (Tregs). Crucially, the text explicitly states that current research on this relationship remains in its infancy, mechanisms are incompletely elucidated, and therapeutic applications (e.g., antibiotics) are supported only by preclinical evidence with clinical validation pending. This directly corroborates the gap's premise regarding insufficient evidence and small sample sizes in non-colitis irAE microbiome studies.\\\", \\\"该研究在黑色素瘤小鼠模型中（每组 n=6）证实了 PD-1 抑制剂治疗会改变肠道菌群组成（如 Ruminococcaceae、Flexispira 等富集），并与心肌炎严重程度及心脏调节性 T 细胞（Treg）减少显著相关。研究通过粪便微生物清除实验（FMR）表明，抗生素干预可减轻 PD-1 抑制剂诱导的心肌炎，同时保持抗肿瘤效果，提示肠道菌群通过调节 Treg 功能参与非结肠炎 irAE（心肌炎）的发病机制。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed a robust methodological framework useful for review methodology discussions, including longitudinal sampling (baseline, during treatment, at irAE onset, post-immunosuppression), both 16S rRNA and metagenomic shotgun sequencing, and multiple differential abundance tools (ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2) to ensure consistency. The authors discuss limitations regarding sample size for specific taxa and the need for correction for multiple testing, which resulted in some baseline associations (e.g., pathobionts) losing significance after correction.\\\", \\\"The review discusses confounding factors such as concomitant medications (proton pump inhibitors, statins) that may modulate the gut microbiota and influence irAE risk, suggesting these need stratified analysis in future research. It also notes the heterogeneity of ICI-associated myocarditis incidence across different cancer types, warranting further investigation. The text mentions specific preclinical interventions, such as fecal microbiota removal using antibiotic cocktails in mice, which reduced myocardial injury, but emphasizes these findings lack human clinical validation.\\\", \\\"作者明确指出该研究受限于实验动物数量有限（n=6），结论需更大样本量研究进一步确认；且 16S rRNA 测序无法精确到菌种水平，缺乏单一菌群或代谢物的直接因果验证。此外，文中引用了肠道菌群失调与心血管及自身免疫疾病关联的既往背景，为综述提供理论依据。\\\"]\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"需要检索是否有近期发表的、专门针对非结肠炎 irAEs（特别是心肌炎、神经毒性等罕见类型）的大规模微生物组关联研究（human cohort studies）。重点寻找样本量足以支持亚组分析或独立分析的研究，以及多中心联合队列或 Meta 分析结果。\"\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"The gap question asks for large-scale microbiome association studies specifically targeting non-colitis irAEs (e.g., myocarditis, neurotoxicity) to verify evidence insufficiency. This study does not fulfill that requirement because it aggregates all severe irAEs into one group; the specific counts for non-colitis irAEs like myocarditis (n=2) and meningitis (n=2) are too small for independent large-scale association analysis. Thus, the existence of a dedicated large-scale study for non-colitis irAE microbiome signatures remains unconfirmed by this material.\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0197\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"55e5f184350846573ce6b2d40fdcbd15f2602f90\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 2210: Microbiome profiling reveals that fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) modulates response and toxicity when combined with immunotherapy in patients with lung cancer and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate NCT04951583)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2025-2210\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0599\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0605\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"downloads\": 0,\n            \"model_calls\": 2,\n            \"source\": \"judge+focused_local_read\",\n            \"whole_paper_rereads\": 0\n          },\n          \"chapter_ids\": [\n            \"Ch6\"\n          ],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-b3c8ffc2a0ced9d8\",\n          \"question\": \"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"answer_from_local\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"现有文献中尚未发现已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在实体瘤中的疗效。目前最高级别的证据来自 Phase IIa 阶段的随机对照试验和单臂研究，结果呈现异质性且未达成最终确证。\\n\\n具体而言，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）一线治疗患者的 Phase 2a 随机双盲安慰剂对照试验。虽然其次要终点中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点 12 个月 PFS 率未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）虽呈有利趋势但未达显著性（P=0.167）。这表明在特定癌种和一线治疗背景下，FMT 显示出潜在的临床活性信号，但尚不足以作为确证性证据。\\n\\n相比之下，MITRIC 试验是一项针对多种晚期实体瘤（包括黑色素瘤、头颈鳞癌等）ICI 耐药患者的单臂 Phase IIa 篮式试验。该研究结果显示 FMT 安全性良好，但临床疗效有限：客观缓解率（ORR）为 0%，中位 PFS 仅为 1.5 个月，仅 1 名患者获得长期疾病稳定。机制分析提示，这种疗效局限可能与供体菌群定植短暂、宿主基线免疫环境（如髓系优势、高 IL-8）反映的是疾病状态而非 FMT 的直接作用有关。\\n\\n此外，Kim 等人（2024）发表的一项前瞻性单臂研究显示，在抗 PD-1 耐药的晚期实体瘤中，FMT 联合抗 PD-1 治疗可获得 7.7% 的 ORR 和 46.2% 的疾病控制率，并鉴定出特定的有益菌株（Prevotella merdae Immunoactis）。然而，由于缺乏随机对照设计和较大的样本量，这属于概念验证性质的探索性数据。\\n\\n综上所述，尽管有 Phase 2a RCT 显示部分指标改善，也有单臂研究提供机制支持，但目前缺乏大型 III 期 RCT 来确证 FMT 在广泛实体瘤人群中的确切疗效和生存获益。现有的阴性或混合结果提示疗效高度依赖于癌症类型、治疗线数（一线 vs 耐药）、供体选择及宿主免疫背景。\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR: 0%; Median PFS: 1.5 months; Clinical benefit (SD >6mo): 1/12 patients / Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory advanced solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic cancer)：Total (n=12): ORR 0%, Median PFS 1.5 mo\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate: 70% vs 41% (P=0.053); Median PFS: 24.0 vs 9.0 months (HR=0.50, P=0.035); Median OS: 41.0 vs 28.3 months (P=0.167) / Phase 2a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive metastatic RCC (pembrolizumab + axitinib)：Donor FMT (d-FMT) (n=23 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 70%, Median PFS 24.0 mo, Median OS 41.0 mo；Placebo FMT (p-FMT) (n=22 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 41%, Median PFS 9.0 mo, Median OS 28.3 mo\\nKim et al. (P0594) / ORR: 7.7%; DCR: 46.2% / Prospective single-arm single-center study, anti-PD-1 refractory advanced solid cancers (gastric, esophageal, HCC)：Total (n=13): ORR 7.7%, DCR 46.2%\\n\\n截至当前材料覆盖的时间范围（主要文献发表于2024-2025年，系统综述更新至2026年中），尚无已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的确切疗效。现有最高级别的临床证据为 II 期随机对照试验（RCT）。例如，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者的双盲、安慰剂对照 Phase 2a RCT，结果显示虽然中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点（12个月 PFS 率）未达到统计学显著性（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）未显示显著差异。此外，多项单臂 II 期研究（如 MITRIC 试验在 ICI 耐药患者中 ORR 为 0%，FMT-LUMINate 试验在黑色素瘤中 ORR 为 70% 但伴随高比例严重免疫相关不良事件）提供了初步信号，但缺乏对照组验证。多篇综述明确指出，目前证据主要来自回顾性队列或早期（I/II 期）试验，亟需大规模、多中心、标准化的 III 期 RCT 来确证疗效并建立预测模型。\\n\\n[\\\"This study is a systematic review and meta-analysis (search up to September 30, 2024) that included 10 studies involving 164 patients with solid tumors treated with FMT combined with ICIs. The authors report that the included studies comprised 5 phase I trials, 4 phase II–III trials, and 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs), but note that most were early-phase clinical trials with small sample sizes. The pooled objective response rate (ORR) was 43%, with subgroup analysis showing higher ORR (60%) for anti-PD-1 combined with anti-CTLA-4 therapy compared to monotherapy (37%). Crucially, the authors conclude in both the Abstract and Discussion that 'larger-scale randomized controlled trials with long-term follow-up are required to confirm and optimize treatment protocols' and highlight the 'absence of randomized controlled trials' (referring to large-scale/definitive ones) as a limitation. This material directly addresses the gap question by confirming that while preliminary RCT data exists, completed large-scale Phase III evidence is currently lacking and identified as a necessary future step.\\\", \\\"This review explicitly addresses the current clinical evidence level for microbiome interventions in cancer immunotherapy. The authors report that for Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT), the most developed clinical evidence comes from Phase 1 studies in melanoma patients showing recovery of anti–PD-1 response in some cases. For colorectal cancer (CRC), the authors cite a Phase 2 study evaluating FMT with immunotherapy and targeted therapy that reported improvement signals but was designed without a control group, making effectiveness determination difficult. The authors conclude that large-scale prospective studies and well-designed randomized controlled trials are still needed before routine clinical use, and frame FMT in CRC as an investigational intervention rather than an established treatment.\\\", \\\"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study provides detailed safety data (42% grade 1–2 adverse events, 37% grade 3–4 adverse events) and mechanistic hypotheses (e.g., increasing beneficial bacteria like Akkermansia muciniphila, modulating tumor microenvironment) which, while not validating the Phase III gap, offer context on why such trials are being pursued. It also notes heterogeneity in FMT protocols (donor sources, administration routes) as a barrier that large-scale trials need to standardize.\\\", \\\"The review details mechanistic pathways linking specific gut microbes to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) response, which provides biological rationale for ongoing trials. For example, Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) is described as promoting immune evasion via Fap2-TIGIT binding and chemotherapy resistance, while Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) is linked to anti–PD-1 resistance via MDSC activation. Conversely, beneficial bacteria like Bifidobacterium are noted in preclinical models to enhance antitumor efficacy of PD-1 blockade. The authors also discuss confounding factors in microbiome research (e.g., stool transit time, BMI) that complicate biomarker and intervention standardization, relevant for designing future rigorous trials.\\\", \\\"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [],\n          \"still_missing\": \"\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n              \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n              \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0212\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0212\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\n              \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_handle\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W4411127845\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0590\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286044272\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:286044272\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome in colorectal cancer: recent advances and clinical implications\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3393/ac.2026.00010.0001\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"OpenAlex:W3203589616\",\n              \"title\": \"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\n              \"year\": \"2021\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers13194824\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"unresolved_identity\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"chapter_ids\": [],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\",\n          \"question\": \"是否有针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究，以验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"提供的材料中未包含针对非结肠炎类 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有证据主要聚焦于免疫相关结肠炎（ir-colitis）或整体 irAE 分级与临床预后的关联。具体而言，P0284 对黑色素瘤和 NSCLC 患者进行了分析，其中 P0284 的摘要部分明确提到收集了 32 名发生 irAE 的患者粪便样本，并特别指出在培养组学分析中，21 名（66%）患者发生了 ir-colitis，11 名（34%）未发生；其机制验证部分也仅涉及 ir-colitis 的小鼠模型（FMT 实验）。P0017 同样仅关注“immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis”，比较了 8 例结肠炎性 irAE 和 24 例非结肠炎性 irAE 患者的微生物组差异，样本量较小且未扩展至其他器官特异性 irAEs。P0462 虽然探讨了长期生存和 irAEs 的整体关联及分子模拟机制，但未提供针对非结肠炎特定类型 irAEs 的大规模独立验证数据。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模微生物组证据在当前材料中缺失，无法直接解决样本量小或证据不足的问题。\\n\\n现有材料未提供针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究证据，无法证实 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题已得到解决。相反，材料显示目前的研究主要集中在结肠炎型 irAEs 或整体 irAEs 的发生上。例如，P0284 仅分析了 ir-colitis 患者的微生物特征；P0017 的摘要也明确限定于探讨肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂相关结肠炎的关系。虽然 P0197 提到了黑色素瘤患者中出现的心肌炎案例，但将其归因于特定供体菌群（Prevotella copri），这属于个案观察而非大规模验证研究。此外，P0067 指出不同器官的 irAEs 可能涉及不同的机制，且目前缺乏针对非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模数据支持。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组机制仍缺乏大规模研究的直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis. The authors report that while specific microbial signatures (e.g., Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides) and mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) have been identified, current research 'remains in its infancy.' The study explicitly states that therapeutic applications and mechanistic links are currently supported only by preclinical animal studies or small-scale clinical correlations, with 'clinical validation still pending' and a 'considerable distance between research and clinical practice.' It confirms that large-scale rigorously designed studies are lacking.\\\", \\\"The authors state that emerging evidence highlights the gut microbiota as a critical regulator potentially influencing the development and progression of ICI-associated cardiovascular toxicities, including severe conditions such as myocarditis. This study systematically analyzes the incidence, pathophysiological mechanisms, diagnostic criteria, and prognosis of major cardiovascular toxicities linked to ICIs in the context of microbiome interplay.\\\", \\\"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The review details specific mechanistic hypotheses such as the release of mimic peptides triggering autoimmune responses against the heart and the suppression of anti-inflammatory Tregs by dysbiosis. It also notes confounding factors like concomitant use of proton pump inhibitors or statins which may alter microbiota composition and irAE risk. Additionally, it highlights the controversy around antibiotic use, noting that while antibiotics reduced myocardial injury in mouse models, retrospective human studies associate broad-spectrum antibiotics with shortened survival and increased tumor progression risk during ICI therapy.\\\", \\\"The review explores immunomodulatory functions of the gut microbiome that may underlie these adverse events, emphasizing microbiota-mediated systemic immune dysregulation and cardiovascular-specific toxicity pathways. It also discusses future research directions and the clinical implications of integrating gut microbiota modulation into the management of ICI-associated cardiovascular complications.\\\", \\\"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究目前尚不存在。P0600 的研究虽然纳入了发生 irAEs 的患者，但明确将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并为一组进行分析，未对特定器官毒性进行验证；其数据中仅包含 3 例心肌炎病例，作者指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，针对不同类型 irAE 的亚组分析缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0284 的研究同样聚焦于结肠炎（ir-colitis），在黑色素瘤队列中仅有 14 例 ir-colitis 患者，且未涉及心肌炎或神经毒性的独立分析。尽管 P0284 通过宏基因组和培养组学证实了 ir-colitis 患者存在α多样性降低和特定菌群富集，但这些发现仅限于结肠炎表型。因此，当前证据不足以解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的关于非结肠炎 irAEs 样本量小或证据不足的问题，缺乏针对这些罕见非结肠炎表型的特异性微生物组机制验证。\\nP0600 (32名irAE患者队列) / 心肌炎病例数 / 基线微生物组分析时点：myocarditis: 3例\\nP0284 (黑色素瘤队列, n=45) / ir-colitis病例数 / ICI治疗前基线样本：ir-colitis: 14例\\nP0284 (培养组学亚组, n=32) / ir-colitis检出菌种中位数 / 基线或急性期粪便样本：ir-colitis group: 12 species；no-ir-colitis group: 22 species\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏。多项研究指出，由于特定类型 irAEs 发生率较低或样本量有限，亚组分析往往缺乏统计效力或无法进行。例如，P0600 的研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎患者，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组可能缺乏统计效力或不可行。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的整体微生物组差异，但未对心肌炎等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的关联分析。此外，P0197 的摘要提到在黑色素瘤 FMT 试验中，13 名出现 >3 级 irAE 的患者中有 3 例（15%）发生心肌炎，并观察到供体 D5 的粪菌移植与心肌炎相关，但这属于小样本观察性数据，而非大规模验证性研究。其他研究如 P0011 虽然分析了皮肤、血液、内分泌和肝脏毒性，但并未提供针对心肌炎或神经毒性的大规模独立队列数据。因此，目前仍缺乏能够充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题的大规模特异性研究。\\n\\n[\\\"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\\\", \\\"This study provides preclinical mechanistic evidence linking gut microbiota to PD-1 inhibitor-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. The authors established a melanoma mouse model (n=6 per group) showing that PD-1 inhibition induced myocarditis, reduced cardiac regulatory T cells (Tregs), and altered gut microbiota composition. Specific taxa (e.g., Ruminococcaceae, Flexispira) were correlated with cardiac injury markers (CK-MB, cTn-I) and Treg-related gene expression (FOXP3, IL-10). Fecal microbiota removal (antibiotic treatment) attenuated myocarditis and restored Treg levels without compromising antitumor efficacy in this model. These findings support the biological plausibility of a microbiome-immune axis in non-colitis irAEs.\\\", \\\"该综述确认了肠道微生物群被视为 ICI 相关心血管不良事件（包括心肌炎）的关键调节者，并提出了微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调和心血管特异性毒性通路作为潜在机制。作者指出该领域证据正在涌现（Emerging evidence），并强调需要整合微生物群调节管理，这间接支持了当前可能缺乏成熟大规模验证研究的现状。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\\\", \\\"The introduction and discussion cite general background on the association between gut dysbiosis and cardiovascular or autoimmune diseases, and the role of Tregs in maintaining immune homeostasis. The methods detail the 16S rRNA sequencing protocol and the antibiotic cocktail used for microbiota depletion, which may inform future experimental designs. The study also notes limitations such as the small number of experimental animals and the resolution limits of 16S sequencing.\\\", \\\"综述提供了 ICI 相关心血管毒性的发病率、病理生理机制、诊断标准和预后的系统分析框架，旨在为基础和临床研究提供理论基础。材料明确区分了安全性事件（如心肌炎）与治疗效果，但指出免疫调节功能可能 underlying 这些不良事件。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎免疫相关不良反应（irAEs，如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究目前仍然缺乏。具体而言：1. P0600 研究纳入了32名发生irAEs的患者，其中包含3例心肌炎，但作者明确指出由于样本量小且irAE发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型irAE患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行，因此未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。2. P0462 研究是一个前瞻性队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），其严重irAE组仅包含13例患者，其中包括2例心血管毒性和1例肌肉毒性，同样未针对特定非结肠炎亚型进行大规模独立分析，且作者承认样本量有限。3. P0602 提供的是临床前小鼠模型证据（每组n=6），虽然证实了肠道菌群与PD-1抑制剂诱导的心肌炎之间的因果机制（通过调节心脏调节性T细胞），但这属于小规模动物实验，并非人类临床队列的大规模关联研究。综上，现有文献多将非结肠炎irAEs合并分析或因病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，未能充分验证P0051和P0530中提到的证据不足问题。\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏，未能充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题。具体而言：\\n\\n1. **人类队列研究的局限性**：多项已发表的人类研究（如 P0600, P0462, P0049）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论。例如，P0600 纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0462 的严重 irAE 组（n=13）中包含多种类型的 irAEs（包括 2 例心血管毒性），但未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析，且作者承认样本量相对较小。\\n\\n2. **动物模型的补充与局限**：虽然有小规模动物实验（如 P0602，每组 n=6）提供了机制性证据，显示 PD-1 抑制诱导的小鼠心肌炎与肠道微生物群改变及调节性 T 细胞（Tregs）减少有关，并通过粪菌移植（FMT）验证了因果作用，但这些研究规模小，属于临床前模型，不能替代大规模人类队列研究来验证临床流行病学证据。\\n\\n3. **综述与背景研究的共识**：相关综述（如 P0603）指出，尽管有理论框架支持微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调可能导致心肌炎等非结肠炎 irAEs，但该领域的实证证据正在涌现但仍显不足，呼吁未来需要整合更大规模的微生物组数据。\\n\\n综上，目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模、独立分析的微生物组关联研究。现有研究多受限于样本量，无法提供足够的统计效力来明确区分不同器官特异性 irAEs 的微生物组特征。\\n\\n[\\\"This prospective cohort study (Verheijden et al., 2025) analyzed 497 stool samples from 195 cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) to assess gut microbiome associations with severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The study included various irAE types listed in Table 1, such as myocarditis (n=2 total), meningitis (n=2 total), pneumonitis (n=4 total), and colitis (n=6 total), but aggregated them into a single 'severe irAE' endpoint for analysis due to low incidence of individual types. Key findings indicated that a higher baseline relative abundance of a prespecified pathobiont group and a stronger decrease in Ruminococcaceae during treatment were associated with developing severe irAEs. At irAE onset, Ruminococcaceae and specific species (R. bromii, R. callidus) were significantly lower, while Haemophilus parainfluenzae was higher compared to other time points. The authors explicitly note in Section 3.6 that only 17 patients provided samples at severe irAE onset, with diverse irAE types (8 colitis, 3 pancreatitis/diabetes, 2 meningitis, 4 others), limiting subtype-specific analysis.\\\", \\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. It identifies specific microbial signatures linked to severe irAEs, such as higher abundance of pathobionts, decreased Ruminococcaceae, and dynamic changes in Bacteroides (citing Verheijden et al., 2025; Zeng et al., 2023). The authors propose mechanistic hypotheses including molecular mimicry between microbial epitopes and cardiac tissues, and microbiota-mediated suppression of regulatory T cells (Tregs). Crucially, the text explicitly states that current research on this relationship remains in its infancy, mechanisms are incompletely elucidated, and therapeutic applications (e.g., antibiotics) are supported only by preclinical evidence with clinical validation pending. This directly corroborates the gap's premise regarding insufficient evidence and small sample sizes in non-colitis irAE microbiome studies.\\\", \\\"该研究在黑色素瘤小鼠模型中（每组 n=6）证实了 PD-1 抑制剂治疗会改变肠道菌群组成（如 Ruminococcaceae、Flexispira 等富集），并与心肌炎严重程度及心脏调节性 T 细胞（Treg）减少显著相关。研究通过粪便微生物清除实验（FMR）表明，抗生素干预可减轻 PD-1 抑制剂诱导的心肌炎，同时保持抗肿瘤效果，提示肠道菌群通过调节 Treg 功能参与非结肠炎 irAE（心肌炎）的发病机制。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed a robust methodological framework useful for review methodology discussions, including longitudinal sampling (baseline, during treatment, at irAE onset, post-immunosuppression), both 16S rRNA and metagenomic shotgun sequencing, and multiple differential abundance tools (ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2) to ensure consistency. The authors discuss limitations regarding sample size for specific taxa and the need for correction for multiple testing, which resulted in some baseline associations (e.g., pathobionts) losing significance after correction.\\\", \\\"The review discusses confounding factors such as concomitant medications (proton pump inhibitors, statins) that may modulate the gut microbiota and influence irAE risk, suggesting these need stratified analysis in future research. It also notes the heterogeneity of ICI-associated myocarditis incidence across different cancer types, warranting further investigation. The text mentions specific preclinical interventions, such as fecal microbiota removal using antibiotic cocktails in mice, which reduced myocardial injury, but emphasizes these findings lack human clinical validation.\\\", \\\"作者明确指出该研究受限于实验动物数量有限（n=6），结论需更大样本量研究进一步确认；且 16S rRNA 测序无法精确到菌种水平，缺乏单一菌群或代谢物的直接因果验证。此外，文中引用了肠道菌群失调与心血管及自身免疫疾病关联的既往背景，为综述提供理论依据。\\\"]\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"需要检索是否有近期发表的、专门针对非结肠炎 irAEs（特别是心肌炎、神经毒性等罕见类型）的大规模微生物组关联研究（human cohort studies）。重点寻找样本量足以支持亚组分析或独立分析的研究，以及多中心联合队列或 Meta 分析结果。\"\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"The gap question asks for large-scale microbiome association studies specifically targeting non-colitis irAEs (e.g., myocarditis, neurotoxicity) to verify evidence insufficiency. This study does not fulfill that requirement because it aggregates all severe irAEs into one group; the specific counts for non-colitis irAEs like myocarditis (n=2) and meningitis (n=2) are too small for independent large-scale association analysis. Thus, the existence of a dedicated large-scale study for non-colitis irAE microbiome signatures remains unconfirmed by this material.\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0197\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"55e5f184350846573ce6b2d40fdcbd15f2602f90\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 2210: Microbiome profiling reveals that fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) modulates response and toxicity when combined with immunotherapy in patients with lung cancer and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate NCT04951583)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2025-2210\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0599\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0605\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"chapter_ids\": [],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N64e929a3f9de2888bd6a-5a6b848383c152a3\",\n          \"question\": \"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群）在 FMT-LUMINate 研究中仅表现为相关性，是否有后续研究解析其下游信号通路？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"现有材料未提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或 FMT-LUMINate 研究的后续信号通路解析。提供的文献主要聚焦于肠道菌群对实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的调节机制，而非自身免疫性心肌炎。在肿瘤免疫背景下，Prevotella 属菌种与 ICI 治疗反应存在关联：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，特定 Prevotella OTU（如 OTU264, OTU263, OTU261）富集于影像学生物学应答者；同时，P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这被描述为减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫的作用，与心肌炎的致病机制不同。关于代谢物介导的 T 细胞激活机制，材料详细阐述了其他菌属的路径：L. plantarum 产生的 ILA 通过增强 DCs 中 IL-12 分泌激活 CD8+ T 细胞；B. pseudolongum 产物结合 CD4+ T 细胞 A2AR 促进 Th1 分化；以及色氨酸代谢物（如 IAA, IPA, ILA）通过 AhR 通路调节免疫。然而，这些机制均针对肿瘤微环境中的抗肿瘤免疫，未涉及 Prevotella 在心肌炎中的特异性抗原或代谢物-受体相互作用及下游信号级联。\\n\\n现有材料未能提供 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制或后续信号通路解析。在 P0583 研究中，Prevotella spp. 的定植与抗 CTLA-4 治疗相关的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）发生显著相关，但明确报告其与肿瘤反应（response）无关联，且未深入探讨其致病机制。其他综述性材料（如 P0261, P0319, P0447, P0460, P0486, P0036, P0013, P0146, P0297）主要聚焦于 Prevotella 或其他菌种通过代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节抗肿瘤免疫（如 CD8+ T 细胞激活、Treg 分化、DC 成熟）以增强免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的机制。虽然 P0486 提到某些微生物代谢物可能抑制 Tregs 并增强细胞毒性 T 细胞功能从而阻碍结直肠癌进展，P0447 讨论了色氨酸代谢物对免疫的微环境调节，但这些均属于抗肿瘤免疫调节范畴，并未涉及心肌炎这一特定自身免疫不良反应的分子通路。因此，关于 Prevotella 导致心肌炎的特异性抗原识别或下游信号级联反应，当前材料中缺乏直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This study identified pivotal immune-related genes (NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1) and signaling pathways (CD8+ T cell receptor, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, RAGE signaling) enriched in ICI-associated myocarditis samples compared to controls. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and highlighted cell lysis and proinflammatory pathways as characteristic biological enrichments. These findings provide a detailed map of the host immune response landscape in ICI-associated myocarditis, specifically emphasizing cytotoxic lymphocyte activation and inflammatory signaling cascades that could theoretically serve as downstream effectors if triggered by microbial antigens.\\\", \\\"This study utilized bioinformatics analysis on datasets GSE180045 and GSE4172 to characterize the molecular landscape of ICI-associated myocarditis (ICI-MC). The authors identified 32 immune-related differentially expressed genes (IR-DEGs) and highlighted hub genes including KLRB1, NKG7, and GZMH. Functional enrichment analyses indicated that the pathophysiology involves CD8+ T cell receptor signaling, natural killer cell-mediated cytotoxicity, cell lysis, and RAGE signaling. These findings delineate the downstream immune effector mechanisms (specifically cytotoxic T cell and NK cell activation) that characterize ICI-MC, providing a potential target profile for any upstream trigger, including microbial factors.\\\", \\\"本综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制框架，特别是“分子模拟”（molecular mimicry）概念。作者引用了 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该材料详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递（HLA 类分子向 CD4+ T 细胞呈递外源性肽段）在打破免疫耐受中的核心作用，以及微生物抗原如何通过交叉反应激活针对心脏自身抗原的免疫应答。这为理解肠道菌群（包括潜在的 Prevotella spp.）如何通过抗原模拟激活特定 T 细胞亚群提供了理论模型和机制参考。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The analysis relied on bioinformatics methods using the GSE180045 and GSE4172 datasets without explicit wet-lab validation of causal function reported in the abstract. The study design is retrospective and computational, focusing on transcriptomic differences between ICI patients with and without myocarditis. The authors noted drug predictions (e.g., acetohydroxamic-acid) via cMAP database but did not incorporate microbiome data or stratify patients by microbial composition such as Prevotella spp. abundance.\\\", \\\"The study design is a bioinformatics-based screening and validation approach rather than experimental validation of microbial causality. The authors constructed a ceRNA network and predicted potential target drugs, noting acetohydroxamic acid as a compound requiring caution during ICI treatment. The analysis distinguishes ICI-MC from other immune adverse events based on gene expression profiles. The results are derived from public transcriptomic datasets, and the authors note the findings are predictive or hypothesis-generating rather than causal proof.\\\", \\\"文中总结了 HLA 类 I 和类 II 分子在心肌炎中的不同功能（类 I 呈递病毒肽给 CD8+ T 细胞，类 II 呈递外源肽给 CD4+ T 细胞），并列出了与心肌炎或扩张型心肌病（DCM）相关的具体 HLA 等位基因（如 HLA-DR4, HLA-B27, HLA-DR15 等）。此外，文章提出了心肌炎的三相模型（触发、免疫反应、慢性炎症），并指出 HLA 多态性影响胸腺阴性选择和 T 细胞克隆扩增，这些背景信息有助于构建宿主遗传与环境互作的整体病理生理图景。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于下游信号通路的直接证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析明确了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主效应机制，发现 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 是关键枢纽基因，富集通路包括 CD8+ T 细胞受体信号、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路；但这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法建立微生物与这些通路的因果联系。P0597 提供了“分子模拟”理论框架，指出共生细菌（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides）可通过产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位相似的肽段，经 HLA 限制性抗原呈递激活自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，但该综述未涉及 Prevotella 的具体抗原或代谢物证据。P0261 仅报道了在接受抗 PD-(L)1 或联合治疗的患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263 等分类群与最佳放射学疗效存在关联，属于疗效预测标志物，而非心肌炎发病机制的研究。综上，目前缺乏将 Prevotella 特异性成分与 ICI-MC 中观察到的 CD8+/NK 细胞毒性或 RAGE 通路激活直接连接的实验性或临床验证数据。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。P0595 和 P0596 通过生物信息学分析确定了 ICI 相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的关键宿主免疫效应基因（如 NKG7, GZMH, KLRB1）及通路（CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性、RAGE 信号），但明确指出这些研究未包含微生物组数据，无法验证微生物触发假说。P0261 在人类临床数据中观察到特定菌群（包括 Prevotella OTU264/OTU261/OTU263）与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的相关性，但未涉及心肌炎机制或特异性抗原/代谢物。P0319 综述表格指出 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，但这主要关联于炎症缓解而非心肌炎的特异性 T 细胞激活机制。P0597 提供的理论框架（分子模拟）以拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）为例，未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性机制。因此，Prevotella 是否通过特定抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群并导致心肌炎的因果链条，在当前材料中仍为未解之谜。\\n\\n[\\\"该综述阐述了微生物组通过分子模拟（molecular mimicry）诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用机制。文中指出，共生细菌（引用 Gil-Cruz 等人的研究，具体为拟杆菌属 Bacteroides species）可产生与心脏肌球蛋白表位结构相似的肽段模拟物，在肠道内启动自体反应性 CD4+ T 细胞，进而导致心肌炎。该研究还提到抗生素治疗可阻断这一过程，证实了微生物组衍生抗原模拟在疾病启动中的因果作用。此外，文中详细描述了 HLA 限制性抗原呈递如何决定特定 T 细胞亚群（CD4+ 或 CD8+）的激活，以及下游的细胞因子放大和免疫细胞浸润机制，为理解微生物 - 宿主互作提供了理论框架。\\\", \\\"This study identifies a specific molecular mimicry mechanism where Bacillus infantis (strain NRRL B-14911) induces autoimmune myocarditis. The authors found that an epitope (BAC 25-40) from the bacterial allantoate amidohydrolase (AAH) protein shares sequence homology with cardiac myosin heavy chain alpha (Myhc-α 334-352). Active immunization with this epitope induced myocarditis in A/J mice by generating cardiac-reactive T cells. The study provides genomic evidence of virulence factors and confirms the conservation of this mimicry epitope. This serves as a concrete example of a bacterium inducing myocarditis via antigen-specific T cell cross-reactivity, which parallels the type of mechanism (antigen/metabolite -> T cell subset) sought in the gap question, albeit for a different bacterial species.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"文中提供了 HLA I 类和 II 类分子在心肌炎中的功能对比，包括抗原呈递对象（CD8+ vs CD4+ T 细胞）、表达细胞类型及在自身免疫中的具体角色。还涉及病毒持续感染与自身免疫的复杂关系，以及抗肌球蛋白自身抗体与β1-肾上腺素能受体的交叉反应机制。这些内容虽不直接针对 Prevotella，但构成了心肌炎免疫病理的基础背景。\\\", \\\"The authors performed complete genome sequencing using PacBio SMRT technology, phylogenetic analysis of 16S rRNA and ITS regions, and phenotypic microarray analysis to classify the bacterium as Bacillus infantis. They identified 623 potential virulence factors, including adhesins, invasins, and transporters. The study also notes the presence of unique methyltransferases and insertion sequence elements. These details support the characterization of the bacterium but are less directly relevant to the specific signaling pathway question regarding Prevotella.\\\"]\\n\\n当前提供的材料未能回答关于 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制及其在 FMT-LUMINate 研究后的后续解析进展。现有文献主要聚焦于以下两个与目标问题不直接匹配的方向：一是针对其他菌属（如 Bacillus infantis 或 Bacteroides）的分子模拟机制，证实了细菌抗原（如 AAH 蛋白表位）通过与心脏肌球蛋白同源性激活 CD4+ T 细胞导致心肌炎的通用原理，但这并非 Prevotella 的特异性证据；二是基于生物信息学分析的免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）宿主下游效应机制，识别出 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体和 RAGE 信号通路作为组织损伤的共同终末路径，但明确声明这些分析未纳入微生物组数据，无法建立特定微生物（如 Prevotella）与这些通路的因果联系。因此，Prevotella 特异性抗原/代谢物身份、其激活的特定 T 细胞亚群细节，以及 FMT-LUMINate 研究后是否有独立实验验证其下游信号通路，在当前材料中均处于未解状态。\\n\\n现有材料未能解析 Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制，也未提供 FMT-LUMINate 研究后续关于其下游信号通路的实验证据。材料中关于 Prevotella 的信息主要局限于其与癌症免疫治疗疗效的相关性：P0261 指出在食管癌、胃癌和结直肠癌患者中，Prevotella OTU264/OTU263 等物种与最佳放射学反应（RECIST v1.1）相关；P0319 的表格显示 Prevotella spp. 产生的丙酸（Propionate）可抑制巨噬细胞 M1 极化，从而减轻炎症但可能抑制抗肿瘤免疫，这一代谢机制并未被证实与心肌炎发病有关。针对心肌炎机制，P0601 详细描述了 Bacillus infantis 通过分子模拟（BAC 25-40 表位与心脏肌球蛋白重链 α 同源性）激活心脏反应性 T 细胞的特异性路径，但这属于不同菌属的机制，不能外推至 Prevotella。P0595 和 P0596 阐明了免疫检查点抑制剂相关心肌炎（ICI-MC）的宿主下游效应机制，包括 NKG7、GZMH 和 KLRB1 等关键基因上调，以及 CD8+ T 细胞受体、NK 细胞介导的细胞毒性和 RAGE 信号通路的富集，但这些研究均为生物信息学分析，未涉及微生物组数据，因此无法建立 Prevotella 与这些特定信号通路之间的因果联系。P0597 综述提供了微生物组诱导自身免疫性心肌炎的通用框架（如拟杆菌属 Bacteroides 的分子模拟），但未涵盖 Prevotella 的特异性抗原或代谢物证据。综上，Prevotella 是否通过类似分子模拟或特定代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群进而触发上述 ICI-MC 信号通路，目前仍缺乏直接验证。\\n\\n[\\\"This study provides a mechanistic framework for how gut microbiota can trigger autoimmune myocarditis, specifically citing *Bacteroides thetaiotaomicron* where bacterial beta-galactosidase shares sequence homology with cardiac MyHC-α, inducing Th17 polarization. It also details a downstream signaling pathway in myocarditis involving Tenascin-C (TN-C) activating dendritic cells via TLR4 to produce IL-6, IL-1β, and GM-CSF, driving Th17 differentiation.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"General triggers of myocarditis including viruses (CVB3, SARS-CoV-2) and immune checkpoint inhibitors; description of central and peripheral immune tolerance mechanisms; TN-C as a biomarker for disease activity and prognosis.\\\"]\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"专门针对 Prevotella spp. 在心肌炎中的功能验证研究；FMT-LUMINate 研究团队发表的后续出版物，特别是那些旨在解析 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体抗原表位、代谢产物或其与 CD8+/CD4+ T 细胞交叉反应性的实验数据。\"\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"The supplied text does not mention *Prevotella spp.*, the FMT-LUMINate study, or any specific antigens, metabolites, or downstream signaling pathways associated with *Prevotella*-induced myocarditis. The specific molecular mechanism requested in the gap question remains unidentified in this material.\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0601\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"title\": \"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\n              \"year\": \"2016\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"title\": \"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\n              \"title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0486\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"daf9a1dede2bf1241ba0b187914be958d46b79fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Targeting Microbiome Metabolites: Reshaping Immunotherapy and Clinical Management Strategies for Colorectal Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/imm3.70030\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"c59738fb3db453360d9f86e97ad338176abe8eb6\",\n              \"title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1675677\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cbbd16613d73a6baa4dff169701c792f0d38e1e2\",\n              \"title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2025.1570233\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0319\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"896aa96e6dbaae9b8dbaa7d183f459500ad70834\",\n              \"title\": \"Interplay between Gut Microbiome, Metabolites, and Tumor Immunity: Mechanisms and Clinical Translation\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.53941/hm.2026.100010\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"6f9060daa22a7c9efcd4a92919035c5e5c24367a\",\n              \"title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n              \"year\": \"2022\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-21-1129\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"167d738780c05d96b68041fb0211da97bb53b857\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 4136727: The role of immune mechanism in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor-Associated Myocarditis: seeking key genes\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1161/circ.150.suppl_1.4136727\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"38f13e3a33ed5233b0a792fdb8143168a4264099\",\n              \"title\": \"Key immune related genes and potential therapeutic targets in immune checkpoint inhibitor associated myocarditis: a new fing\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/eurheartj/ehaf784.4157\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:287796055\",\n              \"title\": \"Human Leukocyte Antigen Determinants in Myocarditis and Dilated Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1007/s11897-026-00761-0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0601\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:9951952\",\n              \"title\": \"Whole genomic sequence analysis of Bacillus infantis: defining the genetic blueprint of strain NRRL B-14911, an emerging cardiopathogenic microbe\",\n              \"year\": \"2016\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12864-016-2900-2\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:267380691\",\n              \"title\": \"Potential clinical implications of molecular mimicry‐induced autoimmunity\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"unresolved_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0604\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:231980805\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:231980805\",\n              \"title\": \"Immunomodulatory Role of Tenascin-C in Myocarditis and Inflammatory Cardiomyopathy\",\n              \"year\": \"2021\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2021.624703\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"chapter_ids\": [],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"need_id\": \"N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\",\n          \"question\": \"是否有针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究，以验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题？\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"mechanism\",\n          \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"提供的材料中未包含针对非结肠炎类 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有证据主要聚焦于免疫相关结肠炎（ir-colitis）或整体 irAE 分级与临床预后的关联。具体而言，P0284 对黑色素瘤和 NSCLC 患者进行了分析，其中 P0284 的摘要部分明确提到收集了 32 名发生 irAE 的患者粪便样本，并特别指出在培养组学分析中，21 名（66%）患者发生了 ir-colitis，11 名（34%）未发生；其机制验证部分也仅涉及 ir-colitis 的小鼠模型（FMT 实验）。P0017 同样仅关注“immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis”，比较了 8 例结肠炎性 irAE 和 24 例非结肠炎性 irAE 患者的微生物组差异，样本量较小且未扩展至其他器官特异性 irAEs。P0462 虽然探讨了长期生存和 irAEs 的整体关联及分子模拟机制，但未提供针对非结肠炎特定类型 irAEs 的大规模独立验证数据。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模微生物组证据在当前材料中缺失，无法直接解决样本量小或证据不足的问题。\\n\\n现有材料未提供针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究证据，无法证实 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题已得到解决。相反，材料显示目前的研究主要集中在结肠炎型 irAEs 或整体 irAEs 的发生上。例如，P0284 仅分析了 ir-colitis 患者的微生物特征；P0017 的摘要也明确限定于探讨肠道微生物组与免疫检查点抑制剂相关结肠炎的关系。虽然 P0197 提到了黑色素瘤患者中出现的心肌炎案例，但将其归因于特定供体菌群（Prevotella copri），这属于个案观察而非大规模验证研究。此外，P0067 指出不同器官的 irAEs 可能涉及不同的机制，且目前缺乏针对非结肠炎 irAEs 的大规模数据支持。因此，关于非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组机制仍缺乏大规模研究的直接证据。\\n\\n[\\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis. The authors report that while specific microbial signatures (e.g., Flexispira, Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides) and mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) have been identified, current research 'remains in its infancy.' The study explicitly states that therapeutic applications and mechanistic links are currently supported only by preclinical animal studies or small-scale clinical correlations, with 'clinical validation still pending' and a 'considerable distance between research and clinical practice.' It confirms that large-scale rigorously designed studies are lacking.\\\", \\\"The authors state that emerging evidence highlights the gut microbiota as a critical regulator potentially influencing the development and progression of ICI-associated cardiovascular toxicities, including severe conditions such as myocarditis. This study systematically analyzes the incidence, pathophysiological mechanisms, diagnostic criteria, and prognosis of major cardiovascular toxicities linked to ICIs in the context of microbiome interplay.\\\", \\\"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The review details specific mechanistic hypotheses such as the release of mimic peptides triggering autoimmune responses against the heart and the suppression of anti-inflammatory Tregs by dysbiosis. It also notes confounding factors like concomitant use of proton pump inhibitors or statins which may alter microbiota composition and irAE risk. Additionally, it highlights the controversy around antibiotic use, noting that while antibiotics reduced myocardial injury in mouse models, retrospective human studies associate broad-spectrum antibiotics with shortened survival and increased tumor progression risk during ICI therapy.\\\", \\\"The review explores immunomodulatory functions of the gut microbiome that may underlie these adverse events, emphasizing microbiota-mediated systemic immune dysregulation and cardiovascular-specific toxicity pathways. It also discusses future research directions and the clinical implications of integrating gut microbiota modulation into the management of ICI-associated cardiovascular complications.\\\", \\\"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究目前尚不存在。P0600 的研究虽然纳入了发生 irAEs 的患者，但明确将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并为一组进行分析，未对特定器官毒性进行验证；其数据中仅包含 3 例心肌炎病例，作者指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，针对不同类型 irAE 的亚组分析缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0284 的研究同样聚焦于结肠炎（ir-colitis），在黑色素瘤队列中仅有 14 例 ir-colitis 患者，且未涉及心肌炎或神经毒性的独立分析。尽管 P0284 通过宏基因组和培养组学证实了 ir-colitis 患者存在α多样性降低和特定菌群富集，但这些发现仅限于结肠炎表型。因此，当前证据不足以解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的关于非结肠炎 irAEs 样本量小或证据不足的问题，缺乏针对这些罕见非结肠炎表型的特异性微生物组机制验证。\\nP0600 (32名irAE患者队列) / 心肌炎病例数 / 基线微生物组分析时点：myocarditis: 3例\\nP0284 (黑色素瘤队列, n=45) / ir-colitis病例数 / ICI治疗前基线样本：ir-colitis: 14例\\nP0284 (培养组学亚组, n=32) / ir-colitis检出菌种中位数 / 基线或急性期粪便样本：ir-colitis group: 12 species；no-ir-colitis group: 22 species\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模独立微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏。多项研究指出，由于特定类型 irAEs 发生率较低或样本量有限，亚组分析往往缺乏统计效力或无法进行。例如，P0600 的研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎患者，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组可能缺乏统计效力或不可行。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的整体微生物组差异，但未对心肌炎等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的关联分析。此外，P0197 的摘要提到在黑色素瘤 FMT 试验中，13 名出现 >3 级 irAE 的患者中有 3 例（15%）发生心肌炎，并观察到供体 D5 的粪菌移植与心肌炎相关，但这属于小样本观察性数据，而非大规模验证性研究。其他研究如 P0011 虽然分析了皮肤、血液、内分泌和肝脏毒性，但并未提供针对心肌炎或神经毒性的大规模独立队列数据。因此，目前仍缺乏能够充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题的大规模特异性研究。\\n\\n[\\\"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\\\", \\\"This study provides preclinical mechanistic evidence linking gut microbiota to PD-1 inhibitor-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. The authors established a melanoma mouse model (n=6 per group) showing that PD-1 inhibition induced myocarditis, reduced cardiac regulatory T cells (Tregs), and altered gut microbiota composition. Specific taxa (e.g., Ruminococcaceae, Flexispira) were correlated with cardiac injury markers (CK-MB, cTn-I) and Treg-related gene expression (FOXP3, IL-10). Fecal microbiota removal (antibiotic treatment) attenuated myocarditis and restored Treg levels without compromising antitumor efficacy in this model. These findings support the biological plausibility of a microbiome-immune axis in non-colitis irAEs.\\\", \\\"该综述确认了肠道微生物群被视为 ICI 相关心血管不良事件（包括心肌炎）的关键调节者，并提出了微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调和心血管特异性毒性通路作为潜在机制。作者指出该领域证据正在涌现（Emerging evidence），并强调需要整合微生物群调节管理，这间接支持了当前可能缺乏成熟大规模验证研究的现状。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\\\", \\\"The introduction and discussion cite general background on the association between gut dysbiosis and cardiovascular or autoimmune diseases, and the role of Tregs in maintaining immune homeostasis. The methods detail the 16S rRNA sequencing protocol and the antibiotic cocktail used for microbiota depletion, which may inform future experimental designs. The study also notes limitations such as the small number of experimental animals and the resolution limits of 16S sequencing.\\\", \\\"综述提供了 ICI 相关心血管毒性的发病率、病理生理机制、诊断标准和预后的系统分析框架，旨在为基础和临床研究提供理论基础。材料明确区分了安全性事件（如心肌炎）与治疗效果，但指出免疫调节功能可能 underlying 这些不良事件。\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料表明，针对非结肠炎免疫相关不良反应（irAEs，如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究目前仍然缺乏。具体而言：1. P0600 研究纳入了32名发生irAEs的患者，其中包含3例心肌炎，但作者明确指出由于样本量小且irAE发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型irAE患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行，因此未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。2. P0462 研究是一个前瞻性队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），其严重irAE组仅包含13例患者，其中包括2例心血管毒性和1例肌肉毒性，同样未针对特定非结肠炎亚型进行大规模独立分析，且作者承认样本量有限。3. P0602 提供的是临床前小鼠模型证据（每组n=6），虽然证实了肠道菌群与PD-1抑制剂诱导的心肌炎之间的因果机制（通过调节心脏调节性T细胞），但这属于小规模动物实验，并非人类临床队列的大规模关联研究。综上，现有文献多将非结肠炎irAEs合并分析或因病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，未能充分验证P0051和P0530中提到的证据不足问题。\\n\\n现有证据表明，针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究仍然缺乏，未能充分验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题。具体而言：\\n\\n1. **人类队列研究的局限性**：多项已发表的人类研究（如 P0600, P0462, P0049）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少而无法得出具有统计效力的结论。例如，P0600 纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者，其中仅包含 3 例心肌炎，作者明确指出由于样本量小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行。P0462 的严重 irAE 组（n=13）中包含多种类型的 irAEs（包括 2 例心血管毒性），但未对特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析，且作者承认样本量相对较小。\\n\\n2. **动物模型的补充与局限**：虽然有小规模动物实验（如 P0602，每组 n=6）提供了机制性证据，显示 PD-1 抑制诱导的小鼠心肌炎与肠道微生物群改变及调节性 T 细胞（Tregs）减少有关，并通过粪菌移植（FMT）验证了因果作用，但这些研究规模小，属于临床前模型，不能替代大规模人类队列研究来验证临床流行病学证据。\\n\\n3. **综述与背景研究的共识**：相关综述（如 P0603）指出，尽管有理论框架支持微生物群介导的系统性免疫失调可能导致心肌炎等非结肠炎 irAEs，但该领域的实证证据正在涌现但仍显不足，呼吁未来需要整合更大规模的微生物组数据。\\n\\n综上，目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模、独立分析的微生物组关联研究。现有研究多受限于样本量，无法提供足够的统计效力来明确区分不同器官特异性 irAEs 的微生物组特征。\\n\\n[\\\"This prospective cohort study (Verheijden et al., 2025) analyzed 497 stool samples from 195 cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) to assess gut microbiome associations with severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The study included various irAE types listed in Table 1, such as myocarditis (n=2 total), meningitis (n=2 total), pneumonitis (n=4 total), and colitis (n=6 total), but aggregated them into a single 'severe irAE' endpoint for analysis due to low incidence of individual types. Key findings indicated that a higher baseline relative abundance of a prespecified pathobiont group and a stronger decrease in Ruminococcaceae during treatment were associated with developing severe irAEs. At irAE onset, Ruminococcaceae and specific species (R. bromii, R. callidus) were significantly lower, while Haemophilus parainfluenzae was higher compared to other time points. The authors explicitly note in Section 3.6 that only 17 patients provided samples at severe irAE onset, with diverse irAE types (8 colitis, 3 pancreatitis/diabetes, 2 meningitis, 4 others), limiting subtype-specific analysis.\\\", \\\"This narrative review synthesizes existing preclinical and clinical evidence regarding the association between gut microbiota and ICI-associated myocarditis, a non-colitis irAE. It identifies specific microbial signatures linked to severe irAEs, such as higher abundance of pathobionts, decreased Ruminococcaceae, and dynamic changes in Bacteroides (citing Verheijden et al., 2025; Zeng et al., 2023). The authors propose mechanistic hypotheses including molecular mimicry between microbial epitopes and cardiac tissues, and microbiota-mediated suppression of regulatory T cells (Tregs). Crucially, the text explicitly states that current research on this relationship remains in its infancy, mechanisms are incompletely elucidated, and therapeutic applications (e.g., antibiotics) are supported only by preclinical evidence with clinical validation pending. This directly corroborates the gap's premise regarding insufficient evidence and small sample sizes in non-colitis irAE microbiome studies.\\\", \\\"该研究在黑色素瘤小鼠模型中（每组 n=6）证实了 PD-1 抑制剂治疗会改变肠道菌群组成（如 Ruminococcaceae、Flexispira 等富集），并与心肌炎严重程度及心脏调节性 T 细胞（Treg）减少显著相关。研究通过粪便微生物清除实验（FMR）表明，抗生素干预可减轻 PD-1 抑制剂诱导的心肌炎，同时保持抗肿瘤效果，提示肠道菌群通过调节 Treg 功能参与非结肠炎 irAE（心肌炎）的发病机制。\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study employed a robust methodological framework useful for review methodology discussions, including longitudinal sampling (baseline, during treatment, at irAE onset, post-immunosuppression), both 16S rRNA and metagenomic shotgun sequencing, and multiple differential abundance tools (ANCOM-BC, LinDA, MaAsLin2, ALDEx2) to ensure consistency. The authors discuss limitations regarding sample size for specific taxa and the need for correction for multiple testing, which resulted in some baseline associations (e.g., pathobionts) losing significance after correction.\\\", \\\"The review discusses confounding factors such as concomitant medications (proton pump inhibitors, statins) that may modulate the gut microbiota and influence irAE risk, suggesting these need stratified analysis in future research. It also notes the heterogeneity of ICI-associated myocarditis incidence across different cancer types, warranting further investigation. The text mentions specific preclinical interventions, such as fecal microbiota removal using antibiotic cocktails in mice, which reduced myocardial injury, but emphasizes these findings lack human clinical validation.\\\", \\\"作者明确指出该研究受限于实验动物数量有限（n=6），结论需更大样本量研究进一步确认；且 16S rRNA 测序无法精确到菌种水平，缺乏单一菌群或代谢物的直接因果验证。此外，文中引用了肠道菌群失调与心血管及自身免疫疾病关联的既往背景，为综述提供理论依据。\\\"]\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"需要检索是否有近期发表的、专门针对非结肠炎 irAEs（特别是心肌炎、神经毒性等罕见类型）的大规模微生物组关联研究（human cohort studies）。重点寻找样本量足以支持亚组分析或独立分析的研究，以及多中心联合队列或 Meta 分析结果。\"\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"The gap question asks for large-scale microbiome association studies specifically targeting non-colitis irAEs (e.g., myocarditis, neurotoxicity) to verify evidence insufficiency. This study does not fulfill that requirement because it aggregates all severe irAEs into one group; the specific counts for non-colitis irAEs like myocarditis (n=2) and meningitis (n=2) are too small for independent large-scale association analysis. Thus, the existence of a dedicated large-scale study for non-colitis irAE microbiome signatures remains unconfirmed by this material.\",\n          \"allowed_use\": [\n            \"background_context\",\n            \"explicit_objectives\",\n            \"explicit_method_summaries\",\n            \"explicit_reported_findings\",\n            \"explicit_leads\"\n          ],\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0197\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"55e5f184350846573ce6b2d40fdcbd15f2602f90\",\n              \"title\": \"Abstract 2210: Microbiome profiling reveals that fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) modulates response and toxicity when combined with immunotherapy in patients with lung cancer and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate NCT04951583)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2025-2210\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n              \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"08d60ce7ff453c5ae2b4c3a47581b79e02b2b5a0\",\n              \"title\": \"DOP47 Gut microbiome contributes to the development of immune checkpoint inhibitor-related colitis\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1093/ecco-jcc/jjac190.0087\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0011\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"042544f408b07e2d51c57f40f4df614d0c0960a7\",\n              \"title\": \"Correlation of the gut microbiome and immune-related adverse events in gastrointestinal cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2023.1099063\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0067\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"19590ba8c3221ee742d0e85768b8d22521dcbb86\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota diversity is prognostic and associated with benefit from chemo‐immunotherapy in metastatic triple‐negative breast cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1002/1878-0261.13760\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0314\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"873fa8f3f156b691e03d1431a71f79cf1fa30374\",\n              \"title\": \"The Association of the Microbiome with Melanoma Tumor Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Treatment and Immune-Related Adverse Events (NCT05102773)\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1101/2025.01.30.25321413\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"1607ffdb79bd5dbb1f94932e27410c55f0aa8290\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0409\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"b32c1543240c066ebf3d3e797ec04127cb831f40\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota–Tumor Microenvironment Interactions: Mechanisms and Clinical Implications for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Efficacy in Cancer\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.2147/cmar.s405590\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"26d31bd79ed61eee0d3e8ed343dc30afddacf59c\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0599\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n              \"year\": \"2023\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n              \"year\": \"2024\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:289583785\",\n              \"title\": \"Cardiovascular Adverse Events Associated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors from the Perspective of Gut Microecology: Potential Roles and Research Advances of the Gut Microbiota.\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1097/fjc.0000000000001842\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0603\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"conflicting_identity\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0049\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:275340168\",\n              \"title\": \"Gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity.\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ejca.2025.115221\",\n              \"original_source_handle\": \"P0605\",\n              \"identity_status\": \"remapped\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:285883374\",\n              \"title\": \"The gut microbiota: an emerging therapeutic target for ICI-associated myocarditis\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fcimb.2026.1752485\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0602\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"canonical_paper_id\": \"CorpusId:279792240\",\n              \"title\": \"Abnormal gut microbiota may cause PD-1 inhibitor-related cardiotoxicity via suppressing regulatory T cells\",\n              \"year\": \"2025\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41598-025-05635-4\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"chapter_ids\": [],\n          \"unit_key\": \"\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"local_editable_task_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n        \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n        \"Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\",\n        \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n        \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n        \"Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\",\n        \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n        \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n        \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n        \"Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\",\n        \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n        \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n        \"Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n      ],\n      \"fullbody_task_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U1::Ch6_U1_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U2::Ch6_U2_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_P03\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U3::Ch6_U3_T01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P01\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P02\",\n        \"Ch6::Ch6_U4::Ch6_U4_P03\"\n      ],\n      \"source_pool_reference\": \"sources\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"As a narrative review, this paper does not employ a systematic search protocol described in the text. Instead, it synthesizes findings from a broad range of sources including: 1) Historical timeline analysis of key advancements; 2) Summary of clinical trial data (Tables 1-5) linking specific microbial taxa to ICI/ACT outcomes; 3) Mechanistic discussion based on preclinical models (mouse studies) and human cohort analyses regarding immune cell activation, metabolite pathways (SCFAs, bile acids, etc.), and intratumoral interactions; 4) Evaluation of intervention strategies (antibiotics, FMT, probiotics, diet, engineered microbes) by summarizing results from ongoing and completed clinical trials.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides a structured synthesis of clinical and preclinical evidence linking specific gut microbial taxa to ICI and ACT outcomes across multiple cancer types. It categorizes mechanisms into innate/adaptive immunity modulation, metabolite effects, and intratumoral interactions. It also catalogs numerous ongoing clinical trials for FMT, probiotics, and dietary interventions.\",\n            \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks a systematic methodology for study selection, potentially introducing selection bias. Many findings are derived from small-scale clinical studies or animal models, limiting generalizability. The field faces significant heterogeneity in sequencing methods, sample handling, and lack of standardized protocols, making cross-study comparisons difficult. Causal relationships between specific microbes and clinical outcomes are often correlational rather than proven causal.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI therapy (anti-PD-1/PD-L1/CTLA-4)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Specific gut microbial compositions correlate with ICI response. Beneficial taxa include Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia muciniphila, Ruminococcaceae, and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, which are associated with improved survival and tumor regression in melanoma, NSCLC, and RCC. Conversely, antibiotic use generally reduces ICI efficacy.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ACT therapy (CAR-T, TCR-T)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Gut microbiota influences ACT efficacy and toxicity. Certain microbes (e.g., Ruminococcus, Bacteroides) are linked to CAR-T efficacy, while others may predict neurotoxicity or cytokine release syndrome (CRS). Microbial metabolites like SCFAs can enhance CD8+ T cell cytotoxicity.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Mechanisms of Immune Modulation\",\n            \"finding\": \"Microbiota modulate immunity via direct interaction with dendritic cells and macrophages (PRR activation), metabolite signaling (SCFAs, bile acids, tryptophan metabolites influencing T cell differentiation), and molecular mimicry (cross-reactive T cells). Intratumoral microbiota can remodel the TME, promoting TLS formation or inducing immunosuppression.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Intervention Strategies\",\n            \"finding\": \"FMT from ICI responders can overcome resistance in refractory melanoma patients. Probiotics (e.g., Clostridium butyricum CBM588) and dietary interventions (high-fiber, ketogenic) show promise in enhancing ICI response and reducing toxicity, though clinical evidence is still emerging.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"Despite the success of immunotherapies like ICIs and ACTs, patient responses vary widely due to primary or acquired resistance and adverse events. This review aims to elucidate the role of the gut microbiota in shaping these outcomes, identify potential biomarkers for predicting response, and explore microbiota-based strategies to enhance efficacy and mitigate toxicity.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiota and its influence on cancer immunotherapy, specifically immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) and adoptive cell therapies (ACTs). It covers clinical correlations, preclinical mechanisms, intratumoral microbiota, and intervention strategies across various solid tumors and hematologic malignancies.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This paper provides a comprehensive overview of how the gut microbiome modulates the efficacy and toxicity of cancer immunotherapies. It traces the historical evolution from early animal studies to recent clinical trials, detailing specific microbial signatures associated with response or resistance to ICIs and ACTs. The authors synthesize mechanistic insights involving innate and adaptive immune modulation, metabolite production, and tumor microenvironment remodeling. Furthermore, it evaluates therapeutic interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, dietary modifications, and engineered bacteria, while highlighting challenges in standardization and clinical translation.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This review serves as a foundational resource for mapping the relationship between gut microbiome composition and ICI efficacy in solid tumors. It provides specific microbial markers (taxa) associated with response/resistance, details mechanistic pathways (metabolites, immune cell crosstalk), and outlines current intervention strategies (FMT, probiotics, diet). It is particularly useful for identifying candidate biomarkers and understanding the biological plausibility of microbiome-mediated modulation, while also highlighting the methodological challenges and variability that complicate definitive conclusions.\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"Associations are largely correlative from retrospective or small prospective cohorts. Specificity varies by cancer type and ICI agent. Lack of standardized detection methods limits direct comparison. Does not establish causality.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific gut microbial taxa associated with ICI response or resistance in solid tumors. For example, Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, and Ruminococcaceae are linked to better outcomes in melanoma and NSCLC, while certain Proteobacteria or high abundance of Bacteroides intestinalis may correlate with resistance or toxicity. It also notes that beneficial taxa vary by ICI type (anti-PD-1 vs. anti-CTLA-4) and cancer type.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to list candidate microbial biomarkers for predicting ICI efficacy in solid tumors. Helps explain inter-patient variability in treatment response.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are primarily demonstrated in mouse models (preclinical). Human validation is often indirect or observational. Some mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry) are proposed but require further confirmation in humans. Effects can be bidirectional (promoting or suppressing immunity depending on context).\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Details mechanisms by which gut microbiota modulate ICI efficacy: 1) Direct immune modulation via PRR activation (TLR/NLR) leading to DC maturation and T-cell activation; 2) Metabolite-mediated regulation (SCFAs inhibiting HDAC, bile acids affecting Th17/Treg balance, tryptophan metabolites via AhR); 3) Molecular mimicry where bacterial antigens cross-react with tumor antigens; 4) Remodeling of the tumor microenvironment (TME) through intratumoral bacteria or systemic metabolites influencing tertiary lymphoid structures (TLS).\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic explanations for how the microbiome influences ICI response. Supports the biological rationale for microbiome-targeted interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Contextual background on the evolution of microbiome-immunotherapy research\",\n            \"material\": \"Historical perspective section tracing discoveries from 2007 to 2025, highlighting the shift from correlation to mechanistic understanding and clinical trials.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To provide a timeline of key advancements and justify the current interest in microbiome modulation as a critical factor in immunotherapy success.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Discussion of intervention strategies beyond just biomarkers\",\n            \"material\": \"Sections on FMT, probiotics, antibiotics, diet, and engineered microbes, including tables of clinical trials.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To illustrate potential therapeutic avenues for overcoming ICI resistance and managing toxicity, providing examples of how microbiome modulation is being translated into clinical practice.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Challenges and limitations in the field\",\n            \"material\": \"Section on 'Challenges and future directions' discussing technical variability, donor effects in FMT, host genetics, and lack of standardization.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To highlight methodological hurdles and confounding factors that must be considered when interpreting microbiome-ICI associations, explaining why consistent biomarkers are hard to identify.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"The review covers both gut and intratumoral microbiota; ensure distinction is maintained when applying findings to 'gut microbiome' specific facets.\",\n          \"Findings on specific bacterial taxa are highly dependent on the cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. NSCLC) and the specific ICI agent (anti-PD-1 vs. anti-CTLA-4); avoid over-generalizing across all solid tumors.\",\n          \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from murine models; caution is needed when extrapolating to human physiology without explicit human validation mentioned in the text.\",\n          \"Clinical trial data cited are often from early-phase (I/II) or small cohorts; results should not be interpreted as definitive proof of efficacy for interventions like FMT or probiotics.\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"gut microbiota composition and diversity\",\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n          \"solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, HCC, CRC)\",\n          \"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"probiotics and prebiotics\",\n          \"dietary interventions (high-fiber, ketogenic)\",\n          \"microbial metabolites (SCFAs, bile acids, tryptophan metabolites)\",\n          \"intratumoral microbiota\",\n          \"predictive biomarkers for ICI response\",\n          \"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\\\\92125422c10f28cdb7938d2658870c58\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\\\\92125422c10f28cdb7938d2658870c58\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n            \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于FMT联合ICI治疗实体瘤的关键临床数据，特别是其在克服原发性耐药方面的潜力。更重要的是，它提出了一个区别于传统“有益菌定植”假说的新机制框架：即治疗获益主要源于FMT诱导的基线有害病原体（pathobionts）的清除，进而调节宿主代谢和免疫微环境。此外，它还揭示了供体菌群特征（如Prevotella丰度）与特定ICI方案（双免疫检查点抑制）相互作用下的安全性风险。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中ICI的疗效”，提供具体的临床响应率证据，支持FMT作为增敏策略的有效性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“介导该效应的机制是什么”，提供微生物组重塑的具体分子和免疫学路径，挑战传统的“益生菌定植”主导观点，强调“去致病化”的重要性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于讨论ICI疗效与安全性之间的权衡，以及微生物组在预测和管理irAEs中的作用，提示未来FMT研究中供体筛选的重要性。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"为综述中关于“FMT作用机制的争议”提供反面证据或补充视角，即定植效率可能不是决定疗效的唯一或主要因素。\",\n            \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"背景信息，用于对比不同研究中关于FMT机制的解释（定植vs清除）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"跨研究的一致性证据，支持“有害菌清除”作为FMT疗效通用机制的假设。\",\n            \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为外部验证，增强综述中关于机制结论的可信度。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n          \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n          \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"FMT联合ICI的临床疗效（NSCLC, Melanoma）\",\n          \"FMT介导的微生物组重塑机制（有害菌清除 vs 有益菌定植）\",\n          \"肠道微生物-免疫代谢轴（色氨酸代谢, 喹啉酸, 犬尿氨酸）\",\n          \"ICI相关不良反应（irAEs）的微生物驱动因素\",\n          \"供体选择对治疗安全性和有效性的影响\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material\": {\n        \"_progressive_task_requirements\": {\n          \"knowledge_gaps\": [\n            \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\"\n          ],\n          \"questions\": [\n            {\n              \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n              \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n              \"required_output_ids\": [\n                \"O01\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"required_outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n              \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n              \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"_progressive_task_signature\": \"37c81ea7cb18384d\",\n        \"current_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"fulfilled\": false,\n        \"paper_identity\": {\n          \"canonical_paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n          \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n          \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\"\n        },\n        \"paper_title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"plain_text\": \"\",\n        \"prior_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"required_output_ids\": [\n              \"O01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\",\n        \"required_outputs\": [\n          {\n            \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n            \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n            \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"source_hash\": \"8dd08b84648262841f9d35af692160252692383791e7c7d076ecd654063fb0f3\",\n        \"task_hash\": \"4fcf708140bdb8b00ce198191a4362b1ee8545d9d5569d77e4118fb1833a9f61\"\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material_trimmed\": {\n        \"dropped_keys\": {\n          \"material_ready\": 4,\n          \"paper_id\": 42,\n          \"references\": 413,\n          \"review_id\": 23,\n          \"schema_version\": 46,\n          \"status\": 9,\n          \"task_id\": 34,\n          \"workflow\": 21\n        },\n        \"dropped_chars\": 592,\n        \"note\": \"深读材料里的记账字段与论文自带的参考文献表已省略；科学内容（问句材料/发现/条件）保留。需要时可用 locator 读原文。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"assets\",\n            \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n      \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的IIa期篮子试验设计。纳入标准包括ICI治疗后疾病进展、ECOG评分0-1及可测量病灶。供体需为ICI长期响应者（>12个月响应）。干预措施包括基线后第1周和第5周通过结肠镜进行两次FMT，随后在第14、30、78周可通过灌肠进行最多三次补充FMT。ICI治疗保持不变或重新引入。主要终点评估安全性和ORR（基于iRECIST）。次要终点包括可行性、临床获益率、无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、微生物定植（16S rRNA测序）、免疫反应（质谱流式细胞术分析PBMCs）及生物标志物（血清细胞因子）。统计分析采用描述性统计、Kaplan-Meier生存分析及Cox比例风险模型探索免疫特征与预后的关联，未进行多重检验校正。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"证实了在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，使用ICI响应者供体的FMT是安全和可行的。提供了关于FMT后微生物定植动力学（短暂性）和系统性免疫景观（髓系抑制与T细胞活化）的详细生物标志物数据。\",\n            \"limits\": \"样本量小（n=12），试验因入组缓慢提前终止。单臂设计无法确立因果关系，缺乏对照组。未能实现预期的临床疗效（无ORR），限制了对其机制解释的确定性。结果可能受到快速进展性疾病背景的影响，未能在足够长的时间内观察FMT的潜在延迟效应。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"12名ICI耐药晚期实体瘤患者，接受来自ICI响应者的FMT联合ICI治疗\",\n            \"finding\": \"FMT安全性良好，无严重FMT相关不良事件导致停药，但50%患者出现免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），多数为轻度。客观缓解率（ORR）为0%，中位PFS为1.5个月，中位OS为10.1个月。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析\",\n            \"finding\": \"首次FMT后一周，大多数受体的微生物组向供体方向偏移（定植成功），但这种相似性在后续时间点大多下降，表明定植多为暂时性。仅1名获得临床获益的患者实现了持久的供体-受体微生物相似性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"免疫微环境分析\",\n            \"finding\": \"基线时高度分化的T细胞环境（CD8+效应记忆T细胞和TEMRA）与改善的PFS和OS相关；而髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型预后较差。CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平随时间增加，高水平的CD14+单核细胞与较短的PFS和OS相关。这些免疫特征与预后的关联在使用ICI治疗起始日期重新计算时依然成立，提示其反映的是宿主对免疫治疗的固有反应能力，而非FMT的直接因果效应。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"早期研究表明FMT可能逆转ICI耐药，但其适用性在其他肿瘤类型中尚不明确，且关于患者选择、供体选择及给药方案的问题仍未解决。本研究试图回答：在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，重复FMT是否安全可行，以及是否能通过微生物定植和免疫重塑来恢复ICI的疗效。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"针对晚期实体瘤（黑色素瘤、头颈部鳞癌、肾细胞癌、微卫星不稳定性高胰腺癌）中免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药或进展的患者，评估来自ICI长期响应者的粪菌移植（FMT）联合ICI治疗的安全性和有效性。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究是一项单臂IIa期篮子试验（MITRIC），旨在验证通过FMT调节肠道微生物群能否克服已建立的ICI耐药性。研究纳入了12名在转移性阶段对ICI治疗进展的患者，使用ICI长期响应者作为供体，给予患者最多五次FMT（前两次通过结肠镜，后续通过灌肠），并继续原有ICI治疗。主要终点为FMT相关不良事件和客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示FMT安全性良好，但未能观察到客观肿瘤反应（ORR为0%），仅5名患者达到疾病稳定。尽管缺乏总体疗效证据，研究发现FMT诱导了短暂的微生物定植，且外周血中的免疫细胞特征（如分化T细胞与髓系细胞的平衡）与生存期显著相关，但这些免疫特征似乎更多反映疾病本身状态而非FMT的特异性干预效果。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文提供了关于FMT在ICI耐药实体瘤中应用的阴性疗效结果及详细的转化医学发现。对于综述而言，其核心价值在于反驳了“FMT能普遍逆转ICI耐药”的简单假设，并指出了患者选择（如疾病进展速度、既往免疫状态）和供体匹配的重要性。同时，它提供了关于肠道微生物定植持久性与临床获益之间潜在联系的生物学见解，以及系统性免疫景观（特别是髓系细胞和T细胞亚群）作为预后生物标志物的证据。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于ICI耐药/进展人群，不能外推至一线治疗场景。样本量极小，结果可能存在偶然性，但趋势明确。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT在广泛ICI耐药实体瘤队列中的真实世界疗效数据：ORR为0%，中位PFS仅为1.5个月。这表明在非选择性、快速进展的耐药人群中，FMT联合ICI并非有效的挽救疗法。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于支持综述中关于“FMT疗效具有高度情境依赖性”或“需严格筛选患者群体”的论点。对比其他阳性研究，说明患者基线状态（如疾病负荷、进展速度）对FMT结局的关键影响。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"免疫关联分析为探索性，未校正多重检验，且缺乏对照组，无法证明FMT改变了这些免疫特征从而改善了预后。仅描述了相关性，未证明因果机制。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT干预后系统性免疫景观的变化及其与预后的关联：(1) FMT诱导的微生物定植多为暂时性，仅持久定植者与临床获益相关；(2) 基线高分化T细胞表型预示更好预后，而高髓系细胞（CD14+）和高IL-8水平预示不良预后；(3) 这些免疫特征似乎反映了宿主固有的免疫反应能力，而非FMT直接重塑的结果。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于解释FMT起效的潜在机制（需要持久定植和特定的宿主免疫背景）。提供生物标志物候选项（如CD14+单核细胞、IL-8、T细胞分化状态）以预测哪些患者可能从微生物调节中受益。帮助区分“药物直接效应”与“宿主背景效应”。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提供FMT在临床转化中的实际挑战案例，特别是供体选择和患者异质性问题。\",\n            \"material\": \"研究讨论了使用ICI响应者作为供体的局限性（微生物组成差异大），以及不同研究间供体数量（单供体vs多供体）对结果的潜在影响。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"用于讨论“供体选择标准”对FMT疗效的影响，指出单一供体或多供体混合策略的优劣尚无共识，且供体与受体的匹配度可能是关键因素。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提供关于FMT给药途径和频率的可行性数据。\",\n            \"material\": \"比较了结肠镜给药（前两次）和灌肠给药（后续）的可行性及耐受性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"用于综述中关于“FMT最佳给药方案”的部分，说明多次、重复给药在技术上可行，但在临床实践中受限于患者状况和疾病进展。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的阴性结果主要归因于患者群体的快速进展特性和小样本量，不应将其解读为FMT在所有情况下均无效，而应视为特定情境下的失败尝试。\",\n          \"免疫生物标志物的发现是探索性的，且可能与ICI治疗本身的效应混淆，需谨慎解读其作为FMT特异性机制的作用。\",\n          \"微生物定植的暂时性并不必然意味着临床无效，因为唯一获益患者的持久定植提示了两者间的潜在联系，但这仅是个案观察。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) resistance\",\n          \"solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, pancreatic cancer)\",\n          \"microbiota engraftment kinetics\",\n          \"peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs)\",\n          \"myeloid-derived suppressor cells / CD14+ monocytes\",\n          \"T-cell differentiation phenotypes\",\n          \"serum cytokines (IL-8)\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material\": {\n        \"_progressive_task_requirements\": {\n          \"knowledge_gaps\": [\n            \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\"\n          ],\n          \"questions\": [\n            {\n              \"gap_key\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n              \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n              \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n              \"required_output_ids\": [\n                \"O01\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"required_outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n              \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n              \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"_progressive_task_signature\": \"1826ef4c29abfe31\",\n        \"current_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R19\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R18\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R20\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n              \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n              \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"fulfilled\": false,\n        \"paper_identity\": {\n          \"canonical_paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n          \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n          \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\"\n        },\n        \"paper_title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n        \"plain_text\": \"\",\n        \"prior_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n                \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n              \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n              \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n                \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n              \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n              \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R19\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R18\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R20\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n              \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n              \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"gap_key\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"required_output_ids\": [\n              \"O01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\",\n        \"required_outputs\": [\n          {\n            \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n            \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n            \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"source_hash\": \"163af5f925ccdf303a5e1ea759ee09e197370c5f96ebb2b13c0ffe191f601130\",\n        \"task_hash\": \"d5ed1ee74fa77146cbbbb8902e443d73f4d0b6bf5e2f2fa86fc5fd776eb04965\"\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material_trimmed\": {\n        \"dropped_keys\": {\n          \"material_ready\": 4,\n          \"paper_id\": 42,\n          \"references\": 834,\n          \"review_id\": 23,\n          \"schema_version\": 46,\n          \"status\": 9,\n          \"task_id\": 34,\n          \"workflow\": 21\n        },\n        \"dropped_chars\": 1013,\n        \"note\": \"深读材料里的记账字段与论文自带的参考文献表已省略；科学内容（问句材料/发现/条件）保留。需要时可用 locator 读原文。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Identify and retrieve full-text or registry data for actual Phase III randomized controlled trials of FMT or defined microbial consortia in oncology (e.g., TACITO, though noted as randomized, verify if Phase III; other ongoing/completed Phase III trials like those in melanoma or RCC). If no such trials are found in the literature base, explicitly state that no Phase III RCTs have yet confirmed efficacy, using this Phase IIa negative result to illustrate the current stage of evidence (pre-registration/early-phase focus).\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Identify and retrieve full-text or registry data for actual Phase III randomized controlled trials of FMT or defined microbial consortia in oncology (e.g., TACITO, though noted as randomized, verify if Phase III; other ongoing/completed Phase III trials like those in melanoma or RCC). If no such trials are found in the literature base, explicitly state that no Phase III RCTs have yet confirmed efficacy, using this Phase IIa negative result to illustrate the current stage of evidence (pre-registration/early-phase focus).\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n      \"title\": \"Abstract 3463: Longitudinal microbiome-immune dynamics in melanoma patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy\",\n      \"year\": \"2023\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-3463\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"abstract\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"纵向队列研究设计。收集III期黑色素瘤患者在联合ICI治疗前（基线）和治疗后第6周的配对粪便样本（n=126）和外周血PBMC样本（n=71）。使用16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道微生物组成，使用质谱流式细胞术全面 profiling 循环免疫细胞亚群。比较基线与第6周的微生物和免疫指标变化，并分析其与临床应答状态及irAEs严重程度的关联。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向证据，表明肠道微生物组（特别是拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与ICI治疗期间的免疫细胞动态（特别是Tregs）及临床结局（应答和irAEs）存在关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正）、微生物功能推断细节、以及是否控制了其他混杂因素（如抗生素使用、饮食等）。此外，作为会议摘要，缺乏完整的实验细节和长期随访数据。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI治疗前后对比\",\n            \"finding\": \"治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞（Tem）频率增加（P=0.0096）和调节性T细胞（Tregs）频率减少（P=0.0029）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"根据临床应答分类\",\n            \"finding\": \"Tregs的减少主要在应答者中观察到（P=0.0016），而在非应答者中无显著变化（P=0.9515）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"根据irAEs严重程度分类\",\n            \"finding\": \"发生严重irAEs的患者在第6周时Tregs显著缺乏（P=0.0293），相比无或轻度毒性患者。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与免疫变化的关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"在循环Tregs减少的患者中，Tregs减少的程度与基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）相对丰度呈正相关（P<0.0001）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与临床结局的关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"较高的基线拟杆菌属丰度与更严重的irAEs发展（P=0.0472）及第6周前更高的类固醇使用率（P=0.0345）相关。相反，较高的瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）丰度具有保护作用，且瘤胃球菌科主导的微生物组患者中应答者比例更高。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，但具体机制不明。本研究试图解决：肠道微生物如何与免疫系统相互作用以影响ICI的成功或irAEs的发生？特别是特定细菌类群（如拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与免疫细胞亚群变化及临床结局之间的关联。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"III期黑色素瘤患者，接受新辅助联合抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；涉及澳大利亚和荷兰队列（n=126），其中71名患者有匹配的PBMC数据。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"该研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组与免疫系统在ICI治疗中的纵向动态关系及其对疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。通过对126名患者的基线和第6周粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序，并对71名患者的外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）进行质谱流式细胞术分析，研究发现ICI治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞增加和调节性T细胞（Tregs）减少。Tregs的减少主要见于应答者，但在发生严重irAEs的患者中也观察到显著缺乏。基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与Tregs减少程度及严重irAEs风险正相关，而瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用并关联更好的应答。结论指出肠道微生物组可能通过影响免疫平衡的“临界点”来塑造ICI的治疗结果。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组如何通过调节特定免疫细胞亚群（特别是Tregs）来影响ICI疗效和毒性的具体实证数据。它特别强调了‘双刃剑’效应：某些细菌（如拟杆菌属）既关联于免疫激活（Treg减少），也关联于过度免疫反应（严重irAEs），从而帮助解释为何微生物组能预测疗效但也伴随毒性风险。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅针对III期黑色素瘤患者，且为新辅助联合ICI治疗情境；不能直接外推至其他肿瘤类型或单药ICI治疗。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌类群（拟杆菌属、瘤胃球菌科）与ICI疗效（客观缓解）及毒性（irAEs严重程度）的具体关联方向和数据支持。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"可用于综述中讨论微生物组标志物预测疗效和毒性的部分，特别是解释不同细菌类群的差异化作用。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察性关联提出的假设性机制（'suggests that...'），并非经过功能验证的因果机制；需结合其他研究确认其普遍性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制线索：肠道微生物组可能通过影响基线免疫稳态（特别是Tregs的水平）来设定免疫反应的‘阈值’或‘临界点’，从而影响抗肿瘤免疫和irAEs的发生。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"可用于综述中探讨微生物组介导ICI疗效的潜在免疫学机制，特别是Tregs在其中的核心角色。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"可作为综述引言或背景部分，阐述研究该问题的必要性和当前理解的局限性。\",\n            \"material\": \"摘要中提到‘how gut microbes interact with the immune system... remains unclear’，反映了该领域的知识空白和研究动机。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"提供背景信息，说明当前领域对微生物组-免疫互作研究的现状和挑战。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"可用于综述中讨论微生物组标志物的异质性和多效性，避免简单化的‘好菌/坏菌’二分法。\",\n            \"material\": \"拟杆菌属既与Treg减少（通常关联疗效）相关，又与严重irAEs相关；而瘤胃球菌科则显示保护性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"举例说明微生物组影响免疫治疗的复杂性，即同一微生物信号可能同时关联获益和风险。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究为会议摘要，详细的方法学细节（如测序深度、生物信息学流程、流式抗体面板、统计分析模型）未在摘要中提供，需谨慎引用具体数值和方法论细节。\",\n          \"研究对象仅限于III期黑色素瘤患者，且接受的是新辅助联合ICI治疗，结果可能不适用于晚期转移性黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"关联不等于因果：观察到的微生物与免疫细胞及临床结局的关联可能是由其他未测量的混杂因素驱动的，或反映的是反向因果关系。\",\n          \"‘拟杆菌属’是一个属水平的分类单元，其内部物种可能存在功能差异，摘要未提供更精细的分类或功能信息。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"肠道微生物组\",\n          \"免疫检查点抑制剂\",\n          \"黑色素瘤\",\n          \"调节性T细胞 (Tregs)\",\n          \"效应记忆T细胞 (Tem)\",\n          \"免疫相关不良事件 (irAEs)\",\n          \"拟杆菌属 (Bacteroides)\",\n          \"瘤胃球菌科 (Ruminococcaceae)\",\n          \"纵向微生物组-免疫动态\",\n          \"新辅助治疗\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\\\\b33f79e777278a549aec748fde5129d1\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"identity\",\n            \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n            \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\\\\b33f79e777278a549aec748fde5129d1\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n      \"title\": \"The Evolving Landscape of Immunotoxicity: Charting Mechanisms and Future Strategies for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Adverse Events\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1002/mdr2.70019\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"6f8044dc50ea73203f972ec2f8a2e2527694e3d3\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"As a narrative review, the authors synthesized existing literature on ICI-induced irAEs. The structure follows a logical progression: first, elucidating core immunopathological mechanisms (T-cell, B-cell, cytokine, monocyte axes); second, analyzing multidimensional risk factors (host, environment, treatment, tumor, genetics); third, detailing clinical features, grading, and management strategies for irAEs across major organ systems; and fourth, proposing future research directions focusing on shared mechanisms, predictive models, and optimized intervention strategies. The approach relies on summarizing clinical studies, experimental data, and meta-analyses cited in the references.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive, up-to-date synthesis of the multifaceted mechanisms (cellular and molecular) underlying irAEs, integrating T-cell, B-cell, cytokine, and monocyte pathways.\",\n            \"limits\": \"As a review, it does not present new primary experimental data or validate predictive biomarkers clinically; it summarizes existing evidence which may be heterogeneous.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Offers a detailed, organ-system-based classification of irAEs with specific incidence rates, grading criteria, and tiered management strategies, serving as a practical clinical reference.\",\n            \"limits\": \"Management recommendations are largely based on expert consensus and existing guidelines rather than novel randomized controlled trials presented in this paper.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Identifies and categorizes diverse risk factors, highlighting the role of gut microbiota and genetic polymorphisms, pointing towards precision medicine approaches.\",\n            \"limits\": \"Many identified risk factors (e.g., specific microbial strains, genetic variants) are noted as having 'promising' but 'not yet universally validated' predictive value; the paper acknowledges the lack of reliable clinical biomarkers.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI therapy (anti-CTLA-4, anti-PD-1/PD-L1)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Core mechanisms involve Treg exhaustion, Teff overactivation/cross-reactivity, B-cell autoantibody production, cytokine network imbalance, and monocyte/macrophage inflammatory cascades.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Risk factors analysis\",\n            \"finding\": \"Risk is influenced by host factors (age, sex, BMI, comorbidities), gut microbiota dysbiosis (e.g., Akkermansia muciniphila abundance), treatment regimen (combination therapy increases severity, dose-dependency), tumor type/histology (high TMB/high burden), and genetic factors (HLA polymorphisms like HLA-DR4).\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Organ-specific irAEs\",\n            \"finding\": \"Different organs have distinct incidence and severity profiles; e.g., anti-CTLA-4 is linked to colitis/hypophysitis, while anti-PD-1/PD-L1 is linked to pneumonitis/thyroid dysfunction. Rare but fatal events include myocarditis and myasthenia gravis.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Correlation with efficacy\",\n            \"finding\": \"There is a partial statistical correlation between certain irAEs (e.g., vitiligo) and anti-tumor efficacy, suggesting shared antigenic targets, but excessive immunosuppression may diminish efficacy.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"The review addresses the critical challenge that while ICIs significantly improve cancer survival, they cause severe, multi-organ irAEs due to disrupted immune tolerance. Key problems include the lack of reliable predictive biomarkers, incomplete understanding of molecular pathophysiology (especially for rare/fatal irAEs), complex toxicity profiles from combination therapies, and the controversial correlation between irAEs and anti-tumor efficacy. The goal is to provide a systematic framework for clinicians to understand, predict, and manage these toxicities.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) used in cancer therapy, specifically examining the mechanisms, risk factors, and clinical management of immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It covers various organ systems (skin, gastrointestinal, endocrine, cardiovascular, etc.) and discusses future research directions. The scope includes solid tumors generally, with specific mentions of melanoma, lung cancer, renal cell carcinoma, and hepatocellular carcinoma.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This is a comprehensive review article published in 2025 that systematically summarizes the pathophysiology, risk stratification, and clinical management of irAEs associated with ICIs. It details how ICIs disrupt immune homeostasis through T-cell dysfunction, B-cell autoantibody production, cytokine dysregulation, and monocyte-mediated inflammation. The paper categorizes irAEs by organ system, providing incidence rates, grading criteria, and treatment guidelines. It also identifies multiple risk factors including host characteristics, gut microbiota, genetic polymorphisms, and treatment regimens. Finally, it outlines future strategies for prediction, prevention, and targeted intervention to balance anti-tumor efficacy with safety.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This review provides a broad overview of ICI mechanisms and risks, including a dedicated section on gut microbiome dysbiosis as a risk factor for irAEs. However, its focus is primarily on *toxicity* (adverse events) rather than *efficacy*. For the user's query about how the gut microbiome modulates ICI *efficacy* in solid tumors, this paper offers limited direct evidence. It mentions that certain microbes (e.g., Akkermansia muciniphila) can enhance antitumor responses (prolonging OS in NSCLC) but simultaneously increase irAE risk. It serves best as background context for the dual role of microbiota or as a source for mechanisms of toxicity, rather than a primary source for efficacy modulation mechanisms.\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"The association is observational/correlational in the cited studies. The paper emphasizes the *dual effect*: these same microbes may also increase irAE risk. It does not provide mechanistic depth on *how* exactly the microbiome modulates efficacy beyond general immune activation.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Mentions that high abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (>4.8%) is associated with prolonged overall survival in NSCLC patients receiving ICIs, attributing this to enhanced CD8+ T lymphocyte activation and IFN-γ secretion. Also notes that other microbes can enhance antitumor immunity.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support the claim that specific gut microbiota compositions are associated with improved ICI efficacy in solid tumors (specifically NSCLC).\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"The mechanistic details provided are largely inferred from general immunology or cited animal/experimental studies. The paper explicitly states that the molecular interaction networks require further investigation. It does not detail specific microbial metabolites or precise signaling pathways linking microbiota directly to tumor antigen presentation or T-cell priming for efficacy.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Describes mechanisms where gut microbiota influence T-cell subsets (e.g., Th17 differentiation and function). Dysbiosis may disrupt Th17 homeostasis, leading to hyperfunction and pro-inflammatory cytokine release. It also mentions that specific probiotics/prebiotics can alleviate irAE symptoms, implying a regulatory role.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic insights into how gut microbiota might influence the immune response landscape (potentially affecting both efficacy and toxicity) via T-cell regulation (Th17/Treg balance).\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Contextualizes the complexity of ICI therapy by highlighting the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity mediated by common factors like microbiota and immune activation.\",\n            \"material\": \"Discussion of Akkermansia muciniphila having a 'dual effect' (enhancing survival but increasing irAE risk); mention of gut microbiota regulating Th17 cells.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To illustrate the interconnectedness of efficacy and toxicity mechanisms, suggesting that strategies targeting one may impact the other. Useful for discussing the challenges of balancing benefits and risks.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides background on the current state of predictive biomarkers.\",\n            \"material\": \"Statement that despite many potential biomarkers (including microbiota-related ones), there is currently no universally acknowledged reliable biomarker for predicting irAE risk.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To highlight the gap in clinical translation of microbiome-based predictions, supporting arguments for the need for more rigorous validation studies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"The paper's primary focus is on *adverse events* (irAEs), not efficacy. Any claims about efficacy modulation are secondary mentions or part of the discussion on shared mechanisms/toxicity risks.\",\n          \"The link between gut microbiota and efficacy is described as correlational (e.g., abundance levels associated with survival) rather than definitively causal or mechanistically fully elucidated in this text.\",\n          \"Specific microbial species mentioned (e.g., Akkermansia) are linked to outcomes in specific contexts (NSCLC), and results may not be generalizable to all solid tumors or all ICI types without further verification.\",\n          \"Mechanisms involving gut microbiota are often summarized broadly (e.g., 'regulating T-cell subsets') without detailed molecular pathways, requiring caution when inferring specific causal chains.\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"gut microbiome dysbiosis\",\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n          \"solid tumours (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, HCC)\",\n          \"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\n          \"T-cell dysfunction\",\n          \"B-cell autoantibodies\",\n          \"cytokine networks\",\n          \"monocyte/macrophage activation\",\n          \"risk factors (genetics, host, treatment)\",\n          \"organ-specific toxicity management\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\6f8044dc50ea73203f972ec2f8a2e2527694e3d3\\\\024abf8a881fc6ce5a053a7eebb5478f\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\6f8044dc50ea73203f972ec2f8a2e2527694e3d3\\\\024abf8a881fc6ce5a053a7eebb5478f\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n      \"year\": \"2024\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"1. 队列设计：两项前瞻性非随机队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），基于疗效（PFI≥1年）和irAE严重程度（≥2级）将患者分为获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组。采用地标分析（Landmark analysis）以1年为界评估irAE，减少 immortal time bias。2. 多组学分析：宏基因组测序鉴定物种丰度、共现网络、功能通路（如SCFA合成基因）；代谢组GC-MS定量SCFA。3. 分子模拟分析：将微生物序列与自身免疫疾病抗原库及肺癌抗原/抗癌肽数据库比对，识别交叉反应表位。4. 菌株水平分析：使用StrainPhlAn分析大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌的SGBs变异及系统发育信号。5. 外部验证：在McCulloch（黑色素瘤ICI）、Routy（NSCLC ICI）等公共数据集上验证SCFA预测值和抗原模拟结果。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"首次提供实证证据支持微生物组通过分子模拟驱动irAEs（自身免疫抗原模拟）和ICI疗效（肿瘤抗原模拟）的假设。揭示了长期获益者特有的紧凑微生物网络和丁酸高产能力。明确了菌株水平变异（而非仅物种丰度）对临床表型的决定性作用。\",\n            \"limits\": \"样本量较小（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），可能限制统计效力。抗原模拟分析依赖于公共数据库中的已知表位，可能遗漏未表征的关键表位。菌株分析仅针对丰度较高的少数物种。所有样本为基线采集，无法反映治疗过程中的动态变化。外部验证队列的治疗方案和肿瘤类型不完全一致（如黑色素瘤vs肺癌）。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比获益组与耐药组（宏基因组预测+代谢组验证）\",\n            \"finding\": \"获益组富集丙酸（P=0.01）和丁酸/异丁酸（P=0.12/0.02）。乙酸、丙酸、丁酸水平越高，PFS越长，肿瘤进展风险越低（HR<1, P<0.05）。丁酸生产主要受乙酰辅酶A途径介导。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比irAE组与非irAE组\",\n            \"finding\": \"irAE患者微生物中与系统性红斑狼疮（SLE）、皮肤/结缔组织自身免疫病相关的抗原表位对齐数量更多，特别是在免疫性结肠炎患者中SLE相关表位显著富集（P=0.04）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比高疗效组与低疗效组\",\n            \"finding\": \"高疗效组微生物中与肺癌相关的抗原和抗癌肽（ACP）表位对齐数量更多（P=0.07/0.06），并在Routy队列中得到部分验证（P=0.02）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"特定物种（大肠杆菌、普拉梭菌）\",\n            \"finding\": \"菌株水平变异与临床表型强相关。例如，普拉梭菌SGB15342在获益组中富集，而SGB15323/332_group倾向出现在严重irAE组。不同组间存在高突变率，表明菌株特异性决定功能。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI的初始疗效和irAEs，但其对长期生存获益的具体影响及底层机制（如代谢物、分子模拟、菌株变异）尚不清楚。特别是区分长期获益者与耐药者或仅发生irAE者的微生物特征差异。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"中国北京协和医院晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，接受抗PD-1/PD-L1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗。研究聚焦于基线肠道微生物组与代谢组特征对长期疗效（无进展生存期PFI≥1年）及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。样本分为长期获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组，并通过外部公共队列（McCulloch, Routy等）进行验证。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组如何影响肺癌患者ICI治疗的长期结局及其潜在机制。通过前瞻性收集基线粪便样本进行宏基因组和代谢组测序，结合临床随访数据，分析微生物组成、短链脂肪酸（SCFA）水平、分子模拟现象及菌株变异与临床表型的关系。研究发现，长期获益患者拥有更紧凑的微生物网络和高产丁酸/丙酸的能力；irAE患者的微生物中存在与自身免疫抗原相似的表位；响应患者的微生物中富含与肺癌抗原相似的表位；且特定物种（如大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌）的菌株水平变异与临床表型显著相关。这些发现为“智能”粪菌移植提供了理论依据。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组调节ICI疗效和irAEs的多维度机制证据，特别是从代谢产物（SCFAs）、分子模拟（抗原交叉反应）和菌株特异性三个层面。其价值在于将宏观的菌群组成差异细化到具体的代谢通路、抗原表位匹配和微观的基因组变异，为解释“为何某些菌群有益而另一些有害”提供了具体机制素材，并提出了“智能FMT”的概念框架。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"数据主要来自肺癌患者，虽在黑色素瘤队列中验证了丙酸/丁酸趋势，但需注意肿瘤类型的异质性。关联性强，但因果链条需结合其他干预研究理解。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）作为预测ICI长期疗效的生物标志物的实证数据。具体指出丁酸生产依赖乙酰辅酶A途径，且高水平SCFA与延长PFS和降低进展风险相关。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中讨论微生物代谢产物如何直接促进抗肿瘤免疫或改善预后。可作为支持“有益菌群通过代谢物发挥作用”这一观点的具体证据。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"分子模拟的证据基于序列同源性比对，属于相关性/预测性证据，尚未通过体内实验直接证明T细胞交叉反应。抗原数据库可能存在偏差。菌株分析仅限于少数物种。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提出了并初步验证了“分子模拟”机制：1) 微生物抗原模拟宿主自身免疫抗原导致irAEs（特别是SLE相关表位在结肠炎患者中富集）；2) 微生物抗原模拟肿瘤抗原增强ICI疗效。同时强调了菌株特异性（如大肠杆菌毒力基因簇）在决定irAE或耐药中的作用。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中解释irAEs发生的免疫学机制，以及微生物如何被免疫系统识别从而间接或直接影响抗肿瘤效果。可用于讨论为何同一物种在不同个体或菌株下表现不同。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"定义了“长期获益”患者的微生物特征（紧凑网络、高产丁酸），区别于短期响应或仅发生irAE的患者。\",\n            \"material\": \"Co-occurrence networks showing compactness in benefit group; enrichment of butyrate producers like F. prausnitzii, Blautia.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为背景或对比基准，说明长期生存者与短期响应者在微生物生态结构上的潜在差异。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提出了“智能FMT”的概念，即选择具有特定菌株动力学、SCFA生产能力且不模拟自身免疫抗原的细菌制剂。\",\n            \"material\": \"Discussion section proposing 'smart' FMT based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为未来干预策略的理论基础或展望部分，展示当前研究如何转化为临床转化思路。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的分子模拟结论是基于生物信息学预测（序列比对），并非直接的免疫学功能验证（如T细胞克隆追踪），在综述中应表述为“提示”或“初步证据”，而非确证机制。\",\n          \"菌株水平的发现仅适用于大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌等丰度较高的物种，不能推广到所有微生物。\",\n          \"外部验证队列（McCulloch, Routy）在肿瘤类型和治疗方案上与主队列存在差异，解读时需考虑肿瘤微环境异质性的影响。\",\n          \"irAE分析采用了地标分析以校正时间偏倚，这是该方法学上的优势，但在比较不同研究时需注意终点定义的一致性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) production pathways (acetyl-CoA, succinate)\",\n          \"Molecular mimicry: Microbial epitopes vs Autoimmune antigens (SLE, colitis)\",\n          \"Molecular mimicry: Microbial epitopes vs Tumor antigens/Anticancer peptides\",\n          \"Strain-level variation in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii\",\n          \"Microbial co-occurrence network topology in long-term responders\",\n          \"Landmark analysis for irAEs to avoid immortal time bias\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-u2gi65cq\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_4e312d3d88\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Use this study to summarize current mechanistic hypotheses for irAEs (molecular mimicry, SCFA depletion, strain variation) and to cite as an example of existing literature that, despite mechanistic depth, remains limited by small sample sizes and composite irAE grouping. This supports the argument that large-scale, subtype-specific studies are still needed to validate findings for non-colitis irAEs.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The specific request for large-scale microbiome association studies focused on non-colitis irAEs (such as myocarditis or neurotoxicity) is not fulfilled by this material. While this study includes some non-colitis irAE cases (e.g., cardiovascular, muscle) within a composite 'severe irAE' group, the total sample size (n=13 for severe irAE) is small, and there is no dedicated large-scale analysis for specific non-colitis subtypes. The authors' own admission of limited sample size confirms the ongoing evidence gap regarding statistical power for specific irAE subtypes.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\\\\e6d0d6ef9a5d062d4cdc8e2e4fb5ee85\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\\\\e6d0d6ef9a5d062d4cdc8e2e4fb5ee85\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiota composition in patients with advanced malignancies experiencing immune-related adverse events\",\n      \"year\": \"2023\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2023.1109281\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:257062954\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"采用混合研究设计：1. 临床观察性研究：前瞻性收集93份来自37名抗PD-1治疗肺癌患者的粪便样本，以及61份来自33名发生irAEs的多癌种患者样本。使用16S rDNA扩增子测序进行微生物组分析，计算α/β多样性，使用LEfSe识别差异菌属，并通过随机森林算法构建irAE预测模型。2. 动物因果验证：将C57BL/6小鼠经抗生素鸡尾酒处理清除原有菌群后，分别移植来自有结肠炎型irAE患者和无irAE患者的粪便菌群。随后给予抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4单抗诱导免疫反应，评估结肠炎发生率、疾病活动指数、组织病理学及炎症因子表达。3. 功能机制推测：基于16S数据使用Tax4fun和KEGG数据库预测微生物功能通路，重点关注短链脂肪酸（如丁酸）产生菌丰度及代谢途径差异。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了在非黑色素瘤实体瘤（主要是肺癌）背景下，肠道微生物群与irAEs发生的关联证据；区分了结肠炎型与非结肠炎型irAEs的微生物特征差异；通过人源化小鼠FMT实验提供了微生物群导致免疫性结肠炎的因果证据；识别出丁酸产生菌丰度降低可能与irAEs发生有关。\",\n            \"limits\": \"样本量较小（最终纳入分析的无irAE组34人，irAE组32人），可能导致统计效力不足或过拟合风险；仅使用16S rDNA测序进行功能预测，缺乏宏基因组或代谢组学的直接验证；基线前ICI治疗前的粪便样本获取困难，限制了基线状态的全面分析；无法完全排除irAEs本身对微生物群的扰动影响（尽管FMT支持因果方向）；预测模型需外部独立队列验证。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1治疗后出现irAEs的患者 vs 未出现irAEs的患者\",\n            \"finding\": \"微生物组成显著不同（P=0.001）。irAE患者中双歧杆菌（Bifidobacterium）、粪杆菌属（Faecalibacterium）和阿加索细菌属（Agathobacter）丰度较低，而红球菌属（Erysipelatoclostridium）丰度较高。主要丁酸产生菌总丰度在irAE患者中更低（P=0.007）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"结肠炎型irAE患者 vs 非结肠炎型irAE患者\",\n            \"finding\": \"微生物组成显著不同（P=0.003）。结肠炎型患者中拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）和双歧杆菌丰度较低，肠球菌属（Enterococcus）丰度较高。主要丁酸产生菌丰度也较低（P=0.018）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"小鼠FMT实验（结肠炎型irAE供体 vs 无irAE供体）+ 抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗\",\n            \"finding\": \"结肠炎型irAE-FMT组小鼠中3/9发展为致命性严重结肠炎，而非irAE-FMT组0/9发病。结肠炎小鼠表现为体重下降更快、DAI评分更高、结肠缩短、组织损伤更重，且结肠组织中Il6和Tnf mRNA水平升高。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"irAE预测模型构建\",\n            \"finding\": \"基于10个主要差异菌属（以Gemella, Dubosiella, Atopobium为主）的随机森林模型在训练集AUC为86.4%，测试集AUC为91.7%。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效，但其作为irAEs发生和严重程度的角色及其因果关系尚未确立。特别是针对除黑色素瘤以外的其他癌症类型（如肺癌），以及不同器官受累的irAEs，微生物群的差异特征和作用机制尚不明确。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"研究对象为接受抗PD-1治疗的晚期胸廓恶性肿瘤（主要为肺癌）患者，以及发生免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）的多种实体瘤患者。研究情境包括临床队列观察和基于人类粪便微生物移植（FMT）的小鼠实验。范围涵盖不同严重程度和器官类型的irAEs，重点聚焦于结肠炎型irAEs。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物群与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗引发的免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的关联及因果关系。研究首先通过16S rDNA测序分析了接受抗PD-1治疗的肺癌患者及发生irAEs的其他癌症患者的粪便样本，比较了有无irAEs、不同严重程度（1-2级 vs 3-4级）以及不同部位（结肠炎型 vs 非结肠炎型）患者间的微生物组成差异，并构建了预测模型。随后，通过抗生素预处理小鼠并进行来自不同患者组的FMT，结合抗PD-1/CTLA-4抗体治疗，验证微生物群对免疫性结肠炎的因果作用。最后，利用功能预测分析探讨了潜在的代谢机制。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物群如何影响ICI治疗副作用（特别是irAEs）的具体实证素材。其核心价值在于不仅描述了相关性，还通过FMT小鼠实验确立了微生物群对免疫性结肠炎的因果贡献，并细化了不同irAE亚型（结肠炎vs非结肠炎）的微生物指纹。这有助于综述中讨论微生物群介导的毒性机制、潜在的保护性菌群标志物（如丁酸产生菌）以及微生物群在预测和管理irAEs中的潜力。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"样本局限于晚期胸廓肿瘤和多癌种irAE患者，结果可能不适用于所有ICI药物（如抗CTLA-4单药）或早期癌症人群。预测模型未经外部验证。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群组成与ICI治疗安全性（irAEs发生）的直接关联数据。具体显示irAE患者中特定有益菌（双歧杆菌、粪杆菌、阿加索细菌）减少，有害菌（红球菌属）增加。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"可用于综述中阐述微生物群特征如何作为irAEs的风险因素或生物标志物。帮助解释为何某些患者更容易发生毒性反应。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"小鼠模型使用了抗生素预处理和联合抗体治疗，与人体的生理状态存在差异。功能分析仅为基于16S的预测，非直接代谢物测量。并非所有接受FMT的小鼠都发病，表明其他宿主因素也参与。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"通过FMT小鼠实验证明了来自irAE患者的微生物群能够因果性地诱导免疫性结肠炎。同时指出丁酸产生菌丰度降低和特定代谢通路（如氨基酸、维生素代谢）的差异，提示代谢机制可能在介导irAEs中起作用。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中讨论irAEs的潜在生物学机制，特别是微生物群-宿主免疫互作中的代谢调节作用。支持“微生物群驱动毒性”的观点，并为通过调节菌群（如补充益生菌）预防irAEs提供理论依据。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"背景与概念框架\",\n            \"material\": \"论文引言部分回顾了微生物群在ICI疗效中的作用，并指出目前研究多集中于黑色素瘤，强调本研究扩展至肺癌等其他实体瘤的重要性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"用于综述中界定研究现状，说明从黑色素瘤向其他实体瘤拓展研究的必要性，以及当前领域对irAEs机制认知的局限性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"实例与反例\",\n            \"material\": \"论文讨论了Faecalibacterium在不同研究中的矛盾结果（有的报道保护，有的报道促炎），并归因于情境依赖性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"用于综述中展示微生物群功能的复杂性，避免单一菌属作用的简单化结论，强调上下文（如ICI类型、基础疾病）对菌群功能的影响。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的因果证据仅限于小鼠模型中的结肠炎表型，不能直接外推至人体所有irAEs的发生机制。\",\n          \"预测模型的AUC值基于内部验证，可能存在过拟合，实际临床应用价值需进一步确认。\",\n          \"功能预测基于16S数据，准确性低于宏基因组测序，代谢通路的差异仅为推测，需代谢组学验证。\",\n          \"样本量较小，特别是严重irAEs亚组分析可能缺乏统计效力。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\n          \"gut microbiota composition\",\n          \"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"butyrate-producing bacteria\",\n          \"colitis-type irAEs\",\n          \"solid tumors (lung cancer)\",\n          \"anti-PD-1 therapy\",\n          \"metabolic pathways prediction\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"在综述中引用此研究作为当前领域局限性的实证案例，说明即使是前瞻性收集样本的研究，针对罕见非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组分析仍受限于样本量。建议后续行动包括检索多中心联合队列、国际微生物组联盟数据或病例报告汇总，以寻找是否有关于特定非结肠炎 irAEs 的汇总分析或 Meta 分析。\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有研究（包括本研究）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少（如本研究仅 3 例心肌炎）而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，无法充分验证或解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题。\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"在综述中引用此研究作为当前领域局限性的实证案例，说明即使是前瞻性收集样本的研究，针对罕见非结肠炎 irAEs 的微生物组分析仍受限于样本量。建议后续行动包括检索多中心联合队列、国际微生物组联盟数据或病例报告汇总，以寻找是否有关于特定非结肠炎 irAEs 的汇总分析或 Meta 分析。\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有研究（包括本研究）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少（如本研究仅 3 例心肌炎）而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，无法充分验证或解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题。\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch1.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n            \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"为综述中关于“FMT作用机制的争议”提供反面证据或补充视角，即定植效率可能不是决定疗效的唯一或主要因素。\",\n            \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"背景信息，用于对比不同研究中关于FMT机制的解释（定植vs清除）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"跨研究的一致性证据，支持“有害菌清除”作为FMT疗效通用机制的假设。\",\n            \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为外部验证，增强综述中关于机制结论的可信度。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中ICI的疗效”，提供具体的临床响应率证据，支持FMT作为增敏策略的有效性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“介导该效应的机制是什么”，提供微生物组重塑的具体分子和免疫学路径，挑战传统的“益生菌定植”主导观点，强调“去致病化”的重要性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于讨论ICI疗效与安全性之间的权衡，以及微生物组在预测和管理irAEs中的作用，提示未来FMT研究中供体筛选的重要性。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于FMT联合ICI治疗实体瘤的关键临床数据，特别是其在克服原发性耐药方面的潜力。更重要的是，它提出了一个区别于传统“有益菌定植”假说的新机制框架：即治疗获益主要源于FMT诱导的基线有害病原体（pathobionts）的清除，进而调节宿主代谢和免疫微环境。此外，它还揭示了供体菌群特征（如Prevotella丰度）与特定ICI方案（双免疫检查点抑制）相互作用下的安全性风险。\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n          \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n          \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"FMT联合ICI的临床疗效（NSCLC, Melanoma）\",\n          \"FMT介导的微生物组重塑机制（有害菌清除 vs 有益菌定植）\",\n          \"肠道微生物-免疫代谢轴（色氨酸代谢, 喹啉酸, 犬尿氨酸）\",\n          \"ICI相关不良反应（irAEs）的微生物驱动因素\",\n          \"供体选择对治疗安全性和有效性的影响\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material\": {\n        \"_progressive_task_requirements\": {\n          \"knowledge_gaps\": [\n            \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\"\n          ],\n          \"questions\": [\n            {\n              \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n              \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n              \"required_output_ids\": [\n                \"O01\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"required_outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n              \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n              \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"_progressive_task_signature\": \"37c81ea7cb18384d\",\n        \"current_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"fulfilled\": false,\n        \"paper_identity\": {\n          \"canonical_paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n          \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n          \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\"\n        },\n        \"paper_title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"plain_text\": \"\",\n        \"prior_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"required_output_ids\": [\n              \"O01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\",\n        \"required_outputs\": [\n          {\n            \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n            \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n            \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"source_hash\": \"8dd08b84648262841f9d35af692160252692383791e7c7d076ecd654063fb0f3\",\n        \"task_hash\": \"4fcf708140bdb8b00ce198191a4362b1ee8545d9d5569d77e4118fb1833a9f61\"\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material_trimmed\": {\n        \"dropped_keys\": {\n          \"material_ready\": 4,\n          \"paper_id\": 42,\n          \"references\": 413,\n          \"review_id\": 23,\n          \"schema_version\": 46,\n          \"status\": 9,\n          \"task_id\": 34,\n          \"workflow\": 21\n        },\n        \"dropped_chars\": 592,\n        \"note\": \"深读材料里的记账字段与论文自带的参考文献表已省略；科学内容（问句材料/发现/条件）保留。需要时可用 locator 读原文。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\on_demand_promotion_local_20261007_10cny\\\\formal_complete_plan\\\\revisions\\\\03912c907286ec6fbd55\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch2.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"assets\",\n            \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n      \"year\": \"2024\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.ebiom.2024.105427\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"1. 队列设计：两项前瞻性非随机队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），基于疗效（PFI≥1年）和irAE严重程度（≥2级）将患者分为获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组。采用地标分析（Landmark analysis）以1年为界评估irAE，减少 immortal time bias。2. 多组学分析：宏基因组测序鉴定物种丰度、共现网络、功能通路（如SCFA合成基因）；代谢组GC-MS定量SCFA。3. 分子模拟分析：将微生物序列与自身免疫疾病抗原库及肺癌抗原/抗癌肽数据库比对，识别交叉反应表位。4. 菌株水平分析：使用StrainPhlAn分析大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌的SGBs变异及系统发育信号。5. 外部验证：在McCulloch（黑色素瘤ICI）、Routy（NSCLC ICI）等公共数据集上验证SCFA预测值和抗原模拟结果。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"首次提供实证证据支持微生物组通过分子模拟驱动irAEs（自身免疫抗原模拟）和ICI疗效（肿瘤抗原模拟）的假设。揭示了长期获益者特有的紧凑微生物网络和丁酸高产能力。明确了菌株水平变异（而非仅物种丰度）对临床表型的决定性作用。\",\n            \"limits\": \"样本量较小（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），可能限制统计效力。抗原模拟分析依赖于公共数据库中的已知表位，可能遗漏未表征的关键表位。菌株分析仅针对丰度较高的少数物种。所有样本为基线采集，无法反映治疗过程中的动态变化。外部验证队列的治疗方案和肿瘤类型不完全一致（如黑色素瘤vs肺癌）。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比获益组与耐药组（宏基因组预测+代谢组验证）\",\n            \"finding\": \"获益组富集丙酸（P=0.01）和丁酸/异丁酸（P=0.12/0.02）。乙酸、丙酸、丁酸水平越高，PFS越长，肿瘤进展风险越低（HR<1, P<0.05）。丁酸生产主要受乙酰辅酶A途径介导。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比irAE组与非irAE组\",\n            \"finding\": \"irAE患者微生物中与系统性红斑狼疮（SLE）、皮肤/结缔组织自身免疫病相关的抗原表位对齐数量更多，特别是在免疫性结肠炎患者中SLE相关表位显著富集（P=0.04）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"对比高疗效组与低疗效组\",\n            \"finding\": \"高疗效组微生物中与肺癌相关的抗原和抗癌肽（ACP）表位对齐数量更多（P=0.07/0.06），并在Routy队列中得到部分验证（P=0.02）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"特定物种（大肠杆菌、普拉梭菌）\",\n            \"finding\": \"菌株水平变异与临床表型强相关。例如，普拉梭菌SGB15342在获益组中富集，而SGB15323/332_group倾向出现在严重irAE组。不同组间存在高突变率，表明菌株特异性决定功能。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI的初始疗效和irAEs，但其对长期生存获益的具体影响及底层机制（如代谢物、分子模拟、菌株变异）尚不清楚。特别是区分长期获益者与耐药者或仅发生irAE者的微生物特征差异。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"中国北京协和医院晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，接受抗PD-1/PD-L1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗。研究聚焦于基线肠道微生物组与代谢组特征对长期疗效（无进展生存期PFI≥1年）及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。样本分为长期获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组，并通过外部公共队列（McCulloch, Routy等）进行验证。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组如何影响肺癌患者ICI治疗的长期结局及其潜在机制。通过前瞻性收集基线粪便样本进行宏基因组和代谢组测序，结合临床随访数据，分析微生物组成、短链脂肪酸（SCFA）水平、分子模拟现象及菌株变异与临床表型的关系。研究发现，长期获益患者拥有更紧凑的微生物网络和高产丁酸/丙酸的能力；irAE患者的微生物中存在与自身免疫抗原相似的表位；响应患者的微生物中富含与肺癌抗原相似的表位；且特定物种（如大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌）的菌株水平变异与临床表型显著相关。这些发现为“智能”粪菌移植提供了理论依据。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"定义了“长期获益”患者的微生物特征（紧凑网络、高产丁酸），区别于短期响应或仅发生irAE的患者。\",\n            \"material\": \"Co-occurrence networks showing compactness in benefit group; enrichment of butyrate producers like F. prausnitzii, Blautia.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为背景或对比基准，说明长期生存者与短期响应者在微生物生态结构上的潜在差异。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提出了“智能FMT”的概念，即选择具有特定菌株动力学、SCFA生产能力且不模拟自身免疫抗原的细菌制剂。\",\n            \"material\": \"Discussion section proposing 'smart' FMT based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为未来干预策略的理论基础或展望部分，展示当前研究如何转化为临床转化思路。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"数据主要来自肺癌患者，虽在黑色素瘤队列中验证了丙酸/丁酸趋势，但需注意肿瘤类型的异质性。关联性强，但因果链条需结合其他干预研究理解。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）作为预测ICI长期疗效的生物标志物的实证数据。具体指出丁酸生产依赖乙酰辅酶A途径，且高水平SCFA与延长PFS和降低进展风险相关。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中讨论微生物代谢产物如何直接促进抗肿瘤免疫或改善预后。可作为支持“有益菌群通过代谢物发挥作用”这一观点的具体证据。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"分子模拟的证据基于序列同源性比对，属于相关性/预测性证据，尚未通过体内实验直接证明T细胞交叉反应。抗原数据库可能存在偏差。菌株分析仅限于少数物种。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提出了并初步验证了“分子模拟”机制：1) 微生物抗原模拟宿主自身免疫抗原导致irAEs（特别是SLE相关表位在结肠炎患者中富集）；2) 微生物抗原模拟肿瘤抗原增强ICI疗效。同时强调了菌株特异性（如大肠杆菌毒力基因簇）在决定irAE或耐药中的作用。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于综述中解释irAEs发生的免疫学机制，以及微生物如何被免疫系统识别从而间接或直接影响抗肿瘤效果。可用于讨论为何同一物种在不同个体或菌株下表现不同。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组调节ICI疗效和irAEs的多维度机制证据，特别是从代谢产物（SCFAs）、分子模拟（抗原交叉反应）和菌株特异性三个层面。其价值在于将宏观的菌群组成差异细化到具体的代谢通路、抗原表位匹配和微观的基因组变异，为解释“为何某些菌群有益而另一些有害”提供了具体机制素材，并提出了“智能FMT”的概念框架。\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的分子模拟结论是基于生物信息学预测（序列比对），并非直接的免疫学功能验证（如T细胞克隆追踪），在综述中应表述为“提示”或“初步证据”，而非确证机制。\",\n          \"菌株水平的发现仅适用于大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌等丰度较高的物种，不能推广到所有微生物。\",\n          \"外部验证队列（McCulloch, Routy）在肿瘤类型和治疗方案上与主队列存在差异，解读时需考虑肿瘤微环境异质性的影响。\",\n          \"irAE分析采用了地标分析以校正时间偏倚，这是该方法学上的优势，但在比较不同研究时需注意终点定义的一致性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) production pathways (acetyl-CoA, succinate)\",\n          \"Molecular mimicry: Microbial epitopes vs Autoimmune antigens (SLE, colitis)\",\n          \"Molecular mimicry: Microbial epitopes vs Tumor antigens/Anticancer peptides\",\n          \"Strain-level variation in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii\",\n          \"Microbial co-occurrence network topology in long-term responders\",\n          \"Landmark analysis for irAEs to avoid immortal time bias\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-u2gi65cq\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_4e312d3d88\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Use this study to summarize current mechanistic hypotheses for irAEs (molecular mimicry, SCFA depletion, strain variation) and to cite as an example of existing literature that, despite mechanistic depth, remains limited by small sample sizes and composite irAE grouping. This supports the argument that large-scale, subtype-specific studies are still needed to validate findings for non-colitis irAEs.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The specific request for large-scale microbiome association studies focused on non-colitis irAEs (such as myocarditis or neurotoxicity) is not fulfilled by this material. While this study includes some non-colitis irAE cases (e.g., cardiovascular, muscle) within a composite 'severe irAE' group, the total sample size (n=13 for severe irAE) is small, and there is no dedicated large-scale analysis for specific non-colitis subtypes. The authors' own admission of limited sample size confirms the ongoing evidence gap regarding statistical power for specific irAE subtypes.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\on_demand_promotion_local_20261007_10cny\\\\formal_complete_plan\\\\revisions\\\\03912c907286ec6fbd55\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch2.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\\\\e6d0d6ef9a5d062d4cdc8e2e4fb5ee85\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\cc2b555e2b10a62d0141cb12ab5cefa6e47d570c\\\\e6d0d6ef9a5d062d4cdc8e2e4fb5ee85\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n      \"title\": \"Abstract 3463: Longitudinal microbiome-immune dynamics in melanoma patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy\",\n      \"year\": \"2023\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1158/1538-7445.am2023-3463\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"abstract\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"纵向队列研究设计。收集III期黑色素瘤患者在联合ICI治疗前（基线）和治疗后第6周的配对粪便样本（n=126）和外周血PBMC样本（n=71）。使用16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道微生物组成，使用质谱流式细胞术全面 profiling 循环免疫细胞亚群。比较基线与第6周的微生物和免疫指标变化，并分析其与临床应答状态及irAEs严重程度的关联。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向证据，表明肠道微生物组（特别是拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与ICI治疗期间的免疫细胞动态（特别是Tregs）及临床结局（应答和irAEs）存在关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正）、微生物功能推断细节、以及是否控制了其他混杂因素（如抗生素使用、饮食等）。此外，作为会议摘要，缺乏完整的实验细节和长期随访数据。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI治疗前后对比\",\n            \"finding\": \"治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞（Tem）频率增加（P=0.0096）和调节性T细胞（Tregs）频率减少（P=0.0029）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"根据临床应答分类\",\n            \"finding\": \"Tregs的减少主要在应答者中观察到（P=0.0016），而在非应答者中无显著变化（P=0.9515）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"根据irAEs严重程度分类\",\n            \"finding\": \"发生严重irAEs的患者在第6周时Tregs显著缺乏（P=0.0293），相比无或轻度毒性患者。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与免疫变化的关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"在循环Tregs减少的患者中，Tregs减少的程度与基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）相对丰度呈正相关（P<0.0001）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与临床结局的关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"较高的基线拟杆菌属丰度与更严重的irAEs发展（P=0.0472）及第6周前更高的类固醇使用率（P=0.0345）相关。相反，较高的瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）丰度具有保护作用，且瘤胃球菌科主导的微生物组患者中应答者比例更高。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，但具体机制不明。本研究试图解决：肠道微生物如何与免疫系统相互作用以影响ICI的成功或irAEs的发生？特别是特定细菌类群（如拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与免疫细胞亚群变化及临床结局之间的关联。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"III期黑色素瘤患者，接受新辅助联合抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；涉及澳大利亚和荷兰队列（n=126），其中71名患者有匹配的PBMC数据。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"该研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组与免疫系统在ICI治疗中的纵向动态关系及其对疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。通过对126名患者的基线和第6周粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序，并对71名患者的外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）进行质谱流式细胞术分析，研究发现ICI治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞增加和调节性T细胞（Tregs）减少。Tregs的减少主要见于应答者，但在发生严重irAEs的患者中也观察到显著缺乏。基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与Tregs减少程度及严重irAEs风险正相关，而瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用并关联更好的应答。结论指出肠道微生物组可能通过影响免疫平衡的“临界点”来塑造ICI的治疗结果。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"可作为综述引言或背景部分，阐述研究该问题的必要性和当前理解的局限性。\",\n            \"material\": \"摘要中提到‘how gut microbes interact with the immune system... remains unclear’，反映了该领域的知识空白和研究动机。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"提供背景信息，说明当前领域对微生物组-免疫互作研究的现状和挑战。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"可用于综述中讨论微生物组标志物的异质性和多效性，避免简单化的‘好菌/坏菌’二分法。\",\n            \"material\": \"拟杆菌属既与Treg减少（通常关联疗效）相关，又与严重irAEs相关；而瘤胃球菌科则显示保护性。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"举例说明微生物组影响免疫治疗的复杂性，即同一微生物信号可能同时关联获益和风险。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅针对III期黑色素瘤患者，且为新辅助联合ICI治疗情境；不能直接外推至其他肿瘤类型或单药ICI治疗。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌类群（拟杆菌属、瘤胃球菌科）与ICI疗效（客观缓解）及毒性（irAEs严重程度）的具体关联方向和数据支持。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"可用于综述中讨论微生物组标志物预测疗效和毒性的部分，特别是解释不同细菌类群的差异化作用。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察性关联提出的假设性机制（'suggests that...'），并非经过功能验证的因果机制；需结合其他研究确认其普遍性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制线索：肠道微生物组可能通过影响基线免疫稳态（特别是Tregs的水平）来设定免疫反应的‘阈值’或‘临界点’，从而影响抗肿瘤免疫和irAEs的发生。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"可用于综述中探讨微生物组介导ICI疗效的潜在免疫学机制，特别是Tregs在其中的核心角色。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于肠道微生物组如何通过调节特定免疫细胞亚群（特别是Tregs）来影响ICI疗效和毒性的具体实证数据。它特别强调了‘双刃剑’效应：某些细菌（如拟杆菌属）既关联于免疫激活（Treg减少），也关联于过度免疫反应（严重irAEs），从而帮助解释为何微生物组能预测疗效但也伴随毒性风险。\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究为会议摘要，详细的方法学细节（如测序深度、生物信息学流程、流式抗体面板、统计分析模型）未在摘要中提供，需谨慎引用具体数值和方法论细节。\",\n          \"研究对象仅限于III期黑色素瘤患者，且接受的是新辅助联合ICI治疗，结果可能不适用于晚期转移性黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"关联不等于因果：观察到的微生物与免疫细胞及临床结局的关联可能是由其他未测量的混杂因素驱动的，或反映的是反向因果关系。\",\n          \"‘拟杆菌属’是一个属水平的分类单元，其内部物种可能存在功能差异，摘要未提供更精细的分类或功能信息。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"肠道微生物组\",\n          \"免疫检查点抑制剂\",\n          \"黑色素瘤\",\n          \"调节性T细胞 (Tregs)\",\n          \"效应记忆T细胞 (Tem)\",\n          \"免疫相关不良事件 (irAEs)\",\n          \"拟杆菌属 (Bacteroides)\",\n          \"瘤胃球菌科 (Ruminococcaceae)\",\n          \"纵向微生物组-免疫动态\",\n          \"新辅助治疗\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\on_demand_promotion_local_20261007_10cny\\\\formal_complete_plan\\\\revisions\\\\03912c907286ec6fbd55\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch2.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\\\\b33f79e777278a549aec748fde5129d1\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"identity\",\n            \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n            \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n            \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n            \"status\": \"partial\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2709ffca937655fdff12c871b14cb93ee1830d79\\\\b33f79e777278a549aec748fde5129d1\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n      \"title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1186/s40168-026-02419-4\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"The research design involves three main components: 1) Clinical Cohort Analysis: Retrospective and prospective analysis of three independent cohorts (melanoma and NSCLC) to assess the association between irAE grades and survival outcomes, correcting for immortal time bias. 2) Microbiome Profiling: Shotgun metagenomics and high-throughput culturomics were performed on fecal samples from patients at baseline and at the onset of ir-colitis to characterize taxonomic shifts and isolate viable bacteria. 3) Functional Validation: Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) from ir-colitis patients into antibiotic-treated mice to assess effects on tumor growth and inflammation. Specific isolates (P. bifermentans, C. paraputrificum, P. sordellii) were tested in vitro (Caco-2 co-culture for barrier integrity and cytokine expression) and in vivo (oral gavage in DSS colitis and MCA-205 tumor models) to determine direct effects. Cell-free supernatants and heat-killed bacteria were also tested to distinguish live-bacteria-dependent effects from metabolite-mediated effects.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides empirical evidence linking specific gut bacteria (P. bifermentans) to both irAE pathogenesis and enhanced ICI efficacy through distinct mechanisms (barrier disruption vs. metabolite secretion).\",\n            \"limits\": \"The exact nature of the active < 3 kDa metabolite and its precise immune mechanism remain unidentified. The study relies on a limited number of matched longitudinal samples and mouse models that may not fully recapitulate human ir-colitis complexity.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Three independent cohorts of melanoma and NSCLC patients treated with ICI\",\n            \"finding\": \"Grade ≥ 2 irAEs are associated with significantly longer overall survival and progression-free survival, even after adjusting for immortal time bias.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Baseline stool samples from melanoma patients analyzed via shotgun metagenomics\",\n            \"finding\": \"Patients developing grade ≥ 2 irAEs exhibited lower alpha diversity and enrichment of pro-inflammatory taxa including Ruminococcus gnavus and Streptococcus vestibularis compared to those without irAEs.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Stool samples from patients with ir-colitis analyzed via culturomics\",\n            \"finding\": \"Paraclostridium bifermentans was isolated and found to be enriched in patients with acute ir-colitis compared to baseline or non-ir-colitis controls.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"In vivo mouse models receiving FMT from ir-colitis patients\",\n            \"finding\": \"FMT induced surrogate markers of intestinal inflammation (increased Lcn-2 and LPS) and enhanced the anti-tumor efficacy of dual anti-PD-1/CTLA-4 therapy.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"In vitro Caco-2 monolayer co-culture with P. bifermentans\",\n            \"finding\": \"Live P. bifermentans disrupted epithelial barrier integrity (reduced ZO-1 and Occludin signals) and increased pro-inflammatory cytokines (TNF-α and IL-1β); this effect was not observed with cell-free supernatant.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"In vivo murine tumor model with oral gavage of P. bifermentans derivatives\",\n            \"finding\": \"Oral administration of P. bifermentans enhanced anti-tumor response to dual ICI; this beneficial effect was retained by cell-free supernatant filtered to < 3 kDa, indicating mediation by a small-molecule metabolite rather than live bacteria.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"The study aims to resolve the mechanism underlying the observed correlation between irAEs and improved ICI efficacy. Specifically, it seeks to determine if specific gut microbial signatures predict irAEs and efficacy, and to identify causal bacterial agents that might drive both inflammation and anti-tumor responses.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The study focuses on patients with advanced melanoma and non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI). It investigates the relationship between gut microbiome composition, the development of immune-related adverse events (irAEs), and clinical outcomes (overall survival and progression-free survival). The research combines clinical cohort analysis with shotgun metagenomics and culturomics to identify specific bacterial taxa and their functional roles.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This study addresses the paradoxical link between immune-related adverse events (irAEs) and improved efficacy in ICI therapy by dissecting the role of the gut microbiome. Using three independent cohorts totaling 589 patients with melanoma or NSCLC, the authors first validated that grade ≥ 2 irAEs are associated with significantly longer overall survival and progression-free survival, even after adjusting for immortal time bias. They then employed a combined approach of shotgun metagenomics and culturomics on fecal samples collected at baseline and during ir-colitis onset. Metagenomic analysis revealed that patients developing irAEs had lower alpha diversity and enrichment of pro-inflammatory taxa such as Ruminococcus gnavus and Streptococcus vestibularis. Culturomics identified Paraclostridium bifermentans as enriched in patients with acute ir-colitis. Functional validation in mice demonstrated that fecal microbiota transplantation from an ir-colitis patient induced subclinical colitis markers and enhanced anti-tumor activity of dual ICI. Specifically, P. bifermentans was shown to disrupt epithelial barrier integrity in vitro and exacerbate colitis in vivo via live bacteria interaction, while its anti-tumor benefit was mediated by a secreted low-molecular-weight metabolite (< 3 kDa). These findings provide a mechanistic link suggesting that specific pro-inflammatory bacteria can simultaneously drive toxicity and enhance therapeutic efficacy.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Relevant for sections discussing limitations of current microbiome profiling techniques and the need for functional validation.\",\n            \"material\": \"Comparison of metagenomics and culturomics results showing that culturomics recovers live, low-abundance bacteria (like P. bifermentans) missed or less characterized by sequencing alone.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To discuss methodological considerations in microbiome research, highlighting the value of integrating culture-based methods with sequencing for functional discovery.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Useful for methodological critiques or discussions on how to properly interpret associations between toxicity and efficacy in clinical trials.\",\n            \"material\": \"Discussion of immortal time bias in analyzing irAE-survival associations and the correction applied in this study.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To provide context on statistical challenges in observational oncology studies involving time-dependent covariates like irAEs.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"The association is observational; causality is inferred through subsequent mechanistic studies but not proven in the clinical cohort alone. Results may vary by cancer type and geography.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Validates the clinical association between irAEs and improved ICI outcomes across multiple solid tumor cohorts (melanoma and NSCLC), confirming that higher-grade irAEs correlate with longer OS and PFS. Identifies specific microbial signatures (e.g., S. vestibularis, H. porci) associated with both irAE and response states.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support the general observation that microbiome composition correlates with ICI efficacy and toxicity. Provides data on how irAE status serves as a proxy for favorable microbial environments in some contexts.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"The mechanism is derived from mouse models and in vitro assays; the exact metabolite identity is unknown. The effect of live bacteria on barrier integrity is distinct from the metabolite's effect on tumor response, highlighting complex, context-dependent interactions.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Demonstrates a specific mechanism where Paraclostridium bifermentans enhances ICI efficacy via a secreted low-molecular-weight metabolite (< 3 kDa), while simultaneously causing ir-colitis through live-bacteria-induced epithelial barrier disruption. Shows that FMT from ir-colitis patients transfers both inflammatory potential and enhanced ICI response.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Provides a detailed mechanistic example of how a single microbe can have dual, distinct effects on host physiology (toxicity vs. efficacy). Illustrates the role of microbial metabolites in potentiating ICI, offering a potential avenue for targeted therapies (e.g., purified metabolites).\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This paper offers concrete mechanistic insights into how the gut microbiome modulates ICI efficacy, specifically addressing the 'dual role' of certain bacteria in causing toxicity while boosting anti-tumor immunity. It provides a rare example of a single bacterial species (Paraclostridium bifermentans) being functionally linked to both irAE and efficacy, distinguishing between live-bacteria-dependent inflammatory effects and metabolite-mediated immunostimulatory effects. This is valuable for explaining mechanisms where microbial components directly influence host physiology and immune response.\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"The study identifies P. bifermentans as a key player, but the exact metabolite responsible for the anti-tumor effect is not characterized; do not overstate the specificity of the molecular mechanism.\",\n          \"Mouse models used (MCA-205, DSS) have limitations in fully recapitulating human ir-colitis; results should be framed as preclinical evidence supporting human observations.\",\n          \"The 'dual role' of P. bifermentans involves two different mechanisms (live bacteria for toxicity, metabolite for efficacy); ensure this distinction is clear when citing.\",\n          \"Clinical associations are based on retrospective/prospective cohorts with potential confounders; causality is established primarily through animal models, not clinical intervention.\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"Paraclostridium bifermentans\",\n          \"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) efficacy\",\n          \"gut microbiome diversity\",\n          \"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"epithelial barrier integrity\",\n          \"microbial metabolites (< 3 kDa)\",\n          \"shotgun metagenomics\",\n          \"culturomics\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\on_demand_promotion_local_20261007_10cny\\\\formal_complete_plan\\\\revisions\\\\03912c907286ec6fbd55\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch2.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\\\\25b15fdd88b6298d598d73dd0806a771\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-7974b6c4dd5220685baa\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"assets\",\n            \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_body_too_large\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\7cdc8a62c7a781f0b9a88abe52934ab9b889134d\\\\25b15fdd88b6298d598d73dd0806a771\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n      \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"As a narrative review, this paper does not employ a systematic search protocol described in the text. Instead, it synthesizes findings from a broad range of sources including: 1) Historical timeline analysis of key advancements; 2) Summary of clinical trial data (Tables 1-5) linking specific microbial taxa to ICI/ACT outcomes; 3) Mechanistic discussion based on preclinical models (mouse studies) and human cohort analyses regarding immune cell activation, metabolite pathways (SCFAs, bile acids, etc.), and intratumoral interactions; 4) Evaluation of intervention strategies (antibiotics, FMT, probiotics, diet, engineered microbes) by summarizing results from ongoing and completed clinical trials.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides a structured synthesis of clinical and preclinical evidence linking specific gut microbial taxa to ICI and ACT outcomes across multiple cancer types. It categorizes mechanisms into innate/adaptive immunity modulation, metabolite effects, and intratumoral interactions. It also catalogs numerous ongoing clinical trials for FMT, probiotics, and dietary interventions.\",\n            \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks a systematic methodology for study selection, potentially introducing selection bias. Many findings are derived from small-scale clinical studies or animal models, limiting generalizability. The field faces significant heterogeneity in sequencing methods, sample handling, and lack of standardized protocols, making cross-study comparisons difficult. Causal relationships between specific microbes and clinical outcomes are often correlational rather than proven causal.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI therapy (anti-PD-1/PD-L1/CTLA-4)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Specific gut microbial compositions correlate with ICI response. Beneficial taxa include Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia muciniphila, Ruminococcaceae, and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, which are associated with improved survival and tumor regression in melanoma, NSCLC, and RCC. Conversely, antibiotic use generally reduces ICI efficacy.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ACT therapy (CAR-T, TCR-T)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Gut microbiota influences ACT efficacy and toxicity. Certain microbes (e.g., Ruminococcus, Bacteroides) are linked to CAR-T efficacy, while others may predict neurotoxicity or cytokine release syndrome (CRS). Microbial metabolites like SCFAs can enhance CD8+ T cell cytotoxicity.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Mechanisms of Immune Modulation\",\n            \"finding\": \"Microbiota modulate immunity via direct interaction with dendritic cells and macrophages (PRR activation), metabolite signaling (SCFAs, bile acids, tryptophan metabolites influencing T cell differentiation), and molecular mimicry (cross-reactive T cells). Intratumoral microbiota can remodel the TME, promoting TLS formation or inducing immunosuppression.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Intervention Strategies\",\n            \"finding\": \"FMT from ICI responders can overcome resistance in refractory melanoma patients. Probiotics (e.g., Clostridium butyricum CBM588) and dietary interventions (high-fiber, ketogenic) show promise in enhancing ICI response and reducing toxicity, though clinical evidence is still emerging.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"Despite the success of immunotherapies like ICIs and ACTs, patient responses vary widely due to primary or acquired resistance and adverse events. This review aims to elucidate the role of the gut microbiota in shaping these outcomes, identify potential biomarkers for predicting response, and explore microbiota-based strategies to enhance efficacy and mitigate toxicity.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiota and its influence on cancer immunotherapy, specifically immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) and adoptive cell therapies (ACTs). It covers clinical correlations, preclinical mechanisms, intratumoral microbiota, and intervention strategies across various solid tumors and hematologic malignancies.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This paper provides a comprehensive overview of how the gut microbiome modulates the efficacy and toxicity of cancer immunotherapies. It traces the historical evolution from early animal studies to recent clinical trials, detailing specific microbial signatures associated with response or resistance to ICIs and ACTs. The authors synthesize mechanistic insights involving innate and adaptive immune modulation, metabolite production, and tumor microenvironment remodeling. Furthermore, it evaluates therapeutic interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, dietary modifications, and engineered bacteria, while highlighting challenges in standardization and clinical translation.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Contextual background on the evolution of microbiome-immunotherapy research\",\n            \"material\": \"Historical perspective section tracing discoveries from 2007 to 2025, highlighting the shift from correlation to mechanistic understanding and clinical trials.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To provide a timeline of key advancements and justify the current interest in microbiome modulation as a critical factor in immunotherapy success.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Discussion of intervention strategies beyond just biomarkers\",\n            \"material\": \"Sections on FMT, probiotics, antibiotics, diet, and engineered microbes, including tables of clinical trials.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To illustrate potential therapeutic avenues for overcoming ICI resistance and managing toxicity, providing examples of how microbiome modulation is being translated into clinical practice.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"Challenges and limitations in the field\",\n            \"material\": \"Section on 'Challenges and future directions' discussing technical variability, donor effects in FMT, host genetics, and lack of standardization.\",\n            \"purpose\": \"To highlight methodological hurdles and confounding factors that must be considered when interpreting microbiome-ICI associations, explaining why consistent biomarkers are hard to identify.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"Associations are largely correlative from retrospective or small prospective cohorts. Specificity varies by cancer type and ICI agent. Lack of standardized detection methods limits direct comparison. Does not establish causality.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific gut microbial taxa associated with ICI response or resistance in solid tumors. For example, Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, and Ruminococcaceae are linked to better outcomes in melanoma and NSCLC, while certain Proteobacteria or high abundance of Bacteroides intestinalis may correlate with resistance or toxicity. It also notes that beneficial taxa vary by ICI type (anti-PD-1 vs. anti-CTLA-4) and cancer type.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to list candidate microbial biomarkers for predicting ICI efficacy in solid tumors. Helps explain inter-patient variability in treatment response.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are primarily demonstrated in mouse models (preclinical). Human validation is often indirect or observational. Some mechanisms (e.g., molecular mimicry) are proposed but require further confirmation in humans. Effects can be bidirectional (promoting or suppressing immunity depending on context).\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Details mechanisms by which gut microbiota modulate ICI efficacy: 1) Direct immune modulation via PRR activation (TLR/NLR) leading to DC maturation and T-cell activation; 2) Metabolite-mediated regulation (SCFAs inhibiting HDAC, bile acids affecting Th17/Treg balance, tryptophan metabolites via AhR); 3) Molecular mimicry where bacterial antigens cross-react with tumor antigens; 4) Remodeling of the tumor microenvironment (TME) through intratumoral bacteria or systemic metabolites influencing tertiary lymphoid structures (TLS).\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic explanations for how the microbiome influences ICI response. Supports the biological rationale for microbiome-targeted interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This review serves as a foundational resource for mapping the relationship between gut microbiome composition and ICI efficacy in solid tumors. It provides specific microbial markers (taxa) associated with response/resistance, details mechanistic pathways (metabolites, immune cell crosstalk), and outlines current intervention strategies (FMT, probiotics, diet). It is particularly useful for identifying candidate biomarkers and understanding the biological plausibility of microbiome-mediated modulation, while also highlighting the methodological challenges and variability that complicate definitive conclusions.\",\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"The review covers both gut and intratumoral microbiota; ensure distinction is maintained when applying findings to 'gut microbiome' specific facets.\",\n          \"Findings on specific bacterial taxa are highly dependent on the cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. NSCLC) and the specific ICI agent (anti-PD-1 vs. anti-CTLA-4); avoid over-generalizing across all solid tumors.\",\n          \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from murine models; caution is needed when extrapolating to human physiology without explicit human validation mentioned in the text.\",\n          \"Clinical trial data cited are often from early-phase (I/II) or small cohorts; results should not be interpreted as definitive proof of efficacy for interventions like FMT or probiotics.\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"gut microbiota composition and diversity\",\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n          \"solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, HCC, CRC)\",\n          \"fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT)\",\n          \"probiotics and prebiotics\",\n          \"dietary interventions (high-fiber, ketogenic)\",\n          \"microbial metabolites (SCFAs, bile acids, tryptophan metabolites)\",\n          \"intratumoral microbiota\",\n          \"predictive biomarkers for ICI response\",\n          \"immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\on_demand_promotion_local_20261007_10cny\\\\formal_complete_plan\\\\revisions\\\\03912c907286ec6fbd55\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch2.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\\\\92125422c10f28cdb7938d2658870c58\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\\\\92125422c10f28cdb7938d2658870c58\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n      \"title\": \"Abstract B028: Multimodal approach to characterization of metabolism and immune modulation with insights from spatial metabolomics and transcriptomics\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1158/1557-3265.targetedtherap-b028\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"d69f29862a6e18da7c70e3c9d22cd4b7cabc18a3\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch3.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0609\",\n        \"card_path\": \"\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch3.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n            \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于FMT联合ICI治疗实体瘤的关键临床数据，特别是其在克服原发性耐药方面的潜力。更重要的是，它提出了一个区别于传统“有益菌定植”假说的新机制框架：即治疗获益主要源于FMT诱导的基线有害病原体（pathobionts）的清除，进而调节宿主代谢和免疫微环境。此外，它还揭示了供体菌群特征（如Prevotella丰度）与特定ICI方案（双免疫检查点抑制）相互作用下的安全性风险。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中ICI的疗效”，提供具体的临床响应率证据，支持FMT作为增敏策略的有效性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“介导该效应的机制是什么”，提供微生物组重塑的具体分子和免疫学路径，挑战传统的“益生菌定植”主导观点，强调“去致病化”的重要性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于讨论ICI疗效与安全性之间的权衡，以及微生物组在预测和管理irAEs中的作用，提示未来FMT研究中供体筛选的重要性。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"为综述中关于“FMT作用机制的争议”提供反面证据或补充视角，即定植效率可能不是决定疗效的唯一或主要因素。\",\n            \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"背景信息，用于对比不同研究中关于FMT机制的解释（定植vs清除）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"跨研究的一致性证据，支持“有害菌清除”作为FMT疗效通用机制的假设。\",\n            \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为外部验证，增强综述中关于机制结论的可信度。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n          \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n          \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"FMT联合ICI的临床疗效（NSCLC, Melanoma）\",\n          \"FMT介导的微生物组重塑机制（有害菌清除 vs 有益菌定植）\",\n          \"肠道微生物-免疫代谢轴（色氨酸代谢, 喹啉酸, 犬尿氨酸）\",\n          \"ICI相关不良反应（irAEs）的微生物驱动因素\",\n          \"供体选择对治疗安全性和有效性的影响\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material\": {\n        \"_progressive_task_requirements\": {\n          \"knowledge_gaps\": [\n            \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\"\n          ],\n          \"questions\": [\n            {\n              \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n              \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n              \"required_output_ids\": [\n                \"O01\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"required_outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n              \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n              \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"_progressive_task_signature\": \"37c81ea7cb18384d\",\n        \"current_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"fulfilled\": false,\n        \"paper_identity\": {\n          \"canonical_paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n          \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n          \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\"\n        },\n        \"paper_title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"plain_text\": \"\",\n        \"prior_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"required_output_ids\": [\n              \"O01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\",\n        \"required_outputs\": [\n          {\n            \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n            \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n            \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"source_hash\": \"8dd08b84648262841f9d35af692160252692383791e7c7d076ecd654063fb0f3\",\n        \"task_hash\": \"4fcf708140bdb8b00ce198191a4362b1ee8545d9d5569d77e4118fb1833a9f61\"\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material_trimmed\": {\n        \"dropped_keys\": {\n          \"material_ready\": 4,\n          \"paper_id\": 42,\n          \"references\": 413,\n          \"review_id\": 23,\n          \"schema_version\": 46,\n          \"status\": 9,\n          \"task_id\": 34,\n          \"workflow\": 21\n        },\n        \"dropped_chars\": 592,\n        \"note\": \"深读材料里的记账字段与论文自带的参考文献表已省略；科学内容（问句材料/发现/条件）保留。需要时可用 locator 读原文。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch4.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"assets\",\n            \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0088\",\n      \"title\": \"Adverse reactions of immune checkpoint inhibitors combined with Proton pump inhibitors: a pharmacovigilance analysis of drug-drug interactions\",\n      \"year\": \"2024\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1186/s12885-024-12947-7\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"2129f97a58fe871598a9da0cb18083d6d6fa4729\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"1. 数据来源：提取FAERS数据库中2014年Q1至2023年Q4的数据。2. 分组策略：将报告分为三组索引（仅ICI、仅PPI、ICI+PPI）及参考组（无ICI无PPI）。3. 统计方法：使用ROR进行非比例性信号检测；通过无条件逻辑回归计算调整后的ROR（RORadj）以控制混杂；利用加法模型（风险相加）和乘法模型（风险相乘）验证相互作用的稳健性。4. 分层分析：针对阳性信号的SOC，进一步按PD-1、PD-L1、CTLA-4亚型进行子集分析。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"首次利用大规模自发报告系统数据，量化了ICIs与PPIs联用的四种主要DDI信号，并按ICI亚型细化了风险谱。\",\n            \"limits\": \"依赖FAERS自发报告数据，存在报告偏倚、缺失数据、无法计算确切发生率、缺乏临床严重程度分级细节以及未控制所有潜在混杂因素（如肿瘤类型、合并用药复杂性）的限制。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"ICI + PPI vs 其他组合\",\n            \"finding\": \"发现四个SOC存在显著的DDI信号：先天性/家族性/遗传性疾病（RORadj=2.66）、肝胆疾病（RORadj=7.10）、代谢与营养障碍（RORadj=2.66）、皮肤及皮下组织疾病（RORadj=1.53）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"PD-1 + PPI\",\n            \"finding\": \"与先天性/家族性/遗传性疾病、肝胆疾病、皮肤及皮下组织疾病相关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"PD-L1 + PPI\",\n            \"finding\": \"与代谢与营养障碍相关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"CTLA-4 + PPI\",\n            \"finding\": \"与先天性/家族性/遗传性疾病、皮肤及皮下组织疾病相关。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管ICIs和PPIs在癌症治疗中常联合使用，但两者之间的药物相互作用及其潜在的不良后果尚不清楚。研究试图回答：ICIs与PPIs联用是否会增强特定类型不良反应的发生频率？不同亚型的ICI与PPI联用是否存在差异化的风险模式？\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"基于美国FDA不良事件报告系统（FAERS）2014-2023年的真实世界数据，研究免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，包括PD-1、PD-L1、CTLA-4抑制剂）与质子泵抑制剂（PPIs）联合使用时的药物相互作用信号。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"本研究旨在评估ICIs与PPIs联用是否会产生特定的药物相互作用（DDI）。作者利用FAERS数据库，通过非比例性分析计算报告比值比（ROR），并采用逻辑回归调整混杂因素（年龄、性别、报告年份），同时结合加法和乘法模型验证信号稳健性。研究识别出四个存在显著交互作用的标准化MedDRA查询系统器官分类（SOC），并进一步按ICI亚型进行了子集分析。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文提供了ICIs与PPIs联用在真实世界中产生的具体不良反应信号图谱，特别是揭示了PPI可能加剧ICI引起的肝毒性、皮肤毒性及代谢问题的统计学证据。对于综述而言，它提供了关于“PPI作为共病管理药物如何干扰ICI安全性”的实证数据，支持了PPI可能通过改变微环境或药理途径影响ICI疗效/安全性的假设，但需明确其仅为相关性信号而非因果机制证明。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"这是基于自发报告系统的关联性信号，不能直接证明PPI降低了ICI的抗肿瘤疗效，也不能确定具体的生物学机制。样本主要来自老年患者（中位年龄66岁），结果可能受年龄相关共病影响。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了ICIs与PPIs联用导致特定不良反应增加的流行病学证据。数据显示联用组在肝胆、皮肤、代谢及遗传类疾病上的报告率显著高于单药组，提示PPI的使用可能与ICI相关的毒性增强有关。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于论证PPI作为常见伴随用药，可能在真实世界环境中增加ICI治疗的负担或风险，从而解释部分临床观察到的疗效异质性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"这些机制解释是作者基于文献的综合推断，并非本研究的实验结果。研究本身未测量肠道菌群或生物标志物。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"在讨论部分提出了潜在的机制假说：PPI通过抑制胃酸分泌改变肠道菌群组成（减少多样性、改变特定菌属丰度），进而影响全身免疫反应和ICI介导的毒性。此外，还讨论了药代动力学和药效学相互作用的可能性。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"为F2关于机制的问题提供理论背景和支持性假说，特别是关于胃肠道pH值变化对微生物群及随后免疫反应的影响路径。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"提供临床实践现状的背景，强调监测此类相互作用的需求。\",\n            \"material\": \"FAERS数据库中ICIs与PPIs联用的病例特征（中位年龄66岁，男性略多，欧洲报告最多），以及时间趋势（报告量逐年增加）。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为背景信息，展示这两种药物联合使用的普遍性和增长趋势，说明研究该相互作用的重要性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"可用于讨论不同类别ICI在安全性管理上的细微差别，或作为未来研究需要区分ICI亚型的依据。\",\n            \"material\": \"不同ICI亚型（PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4）与PPI联用的差异化信号分布。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"提示不同靶点的ICI与PPI可能存在不同的相互作用风险谱，例如PD-1更关联肝毒性和皮肤毒性，而PD-L1更关联代谢问题。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究结果为信号检测（Signal Detection），表明的是报告频率的异常升高，而非确证的因果关系或临床发生率。\",\n          \"FAERS数据存在严重的报告偏倚（Underreporting）和信息不完整，尤其是关于既往病史和合并用药的详细记录缺失，可能导致混杂因素控制不足。\",\n          \"机制部分（如菌群改变）仅为讨论中的文献回顾和推测，本研究未提供直接的微生物组测序或分子机制证据，不可将其作为机制确定的事实引用。\",\n          \"研究对象为广泛癌症患者，未限定于特定实体瘤，外推至特定固体瘤时需考虑肿瘤类型特异性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n          \"proton pump inhibitors (PPIs)\",\n          \"drug-drug interactions (DDIs)\",\n          \"gut microbiome modulation (implied by mechanism discussion)\",\n          \"hepatotoxicity\",\n          \"cutaneous adverse events\",\n          \"metabolic/nutritional disorders\",\n          \"pharmacovigilance data mining\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch4.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0088\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2129f97a58fe871598a9da0cb18083d6d6fa4729\\\\4e1b93af88df541623acee2d53ed5b51\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\2129f97a58fe871598a9da0cb18083d6d6fa4729\\\\4e1b93af88df541623acee2d53ed5b51\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n      \"year\": \"2026\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n            \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n            \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n            \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n            \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"empirical\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"该论文为综述提供了关于FMT联合ICI治疗实体瘤的关键临床数据，特别是其在克服原发性耐药方面的潜力。更重要的是，它提出了一个区别于传统“有益菌定植”假说的新机制框架：即治疗获益主要源于FMT诱导的基线有害病原体（pathobionts）的清除，进而调节宿主代谢和免疫微环境。此外，它还揭示了供体菌群特征（如Prevotella丰度）与特定ICI方案（双免疫检查点抑制）相互作用下的安全性风险。\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“肠道微生物群如何调节实体瘤中ICI的疗效”，提供具体的临床响应率证据，支持FMT作为增敏策略的有效性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于回答“介导该效应的机制是什么”，提供微生物组重塑的具体分子和免疫学路径，挑战传统的“益生菌定植”主导观点，强调“去致病化”的重要性。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n            \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"用于讨论ICI疗效与安全性之间的权衡，以及微生物组在预测和管理irAEs中的作用，提示未来FMT研究中供体筛选的重要性。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"broader_review_uses\": [\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"为综述中关于“FMT作用机制的争议”提供反面证据或补充视角，即定植效率可能不是决定疗效的唯一或主要因素。\",\n            \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"背景信息，用于对比不同研究中关于FMT机制的解释（定植vs清除）。\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"connection_to_review\": \"跨研究的一致性证据，支持“有害菌清除”作为FMT疗效通用机制的假设。\",\n            \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"作为外部验证，增强综述中关于机制结论的可信度。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n          \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n          \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n          \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\"\n        ],\n        \"topic_handles\": [\n          \"FMT联合ICI的临床疗效（NSCLC, Melanoma）\",\n          \"FMT介导的微生物组重塑机制（有害菌清除 vs 有益菌定植）\",\n          \"肠道微生物-免疫代谢轴（色氨酸代谢, 喹啉酸, 犬尿氨酸）\",\n          \"ICI相关不良反应（irAEs）的微生物驱动因素\",\n          \"供体选择对治疗安全性和有效性的影响\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material\": {\n        \"_progressive_task_requirements\": {\n          \"knowledge_gaps\": [\n            \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\"\n          ],\n          \"questions\": [\n            {\n              \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n              \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n              \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n              \"required_output_ids\": [\n                \"O01\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ],\n          \"required_outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n              \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n              \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"_progressive_task_signature\": \"37c81ea7cb18384d\",\n        \"current_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"fulfilled\": false,\n        \"paper_identity\": {\n          \"canonical_paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n          \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n          \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\"\n        },\n        \"paper_title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"plain_text\": \"\",\n        \"prior_question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"question_material\": [\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n                \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [\n                  \"R23\"\n                ],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n              \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"examples\": [\n              {\n                \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n                \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n                \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n                \"reference_ids\": [],\n                \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"remaining_points\": [\n              \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n              \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"questions\": [\n          {\n            \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n            \"required_output_ids\": [\n              \"O01\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\",\n        \"required_outputs\": [\n          {\n            \"description\": \"Source-based findings, conditions, methods and limits useful to the review.\",\n            \"output_id\": \"O01\",\n            \"output_type\": \"practical_material\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"source_hash\": \"8dd08b84648262841f9d35af692160252692383791e7c7d076ecd654063fb0f3\",\n        \"task_hash\": \"4fcf708140bdb8b00ce198191a4362b1ee8545d9d5569d77e4118fb1833a9f61\"\n      },\n      \"deep_read_material_trimmed\": {\n        \"dropped_keys\": {\n          \"material_ready\": 4,\n          \"paper_id\": 42,\n          \"references\": 413,\n          \"review_id\": 23,\n          \"schema_version\": 46,\n          \"status\": 9,\n          \"task_id\": 34,\n          \"workflow\": 21\n        },\n        \"dropped_chars\": 592,\n        \"note\": \"深读材料里的记账字段与论文自带的参考文献表已省略；科学内容（问句材料/发现/条件）保留。需要时可用 locator 读原文。\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_material\": {\n        \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n        \"evidence\": [],\n        \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n        \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n        \"limitations\": [],\n        \"material_ready\": true,\n        \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n        \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n        \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n        \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n        \"status\": \"unmet\",\n        \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n      },\n      \"supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action\": \"Search for published results from the CanBiome2 trial (NCT06623461) or other large-scale randomized phase III trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated cancer patients to determine if any have been completed and reported since this publication.\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"tool_supplement_materials\": [\n        {\n          \"allowed_use\": [],\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"decision\": \"stop\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"\",\n          \"limits\": [],\n          \"need_id\": \"Nbcf492500208-757e7573bb6bd28e\",\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n              \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"allowed_use\": [],\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"decision\": \"stop\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"\",\n          \"limits\": [],\n          \"need_id\": \"Nc9621a3d541b-757e7573bb6bd28e\",\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"sources\": [\n            {\n              \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n              \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"locator\": {\n        \"writer_packet\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\writer_packets\\\\Ch5.json\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n      },\n      \"card_material\": {\n        \"known_gaps\": [\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n            \"kind\": \"asset\",\n            \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"kind\": \"assets\",\n            \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n            \"status\": \"missing\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n      },\n      \"material_read_from_disk\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n      \"title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n      \"year\": \"2025\",\n      \"doi\": \"10.3389/fmicb.2025.1606684\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"8211fc48bb00f738157c8859ad0748cc7d220f09\",\n      \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n      \"material_status\": \"resolved\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"study_summary_A\": {\n        \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a narrative synthesis of literature from microbiology, immunology, and oncology. They organized the content into thematic sections: introduction to the gut-lung axis, alterations in microbiota composition and metabolism in lung cancer patients, microbial biomarkers for early detection, prediction of immunotherapy response, modulation of drug efficacy, microbiota-targeted therapeutic interventions, and mechanistic insights. The review integrates findings from clinical studies, animal models, and multi-omics analyses to construct a cohesive understanding of the gut-lung axis in lung cancer.\",\n        \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive overview of the gut-lung axis in lung cancer, linking specific microbial taxa and metabolites to clinical outcomes in diagnosis and immunotherapy.\",\n            \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data or perform a systematic meta-analysis. The causal relationships described are largely inferred from correlative clinical studies and preclinical models, which may vary across populations.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial signatures (e.g., A. muciniphila, SCFA producers) and metabolic profiles as potential biomarkers for predicting ICI response.\",\n            \"limits\": \"The generalizability of these biomarkers depends on the heterogeneity of patient cohorts and sequencing methodologies used in the cited studies, which are not standardized in this review.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"contribution\": \"Discusses therapeutic interventions like FMT and probiotics as adjuncts to cancer therapy, highlighting their potential to overcome resistance.\",\n            \"limits\": \"Clinical translation faces challenges including interindividual variability, lack of standardized protocols for FMT/probiotics, and long-term safety concerns, which are noted but not resolved.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"key_findings\": [\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"In lung cancer patients compared to healthy controls\",\n            \"finding\": \"Patients exhibit dysbiosis characterized by increased abundance of Ruminococcus, Enterobacteriaceae, Lachnospiraceae, and decreased levels of Faecalibacterium, Bifidobacterium, and Veillonella. Metabolic profiles show reduced SCFA production and increased lactate.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"For early detection of lung cancer\",\n            \"finding\": \"A panel of 13 microbial biomarkers was identified with high diagnostic potential, achieving an AUC of 92.4% in discovery and 67.7% in validation cohorts using a Patient Discrimination Index (PDI).\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Predicting response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n            \"finding\": \"Baseline presence of Akkermansia muciniphila, Faecalibacterium spp., and Clostridiales correlates with improved ICI outcomes. Higher levels of acetate, propionate, and butyrate are associated with prolonged progression-free survival. A TOPOSCORE integrating species interaction groups and A. muciniphila abundance predicts individual responses.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Impact of antibiotics and probiotics on ICI efficacy\",\n            \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use prior to ICI therapy is associated with reduced overall survival and impaired efficacy. Probiotic supplementation (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Clostridium butyricum) may enhance ICI efficacy and improve survival outcomes in NSCLC patients.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"conditions\": \"Mechanisms of action\",\n            \"finding\": \"Gut microbes modulate lung immunity via metabolites (SCFAs), antigen presentation, and immune cell trafficking. Specific bacteria like A. muciniphila can translocate to tumor tissues, restructure the intratumoral ecosystem, and restore exhausted CD8+ T cells, enhancing anti-PD-1 therapy efficacy.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n        \"problem_or_question\": \"To synthesize existing evidence regarding how the gut microbiome influences lung cancer pathogenesis and treatment efficacy, particularly in the context of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), and to identify potential therapeutic strategies and biomarkers derived from this interaction.\",\n        \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the gut-lung axis in the context of lung cancer, specifically examining non-small cell lung carcinoma (NSCLC) and small cell lung carcinoma. It covers pathogenesis, early detection biomarkers, mechanisms of immune modulation, and therapeutic interventions including immunotherapy response prediction and microbiota-targeted treatments.\",\n        \"work_summary\": \"This is a narrative review synthesizing current knowledge on the role of the gut microbiome in lung cancer development, diagnosis, and treatment. It outlines the bidirectional communication between intestinal microbiota and pulmonary health via immune, neural, and metabolic pathways. The paper highlights microbial signatures predictive of disease and therapy response, discusses microbiota-targeted interventions such as probiotics and fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), and elucidates mechanistic insights into microbial-immune crosstalk. It aims to provide a comprehensive framework for leveraging the gut microbiome in personalized lung cancer management.\"\n      },\n      \"review_planning_B\": {\n        \"planning_summary\": \"This review serves as a foundational resource for understanding the gut-lung axis in lung cancer, particularly its impact on immunotherapy efficacy. It provides detailed descriptions of microbial signatures associated with ICI response, mechanistic pathways involving metabolites and immune cells, and emerging therapeutic strategies. It is highly relevant for facets concerning how the microbiome modulates ICI efficacy and the underlying mechanisms.\",\n        \"facet_contributions\": [\n          {\n            \"boundaries\": \"Focuses primarily on lung cancer; while it mentions other cancers briefly, the detailed evidence is lung-specific. Causal inference is limited to observational associations and preclinical models.\",\n            \"contribution\": \"Details the correlation between specific gut microbiota compositions (e.g., A. muciniphila, SCFA-producing bacteria) and improved clinical outcomes in solid tumors treated with ICIs. It also notes that antibiotic use negatively impacts ICI efficacy.\",\n            \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n            \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments abou
